1
00:01:45,079 --> 00:01:46,495
- THORAIPAKKAM-

2
00:01:47,829 --> 00:01:48,912
- Ma'am?
- <i>Yes, tell me.</i>

3
00:01:49,037 --> 00:01:52,412
He said he would come and talk to my
mother after finishing work, didn't he?

4
00:01:52,454 --> 00:01:53,079
<i>Yes.</i>

5
00:01:53,120 --> 00:01:54,454
But he never showed up.

6
00:01:54,912 --> 00:01:56,954
He hasn't even picked up
my calls for a week.

7
00:01:57,495 --> 00:01:58,829
I'm very scared.

8
00:01:59,412 --> 00:02:00,786
This is my life, ma'am.

9
00:02:00,787 --> 00:02:03,244
<i>He’s avoiding you
even after everything I’ve said?</i>

10
00:02:03,245 --> 00:02:04,245
<i>Don’t you worry.</i>

11
00:02:04,287 --> 00:02:05,453
<i>I'm there for you.</i>

12
00:02:05,454 --> 00:02:07,925
<i>Just watch what I do to him.</i>

13
00:02:08,412 --> 00:02:09,161
Hmm.

14
00:02:09,162 --> 00:02:11,954
[siren goes off]

15
00:02:14,912 --> 00:02:17,537
[song plays on speaker]

16
00:02:20,787 --> 00:02:22,620
[knocks on door]

17
00:02:23,329 --> 00:02:24,162
[door opens]

18
00:02:33,079 --> 00:02:35,662
[song plays on speaker]

19
00:02:57,954 --> 00:02:59,829
Harshitha ma'am...

20
00:03:00,787 --> 00:03:02,244
[throws baton]
You pathetic drunkard!

21
00:03:02,245 --> 00:03:04,704
That’s not Harshitha, man,
that’s Harichandra!

22
00:03:04,745 --> 00:03:05,829
[pulls chair]

23
00:03:06,370 --> 00:03:07,370
Give it to him already!

24
00:03:10,787 --> 00:03:13,412
Were you in love with a girl
named Avantika for four years?

25
00:03:13,579 --> 00:03:14,329
I did.

26
00:03:14,454 --> 00:03:19,954
Did you take her everywhere, parks,
beaches, movies, malls, restaurants?

27
00:03:20,162 --> 00:03:20,995
Yes, I did.

28
00:03:21,245 --> 00:03:21,745
Hmm.

29
00:03:21,787 --> 00:03:24,454
Did you take her to Ooty and book a room?

30
00:03:25,037 --> 00:03:25,787
Yes, I did.

31
00:03:25,995 --> 00:03:28,704
Did you tell her you'll talk to
her mother about the marriage?

32
00:03:28,745 --> 00:03:29,620
Yes, I did.

33
00:03:29,662 --> 00:03:32,537
Then why the hell, instead of going
to her mother's house in Thoraipakkam,

34
00:03:32,579 --> 00:03:34,287
do you have a ticket booked for Dubai?

35
00:03:34,412 --> 00:03:35,079
Sir!

36
00:03:36,954 --> 00:03:40,245
- Lekha-
- Women's Association Head-

37
00:03:43,579 --> 00:03:46,244
Sir, he lured a girl into love,
betrayed her,

38
00:03:46,245 --> 00:03:47,953
and is now trying to flee from the country.

39
00:03:47,954 --> 00:03:50,870
I thought you’d have him stripped down
to his underwear and thrashed by now,

40
00:03:50,912 --> 00:03:53,204
but here you are,
royally questioning him in a chair.

41
00:03:55,995 --> 00:03:57,120
Oh!

42
00:03:57,287 --> 00:04:00,995
And a soda for his hangover, too?

43
00:04:01,037 --> 00:04:02,369
Is this how you conduct
an investigation, sir?

44
00:04:02,370 --> 00:04:04,454
Why don't you sit down and
interrogate him yourself then?

45
00:04:04,495 --> 00:04:06,537
Don't talk without realizing
the seriousness of this, sir!

46
00:04:06,579 --> 00:04:10,037
Watching that girl cry in agony...
even we couldn't bear to see it.

47
00:04:10,162 --> 00:04:12,370
If that girl takes a fatal,
wrong step tomorrow,

48
00:04:12,412 --> 00:04:13,787
who is going to be responsible, sir?

49
00:04:14,037 --> 00:04:15,912
She's asking you...
give her an answer, damn it!

50
00:04:20,537 --> 00:04:21,287
Hey!

51
00:04:21,370 --> 00:04:23,204
Don't let him go! Ladies, surround him
and lock him in right there!

52
00:04:27,745 --> 00:04:29,911
Look, he’s running! He’s running!
Catch him! Grab him!

53
00:04:29,912 --> 00:04:32,245
No matter which country you flee to,
I won’t let you go!

54
00:04:32,287 --> 00:04:33,495
I swear I won't let you go today!

55
00:04:33,537 --> 00:04:35,412
You owe that girl an answer.

56
00:04:35,454 --> 00:04:37,703
Yeah, right. Let's finish this today!

57
00:04:37,704 --> 00:04:38,911
Oh no! Save me, sir!

58
00:04:38,912 --> 00:04:40,411
Please, sir. Just look at his audacity!

59
00:04:40,412 --> 00:04:41,244
Where do you think you are?
What do you think you’re doing?

60
00:04:41,245 --> 00:04:41,662
Thank you, sir.

61
00:04:41,704 --> 00:04:42,870
One hit, that’s all
it’ll take to finish you.

62
00:04:43,995 --> 00:04:47,037
Sir, don't file a case
saying I cheated a girl.

63
00:04:47,954 --> 00:04:50,537
If you want, file a case saying I beat
these nuisances to death right here!

64
00:04:50,579 --> 00:04:53,037
There are a thousand real issues
to fight for in this country for women.

65
00:04:53,329 --> 00:04:53,995
Let me go!

66
00:04:54,329 --> 00:04:57,412
In Porur, a man raped
and killed a seven-year-old child.

67
00:04:57,745 --> 00:04:59,204
The court let him walk free.

68
00:04:59,287 --> 00:05:00,787
Why didn't these people
stand in front of the court

69
00:05:00,829 --> 00:05:02,662
or the police station and ask
why that dog was released?

70
00:05:02,995 --> 00:05:05,245
Their only job is to poke their
noses into useless matters

71
00:05:05,287 --> 00:05:07,579
and stand in the way to cause trouble!

72
00:05:08,079 --> 00:05:09,295
You have so much to say...

73
00:05:09,495 --> 00:05:11,411
then tell us, what on earth
was the problem with your love?

74
00:05:11,412 --> 00:05:12,745
There was no problem in the love, sir...

75
00:05:14,245 --> 00:05:15,537
'Love' itself was the problem!

76
00:05:16,620 --> 00:05:16,953
- L

77
00:05:16,954 --> 00:05:17,286
- Lo

78
00:05:17,287 --> 00:05:17,619
- Lov

79
00:05:17,620 --> 00:05:18,328
- Love

80
00:05:18,329 --> 00:05:18,661
- Love O

81
00:05:18,662 --> 00:05:19,369
- Love Oh

82
00:05:19,370 --> 00:05:19,703
- Love Oh L

83
00:05:19,704 --> 00:05:20,036
- Love Oh Lo

84
00:05:20,037 --> 00:05:20,369
- Love Oh Lov

85
00:05:20,370 --> 00:05:20,744
- Love Oh Love

86
00:05:20,745 --> 00:05:25,315
- Love Oh Love-

87
00:05:29,068 --> 00:05:31,068
Devotional song is playing...

88
00:05:32,537 --> 00:05:33,704
Oh Lord...

89
00:05:39,620 --> 00:05:42,245
[interview runs on TV]

90
00:05:42,287 --> 00:05:44,704
<i>"We've been doing this
every year for years now."</i>

91
00:05:44,870 --> 00:05:49,704
<i>"These days, I don’t see many
Tamil families doing this anymore.</i>

92
00:05:50,037 --> 00:05:52,495
<i>"Back in the day,
during the temple festivals,</i>

93
00:05:52,537 --> 00:05:54,286
<i>they used to sell these
coin boxes in Mylapore."</i>

94
00:05:54,287 --> 00:05:55,203
<i>"It will be made of sand."</i>

95
00:05:55,204 --> 00:05:57,953
<i>"It will be a good feeling to see
money fall out when breaking it."</i>

96
00:05:57,954 --> 00:05:59,912
<i>"No one makes those coin boxes today."</i>

97
00:06:02,662 --> 00:06:03,578
Bless you, my child.

98
00:06:03,579 --> 00:06:05,787
Oh, please!
Keep your 'blessings' to yourself!

99
00:06:05,829 --> 00:06:09,537
<i>"If you're receiving a salary in any form,
it's best to save at least 30% of it."</i>

100
00:06:10,120 --> 00:06:12,495
- Here is your lunch bag.
- Okay, Dad.

101
00:06:12,745 --> 00:06:15,579
So, listen... out of the
money you handed over,

102
00:06:15,620 --> 00:06:19,161
once I cleared the rent,
the light bill, and the provisions...

103
00:06:19,162 --> 00:06:21,162
- what’s left is...
- Why are you explaining all these to me?

104
00:06:21,204 --> 00:06:24,329
No, son... after all those expenses,
there’s about 2000 and change left.

105
00:06:24,370 --> 00:06:25,954
I just thought you might
need it for yourself.

106
00:06:25,995 --> 00:06:28,203
No, Dad. Kavitha mentioned
she needed to buy some books.

107
00:06:28,204 --> 00:06:29,204
Just give it to her.

108
00:06:30,829 --> 00:06:33,745
Hey Raghu, Pushpa Grandma
from D-block passed away.

109
00:06:33,787 --> 00:06:35,204
Can you stop by and pay your
respects on your way out?

110
00:06:35,245 --> 00:06:36,329
I’ve got some work to finish up.

111
00:06:36,370 --> 00:06:36,954
Oh, great!

112
00:06:36,995 --> 00:06:39,162
Just what I need, to go look at
a dead body on my way to the office.

113
00:06:39,204 --> 00:06:39,995
That'll really make my day!

114
00:06:40,037 --> 00:06:41,995
I have a very important meeting today,

115
00:06:42,204 --> 00:06:43,162
I’m leaving now.

116
00:06:43,204 --> 00:06:44,495
- Hey, eat and go...
- Hey!

117
00:06:44,537 --> 00:06:46,078
- Finish your food.
- No, Dad. I'll eat at work.

118
00:06:46,079 --> 00:06:47,454
- Here, at least take this with you.
- Okay.

119
00:06:47,495 --> 00:06:48,161
- Bye, Dad.
- Take care.

120
00:06:48,162 --> 00:06:48,995
- Bye, Mom!
- Okay.

121
00:06:50,329 --> 00:06:53,537
[interview continues on TV]

122
00:06:54,704 --> 00:06:55,370
[door opens]

123
00:07:04,662 --> 00:07:06,412
Where is the D-block?

124
00:07:12,037 --> 00:07:12,870
Sir...

125
00:07:14,329 --> 00:07:15,079
Sir!

126
00:07:16,329 --> 00:07:17,953
Sir, when you see the girl
you love for the very first time...

127
00:07:17,954 --> 00:07:19,244
this is exactly how the background
music should kick in, right?

128
00:07:19,245 --> 00:07:20,036
Yeah, true.

129
00:07:20,037 --> 00:07:21,787
But do you know how it actually
sounded for me, sir?

130
00:07:21,829 --> 00:07:22,829
How did it sound?

131
00:07:24,370 --> 00:07:25,829
[death beat]

132
00:07:26,579 --> 00:07:27,620
[clock strikes]

133
00:07:28,120 --> 00:07:30,662
[death beat continues]

134
00:07:32,162 --> 00:07:34,037
The music was telling me
even back then, sir...

135
00:07:34,329 --> 00:07:35,370
I was just too blind to understand it.

136
00:07:36,912 --> 00:07:39,579
The very same funeral I told
my mother I wouldn’t attend...

137
00:07:39,829 --> 00:07:43,370
she’s standing right at my doorstep,
asking for that same address.

138
00:07:43,829 --> 00:07:45,828
The one decorated
with flowers at the funeral

139
00:07:45,829 --> 00:07:47,704
was that old lady who passed away, sir.

140
00:07:48,265 --> 00:07:49,412
But the one who looked truly beautiful...

141
00:07:49,829 --> 00:07:50,954
it was her.

142
00:08:12,912 --> 00:08:14,662
Hey... Raghu?

143
00:08:14,745 --> 00:08:16,329
You said you had an
urgent meeting at the office,

144
00:08:16,370 --> 00:08:17,662
what on earth are you doing here?

145
00:08:18,787 --> 00:08:21,537
Dad... Grandma passed away.

146
00:08:22,537 --> 00:08:24,662
That is exactly what your
mother told you this morning.

147
00:08:25,120 --> 00:08:25,953
She’s a poor soul, Dad.

148
00:08:25,954 --> 00:08:27,744
Aside from us,
who else does Grandma really have?

149
00:08:27,745 --> 00:08:29,829
To her, we’re just 'someone else' as well.

150
00:08:29,870 --> 00:08:31,579
Brother, can I have a word with you?

151
00:08:31,620 --> 00:08:33,244
- Sit down.
- You’re also just someone else to me.

152
00:08:33,245 --> 00:08:34,245
Thank God!

153
00:08:35,870 --> 00:08:38,495
Look at him... said he wouldn't go,
and now look where he's sitting.

154
00:08:38,954 --> 00:08:40,870
I don’t know why, sir... but it
didn’t even feel like a funeral to me.

155
00:08:40,954 --> 00:08:42,537
It felt more like all my relatives
had gathered there

156
00:08:42,662 --> 00:08:44,495
just to pick out a bride for me.

157
00:08:46,454 --> 00:08:48,036
Hey, why are you just standing there?

158
00:08:48,037 --> 00:08:49,454
Go serve the guests some coffee.

159
00:09:01,954 --> 00:09:03,954
- She looks good, doesn't she?
- Hope you're doing good, dear.

160
00:09:04,745 --> 00:09:05,787
- Mom!
- Huh?

161
00:09:05,912 --> 00:09:07,745
I like this girl very much.

162
00:09:10,829 --> 00:09:11,662
Hey!

163
00:09:12,037 --> 00:09:13,079
What are you saying?

164
00:09:14,412 --> 00:09:16,120
Oh we're still at the funeral?

165
00:09:16,995 --> 00:09:18,495
Nothing seems normal.

166
00:09:19,245 --> 00:09:21,495
Relax, I was just joking.

167
00:09:22,370 --> 00:09:23,370
- Dear.
- Yes?

168
00:09:23,412 --> 00:09:25,079
Something’s wrong with him.
Let's just get out of here.

169
00:09:27,037 --> 00:09:27,954
Do you have a fever?

170
00:09:28,662 --> 00:09:29,662
No... you seem fine.

171
00:09:30,162 --> 00:09:33,954
Fine. I guess he won't be leaving for
that 'meeting' until the burial is over.

172
00:09:34,079 --> 00:09:36,870
Everyone’s here now.
Let's get the procession started.

173
00:09:38,912 --> 00:09:40,187
Oh God!

174
00:09:40,995 --> 00:09:42,870
Wait... if they take the body now,
she's going to leave too.

175
00:09:44,662 --> 00:09:47,204
I'll keep dancing!
I'll just keep dancing!

176
00:09:47,245 --> 00:09:49,745
Nobody goes near the body
until I’m done dancing!

177
00:09:49,787 --> 00:09:50,578
You all hear me?

178
00:09:50,579 --> 00:09:52,079
- Hey, look! It's Michael Jackson.
- Hey!

179
00:09:52,120 --> 00:09:54,161
Aren't you supposed to be at the office?
What are you doing here?

180
00:09:54,162 --> 00:09:56,204
I can't just leave her and go.

181
00:09:57,245 --> 00:10:03,579
♪ She smiles in my dreams,
But scowls when we meet in person... ♪

182
00:10:09,079 --> 00:10:14,995
♪ A Sakura is standing before me
What am I supposed to do? ♪

183
00:10:15,329 --> 00:10:21,245
♪ I get nervous when I go near her
What am I supposed to say? ♪

184
00:10:21,537 --> 00:10:27,829
♪ She walks by watching the time
With such natural beauty... ♪

