200
00:12:32,995 --> 00:12:36,120
♪ She smiles in my dreams,
But scowls when we meet in person... ♪

201
00:12:36,162 --> 00:12:38,537
♪ She smiles in my dreams... ♪

202
00:12:42,620 --> 00:12:44,245
Hey, Gopal! Wake up!

203
00:12:45,037 --> 00:12:46,120
Everyone’s gone!

204
00:12:46,412 --> 00:12:47,870
Look at him, still searching for her.

205
00:12:47,912 --> 00:12:49,453
Huh? Where is everyone?

206
00:12:49,454 --> 00:12:50,495
Let's get out of here!

207
00:12:56,495 --> 00:12:57,579
You idiots!

208
00:12:58,579 --> 00:13:01,537
- So, what happened to Grandma in the end?
- What else could we do, sir?

209
00:13:01,704 --> 00:13:03,954
After the mess we made,
everyone just left.

210
00:13:03,995 --> 00:13:06,537
But we couldn't just leave
Grandma there, right?

211
00:13:06,579 --> 00:13:09,120
We spent our own cash and
made sure everything was done right.

212
00:13:09,787 --> 00:13:11,162
I swear, sir, every cent
came out of our own pockets!

213
00:13:13,954 --> 00:13:17,120
I didn't know who she was, where
she came from, or even her name, sir.

214
00:13:17,454 --> 00:13:20,661
But somehow, I tracked her down
and actually got her to fall for me.

215
00:13:20,662 --> 00:13:22,619
Our very first date.

216
00:13:22,620 --> 00:13:24,579
I went to the spot she picked
and just stood there, waiting for her.

217
00:13:25,287 --> 00:13:27,120
Wait, hold on!

218
00:13:27,245 --> 00:13:29,537
First time you saw her,
the funeral horns were literally blowing.

219
00:13:29,620 --> 00:13:31,619
Then she served you coffee.

220
00:13:31,620 --> 00:13:33,078
How are you already talking about dating?

221
00:13:33,079 --> 00:13:34,619
When did you even propose?

222
00:13:34,620 --> 00:13:36,412
How did you actually
get her to fall for you?

223
00:13:36,495 --> 00:13:39,787
Sir, the story isn't about
how I made her fall in love with me.

224
00:13:39,912 --> 00:13:41,662
The story is about the
problems that followed.

225
00:13:41,704 --> 00:13:44,370
Man, can't you just
tell the story in order?

226
00:13:44,454 --> 00:13:46,412
You're jumping all over the place!

227
00:13:51,662 --> 00:13:53,870
Look, this isn't some
bedtime story for kids,

228
00:13:54,204 --> 00:13:57,162
and I’m definitely no Rajamouli to
give you a perfectly directed screenplay.

229
00:13:57,412 --> 00:14:00,204
Honestly, I’m just a chaotic mess, sir.

230
00:14:00,537 --> 00:14:02,579
Just listen to it in my order.

231
00:14:27,704 --> 00:14:28,370
Hi.

232
00:14:28,579 --> 00:14:29,162
Hi.

233
00:14:29,662 --> 00:14:31,287
- Shall we go?
- Where?

234
00:14:32,245 --> 00:14:32,787
Starbucks?

235
00:14:32,912 --> 00:14:34,787
- Hmm, let's go.
- Hmm.

236
00:14:36,870 --> 00:14:37,662
Auto!

237
00:14:39,204 --> 00:14:40,704
Why are you calling for an auto now?

238
00:14:42,079 --> 00:14:44,495
Oh, is it nearby?
Let's walk then!

239
00:14:48,745 --> 00:14:49,787
Isn't this your bike?

240
00:14:50,287 --> 00:14:51,328
No... this isn't my bike.

241
00:14:51,329 --> 00:14:52,245
Then where is your bike?

242
00:14:52,370 --> 00:14:53,829
I don't actually have a bike.

243
00:14:55,287 --> 00:14:56,286
Then how do you get to work?

244
00:14:56,287 --> 00:14:57,994
The office cab picks me up.

245
00:14:57,995 --> 00:15:00,162
If I need to go somewhere nearby,
I usually take my Dad’s moped.

246
00:15:00,204 --> 00:15:02,204
But I couldn't exactly
pick you up on a moped, right?

247
00:15:02,287 --> 00:15:03,537
That’s why I called an auto.

248
00:15:03,620 --> 00:15:05,329
Me? In an auto?
Not happening. Get lost!

249
00:15:05,454 --> 00:15:07,954
Okay, fine, no auto! I’ll book
a cab right away. Just don't be mad.

250
00:15:08,120 --> 00:15:09,494
It’s our first time out together,

251
00:15:09,495 --> 00:15:10,829
and you didn't even think about
how we were going to travel?

252
00:15:10,870 --> 00:15:13,370
Wait! One second, just hear me out!
Hey! Don't go!

253
00:15:14,120 --> 00:15:16,245
Fine, no cab!
How about the Metro?

254
00:15:16,287 --> 00:15:16,995
Why stop there?

255
00:15:17,495 --> 00:15:19,954
Why don't you just put her on an
elephant and take her for a royal ride?

256
00:15:20,829 --> 00:15:22,704
Forget her, I wouldn't even come.

257
00:15:22,745 --> 00:15:24,329
What made you think
she’d be okay with an auto?

258
00:15:25,120 --> 00:15:26,537
First things first, go buy a bike!

259
00:15:27,412 --> 00:15:29,412
[tattoo needle buzzing]

260
00:15:29,454 --> 00:15:31,079
So, a bike is okay for you?

261
00:15:31,120 --> 00:15:32,245
No. I prefer cars!

262
00:15:32,329 --> 00:15:33,954
Huh?! Why don't you just ask
for an airplane while you're at it?

263
00:15:37,495 --> 00:15:40,578
Look, wanting to buy
a bike isn't a mistake.

264
00:15:40,579 --> 00:15:43,537
But... thinking
you can just buy it on EMI?

265
00:15:44,079 --> 00:15:45,620
That feels like a mistake.

266
00:15:46,620 --> 00:15:47,661
Just a second.

267
00:15:47,662 --> 00:15:48,995
[interview on TV]

268
00:15:51,954 --> 00:15:52,661
Hey, Raghu.

269
00:15:52,662 --> 00:15:53,454
- What is it, Mom?
- Here.

270
00:15:53,495 --> 00:15:54,870
- Take this.
- What is this?

271
00:15:54,912 --> 00:15:57,204
It’s alright, I heard it all.
Keep the money.

272
00:15:58,245 --> 00:16:00,037
I think your Dad went inside
just to get some money for you.

273
00:16:00,162 --> 00:16:01,870
If he gives it, don't say no. Take it!

274
00:16:02,704 --> 00:16:05,412
Kavitha dear... add a little sugar
to the sambar, will you?

275
00:16:05,454 --> 00:16:07,745
[interview continues on TV]

276
00:16:09,787 --> 00:16:11,454
Did your Mom give you any money?

277
00:16:11,829 --> 00:16:12,662
No, Dad.

278
00:16:13,329 --> 00:16:14,745
I know! Come on, just show it to me!

279
00:16:16,537 --> 00:16:18,537
Here. This is my share.

280
00:16:19,579 --> 00:16:22,750
Look, it's fine to save up money
to buy something.

281
00:16:22,829 --> 00:16:26,120
But you should never buy something
only to end up drowning in debt.

282
00:16:26,287 --> 00:16:28,995
And... I’ve told you this
since you were a kid...

283
00:16:29,120 --> 00:16:33,162
people like us need to find
big happiness in small things.

284
00:16:33,204 --> 00:16:34,329
What can we do?

285
00:16:34,370 --> 00:16:36,245
We’re middle class, after all.

286
00:16:36,704 --> 00:16:38,704
- Go ahead... buy the bike you like.
- Okay, Dad.

287
00:16:41,037 --> 00:16:43,245
But make sure you pick a colour
that everyone will actually like!

288
00:16:45,120 --> 00:16:46,870
Sir, this bike comes in three colours.

289
00:16:46,912 --> 00:16:48,620
Red, black and blue.

290
00:16:48,704 --> 00:16:50,412
The blue one is priced at...

291
00:16:50,454 --> 00:16:52,787
Dude! If you ride into
the area on this thing,

292
00:16:52,829 --> 00:16:54,454
the whole neighbourhood
is going to go nuts!

293
00:16:54,579 --> 00:16:57,370
This isn't the one I came for, man.

294
00:16:57,620 --> 00:16:59,454
The one I’m buying... is right over here.

295
00:17:02,870 --> 00:17:05,287
Hey?! That’s a bike for girls to ride!

296
00:17:05,329 --> 00:17:06,954
This is the bike
for taking girls on a ride.

297
00:17:06,995 --> 00:17:08,579
Listen to me, buy this one!

298
00:17:08,662 --> 00:17:11,037
Hey, she just told me to get a bike.

299
00:17:11,120 --> 00:17:13,370
If I buy it in her favourite colour,
problem solved!

300
00:17:13,829 --> 00:17:14,995
Just do whatever, man!

301
00:17:15,037 --> 00:17:17,495
This guy is trying to hype me up
without even knowing my budget.

302
00:17:18,662 --> 00:17:19,454
<i>Hello.</i>

303
00:17:19,579 --> 00:17:20,370
Yes, what's up?

304
00:17:20,662 --> 00:17:22,829
Hey, I’m at the showroom to buy a bike.

305
00:17:22,870 --> 00:17:24,287
Tell me what colour you like.

306
00:17:24,495 --> 00:17:25,370
That's great news!

307
00:17:25,454 --> 00:17:26,953
But wait, which bike are you getting?

308
00:17:26,954 --> 00:17:28,495
Just tell me the colour you like.

309
00:17:28,537 --> 00:17:29,870
First, tell me which bike!

310
00:17:30,829 --> 00:17:31,620
Yamaha Ray.

311
00:17:31,995 --> 00:17:32,662
Come again.

312
00:17:32,704 --> 00:17:33,453
Yamaha Ray.

313
00:17:33,454 --> 00:17:34,579
They say it gives really good mileage.

314
00:17:34,870 --> 00:17:39,078
What? You mean that bike family guys
use to carry water cans? That one?

315
00:17:39,079 --> 00:17:42,037
Hey, what’s wrong with this bike?

316
00:17:42,079 --> 00:17:43,829
If you're going to buy that bike,

317
00:17:43,954 --> 00:17:46,120
I’d rather just take a cab
to the office for the rest of my life.

318
00:17:46,454 --> 00:17:48,995
Buy a sports bike or just
forget about the whole thing!

319
00:17:49,037 --> 00:17:49,537
Hey! Hey!

320
00:17:52,662 --> 00:17:55,704
What? Did she call it a water-can bike?

321
00:17:56,412 --> 00:17:58,495
Hey... how did you know?!

322
00:17:58,537 --> 00:17:59,537
I know everything, man.

323
00:18:00,704 --> 00:18:01,204
Sir!

324
00:18:02,454 --> 00:18:05,494
He has 1 lakh in hand and
earns 40,000 rupees a month.

325
00:18:05,495 --> 00:18:07,870
Can we work out a deal for the
bike with that down payment?

326
00:18:08,787 --> 00:18:10,954
I went there to pay in full,

327
00:18:10,995 --> 00:18:12,954
but she made me to use
that money as a down payment

328
00:18:13,162 --> 00:18:16,079
and locked me into a 6,800 rupee EMI!

329
00:18:16,245 --> 00:18:17,829
And the real tragedy is...

330
00:18:18,079 --> 00:18:21,120
The 1-lakh bike gives 50km mileage,

331
00:18:21,204 --> 00:18:24,412
but this 3-lakh beast barely hits 30!

332
00:18:24,579 --> 00:18:27,120
It feels like a manufacturing defect, sir.

333
00:18:27,245 --> 00:18:30,995
I spend my whole day picking her up,

334
00:18:31,037 --> 00:18:32,411
dropping her off at her workplace,

335
00:18:32,412 --> 00:18:36,036
racing to my workplace
and finish my work on time,

336
00:18:36,037 --> 00:18:37,329
and race back to her place

337
00:18:37,412 --> 00:18:39,411
and by the time
I pick her up and drop again,

338
00:18:39,412 --> 00:18:41,662
the fuel cost and
maintenance cost sky rockets.

339
00:18:42,245 --> 00:18:43,454
Honestly,

340
00:18:43,495 --> 00:18:44,745
even a Swiggy or Zomato rider

341
00:18:44,787 --> 00:18:46,495
wouldn't have clocked this many
kilometres to support a family!

342
00:18:46,537 --> 00:18:48,036
I’ve driven more for her
than they do for a living.

343
00:18:48,037 --> 00:18:50,911
Tell me, sir...
why did I even buy this bike?

344
00:18:50,912 --> 00:18:53,245
Oh my, oh my, oh my...

345
00:18:53,287 --> 00:18:56,286
you say you clocked all those kilometres,
but was it just for the ride?

346
00:18:56,287 --> 00:18:58,369
Think about, how many potholes,
how many bumps,

347
00:18:58,370 --> 00:18:59,703
and how many speed breakers did you hit?

348
00:18:59,704 --> 00:19:01,203
How many red lights did you
'conveniently' stop at?

349
00:19:01,204 --> 00:19:02,579
And tell me the truth,
how many sharp turns did you take

350
00:19:02,620 --> 00:19:04,079
just to make her hold on tighter? Huh?

351
00:19:04,204 --> 00:19:06,369
Oh, please! How many
sudden brakes did you hit

352
00:19:06,370 --> 00:19:08,079
just to bring her from
the back seat to the front?

353
00:19:08,120 --> 00:19:10,745
You're acting like you suffered so much!

354
00:19:11,037 --> 00:19:12,454
Hmm... she's right.

355
00:19:12,495 --> 00:19:14,619
Do you guys ever actually ride straight?

356
00:19:14,620 --> 00:19:16,037
You’re always at an angle!

357
00:19:16,079 --> 00:19:18,829
Sir, do you have any idea how she
actually sits behind me on that bike?

358
00:19:28,495 --> 00:19:30,619
Why did I even buy this bike for someone
who leaves so much gap between us?

359
00:19:30,620 --> 00:19:33,037
I’ve been picking her up and
dropping her off for three months,

360
00:19:33,079 --> 00:19:34,537
and sometimes I even doubt

361
00:19:34,579 --> 00:19:36,036
if she’s actually sitting on my bike

362
00:19:36,037 --> 00:19:38,204
or if she’s hitched a ride
with someone else behind me!

363
00:19:38,412 --> 00:19:40,412
Nobody understood my pain, sir...

364
00:19:40,662 --> 00:19:41,995
except for one dog.

365
00:19:42,120 --> 00:19:42,870
Huh?!

366
00:19:46,662 --> 00:19:48,178
No...

367
00:19:51,829 --> 00:19:54,579
Well, whatever happened,
you got what you wanted in the end.

368
00:19:55,204 --> 00:19:56,870
Maybe... but something
I didn't expect happened too, sir.

369
00:19:57,079 --> 00:19:57,745
Huh?!

370
00:19:59,329 --> 00:20:01,704
[movie running in theatre]

371
00:20:03,412 --> 00:20:04,704
Everyone was watching the movie,

372
00:20:05,120 --> 00:20:06,620
but I was just staring at her.

373
00:20:07,204 --> 00:20:08,329
I don't know why, sir...

374
00:20:08,495 --> 00:20:09,995
but someone else was staring at me.

375
00:20:17,204 --> 00:20:18,704
[phone rings]

376
00:20:24,287 --> 00:20:26,162
- Tell me, dude.
- What's up, dude?

377
00:20:26,204 --> 00:20:29,037
First time going to a movie with her...
I bet the sparks are flying, huh?

378
00:20:30,245 --> 00:20:31,537
Nothing happened, man.

379
00:20:31,745 --> 00:20:32,995
She's just locked into the movie.

380
00:20:33,287 --> 00:20:34,870
That’s how girls are!

381
00:20:34,912 --> 00:20:37,036
It’s up to us to do something and
make the 'move' to win them over.

382
00:20:37,037 --> 00:20:38,370
That's all fine, dude.

383
00:20:38,870 --> 00:20:41,954
But the guy in the next seat...
he wouldn't take his eyes off me.

384
00:20:43,370 --> 00:20:46,495
Why would he even look at you
when you aren't doing anything?

385
00:20:46,995 --> 00:20:48,079
Don't worry, man.

386
00:20:48,120 --> 00:20:50,245
He’ll get annoyed
and turn away in a bit.

387
00:20:52,829 --> 00:20:54,536
Dude, dude!
I think he finally got annoyed.

388
00:20:54,537 --> 00:20:55,412
He turned away!

389
00:20:55,454 --> 00:20:56,995
Make your move!

390
00:21:12,162 --> 00:21:12,995
[lights come on]

391
00:21:18,579 --> 00:21:19,454
Hey!

392
00:21:20,037 --> 00:21:21,037
Come, let's go to the canteen.

393
00:21:33,912 --> 00:21:36,495
Brother... you can't see?

394
00:21:36,537 --> 00:21:39,287
Were you sitting turned
like that just to hear the dialogue?

395
00:21:39,495 --> 00:21:40,579
What an idiot I've been!

396
00:21:40,745 --> 00:21:43,120
Man, I wasted the whole
first half being terrified for no reason!

397
00:21:48,704 --> 00:21:50,745
Is he actually going to eat all of that,
or is he planning to sell it inside?

398
00:21:52,995 --> 00:21:55,454
- Hey, Raghu, pay the bill and come.
- Okay.

399
00:21:56,204 --> 00:21:58,662
My girl's easy.
Just one coffee, that's it.

400
00:22:00,454 --> 00:22:02,412
So, what’s the damage?
How much for the coffee?

401
00:22:02,454 --> 00:22:04,829
- 3,600 rupees.
- 3,600 rupees?!

402
00:22:05,204 --> 00:22:07,661
3,600 rupees for a cold coffee?!

403
00:22:07,662 --> 00:22:10,245
No, sir... she ordered everything
straight to her seat!

404
00:22:11,454 --> 00:22:12,787
Enjoy your cinema, sir.

405
00:22:12,870 --> 00:22:13,704
Hmm...

406
00:22:16,162 --> 00:22:16,661
[payment notification]

407
00:22:16,662 --> 00:22:17,954
You enjoy.

408
00:22:19,954 --> 00:22:22,162
They manage to make a whole
movie on a planned budget, sir.

409
00:22:22,329 --> 00:22:25,370
But we can't even watch the movie
within our planned budget!

410
00:22:38,495 --> 00:22:39,003
Sir!

411
00:22:39,370 --> 00:22:40,537
Did you see that, sir?

412
00:22:40,620 --> 00:22:43,411
Sir, he didn't go to that theatre
with that girl to watch a movie at all.

413
00:22:43,412 --> 00:22:46,079
As if she came to the theatre
to watch the movie!

414
00:22:55,329 --> 00:22:58,412
Hey, if you're blowing 4,000 rupees
on a single movie outing,

415
00:22:58,454 --> 00:23:00,787
how did you get by on a 40,000 salary?

416
00:23:03,870 --> 00:23:06,204
Look at you, buddy, getting credit cards.

417
00:23:06,245 --> 00:23:08,453
- Didn't you say you'd never take a loan?
- What can I do?

418
00:23:08,454 --> 00:23:09,662
Commitments have piled up.

419
00:23:09,704 --> 00:23:12,037
Is Avantika making you
empty your pockets?

420
00:23:12,079 --> 00:23:14,245
When do girls ever let a guy
keep money in his pocket?

421
00:23:14,495 --> 00:23:15,204
Oh boy!

422
00:23:15,245 --> 00:23:17,620
You people make our wallets weak
before the weekend even ends.

423
00:23:17,745 --> 00:23:19,662
Hey, why are you whining for just this?

424
00:23:19,704 --> 00:23:21,870
My guy has already maxed out four cards!

425
00:23:21,912 --> 00:23:23,704
I can't afford that kind of luxury.

426
00:23:23,745 --> 00:23:27,037
You're not just spending money, man...
it's all an investment!

427
00:23:27,245 --> 00:23:30,495
After marriage, you're going to collect it
all back from your father-in-law anyway.

428
00:23:30,912 --> 00:23:32,620
As if you guys are going
to generously hand it over.

429
00:23:32,829 --> 00:23:33,704
Give me the card.

430
00:23:33,829 --> 00:23:36,123
Hmm, as if you guys would
ever let us skip paying.

431
00:23:36,329 --> 00:23:38,079
Look how sharp he is already!

432
00:23:39,222 --> 00:23:40,007
Raghu...

433
00:23:41,329 --> 00:23:42,995
Why did both come at once?

434
00:23:45,204 --> 00:23:47,036
Well, look who's here!
What brings you to my office, Avantika?

435
00:23:47,037 --> 00:23:49,537
The servers are down at my office.
Come on, let's go out!

436
00:23:49,620 --> 00:23:52,245
Hey! The manufacturing unit at
my office is actually up and running.

437
00:23:52,537 --> 00:23:54,911
Oh come on... just apply
for permission and come out!

438
00:23:54,912 --> 00:23:55,745
Where are we going?

439
00:23:55,787 --> 00:23:56,829
Window shopping!

440
00:23:59,651 --> 00:24:01,345
- Raghu, how does it look?
- Huh.

441
00:24:01,370 --> 00:24:02,412
Well then, come pay the bill.

442
00:24:03,245 --> 00:24:05,079
I guess the window shopping
was only for me.

443
00:24:05,287 --> 00:24:06,412
56,000 rupees?!

444
00:24:06,454 --> 00:24:07,744
Why is it so expensive, sir?

445
00:24:07,745 --> 00:24:09,954
Sir, all are new collections
and imported items.

446
00:24:09,995 --> 00:24:12,704
What? Since when is this
scrap metal considered 'imported'?

447
00:24:13,662 --> 00:24:15,454
Please... everyone's watching us.

448
00:24:15,746 --> 00:24:16,537
Just pay for it and come.

449
00:24:17,245 --> 00:24:18,579
You girls will never change.

450
00:24:25,287 --> 00:24:29,079
♪ I'm just a broke boy,
but I tried to change for you... ♪

451
00:24:30,329 --> 00:24:34,245
♪ Because I wanted to give you
a truly luxurious life... ♪

452
00:24:36,204 --> 00:24:40,079
♪ I searched everywhere looking
for someone like you... ♪

453
00:24:40,120 --> 00:24:41,954
♪ But nobody else out here
even comes close... ♪

454
00:24:41,995 --> 00:24:45,162
♪ I'm just a broke boy,
but I tried to change for you... ♪

455
00:24:46,787 --> 00:24:49,745
♪ I swiped my card for every dance move
and trend you made... ♪

456
00:24:49,787 --> 00:24:52,286
♪ Just trying to match your energy
and vibe along with you... ♪

457
00:24:52,287 --> 00:24:56,370
♪ And now my bank account
is sitting at a zero balance... ♪

458
00:25:14,870 --> 00:25:15,786
Dude, buy me some momos.

459
00:25:15,787 --> 00:25:17,036
- This momo?
- This looks good, right?

460
00:25:17,037 --> 00:25:18,162
- Yes.
- Can I get this for 100 rupees?

461
00:25:18,204 --> 00:25:19,412
- When it's for her, you spend money.
- No way.

462
00:25:19,454 --> 00:25:20,912
- But when it's me, you just make me spend!
- It's 150 rupees final.

463
00:25:21,297 --> 00:25:22,203
- Are you trying to cheat me?
- It's good, man.

464
00:25:22,579 --> 00:25:23,829
- It'll be good for you.
- I'll give you only 100 rupees.

465
00:25:23,870 --> 00:25:25,828
- I won't give anything more.
- Wait, wait, wait.

466
00:25:25,829 --> 00:25:26,912
Is he going to ask something else?

467
00:25:26,954 --> 00:25:28,495
I've heard this voice somewhere.

468
00:25:28,537 --> 00:25:29,786
I'm not buying you any 'voice'.

469
00:25:29,787 --> 00:25:31,411
- Look at the board.
- You can only use it once.

470
00:25:31,412 --> 00:25:33,787
- Listen madam, the sign says 150 rupees.
- Make it 100 rupees, brother.

471
00:25:33,870 --> 00:25:34,829
Brother, 100 rupees final.

472
00:25:34,870 --> 00:25:36,619
- 150, fixed price. Read the board.
- Oh no! 150 for this?

473
00:25:36,620 --> 00:25:37,536
- 150 rupees?
- Yes, madam.

474
00:25:37,537 --> 00:25:38,954
- Take 100 rupees, or keep it yourself!
- 100 rupees? No way.

475
00:25:38,995 --> 00:25:40,578
Move along.
Put it back and move along.

476
00:25:40,579 --> 00:25:42,704
He's blatantly trying to
rip me off for 50 rupees!

477
00:25:42,745 --> 00:25:44,287
- Flat 150 rupees for any item!
- Hey!

478
00:25:44,412 --> 00:25:46,454
Even if it's 50,000 rupees of my money,
she just throws it away?

479
00:25:46,579 --> 00:25:48,829
But if it's 50 rupees of her money,
she talks this much?

480
00:25:49,329 --> 00:25:52,995
Dude, if it's the guys' money,
it's high-end shopping at City Centre.

481
00:25:53,037 --> 00:25:56,036
But if it's the girls' money,
it's bargaining in the centre of the city!

482
00:25:56,037 --> 00:25:57,037
Let's go see what's happening.

483
00:25:57,079 --> 00:25:58,954
150 rupees!
Pick anything at just 150 rupees!

484
00:25:58,995 --> 00:26:00,120
- Tell me, boss!
- Brother...

485
00:26:00,745 --> 00:26:01,620
What's the problem, brother?

486
00:26:02,162 --> 00:26:03,579
She's just a cheap chick, boss.

487
00:26:04,037 --> 00:26:05,787
Wearing jeans and acting elite,

488
00:26:06,037 --> 00:26:08,079
but haggling over 50 rupees
for half an hour!

489
00:26:08,287 --> 00:26:10,620
Spend 1,000 rupees,
and you can easily score her, boss.

490
00:26:14,787 --> 00:26:16,162
Why the hell did you slap me?!

491
00:26:17,120 --> 00:26:17,911
What do you mean 'why'?!

492
00:26:17,912 --> 00:26:20,328
Do you have any idea how many
lakhs he spent just to win her over?

493
00:26:20,329 --> 00:26:21,619
And you casually say
1,000 rupees is enough?

494
00:26:21,620 --> 00:26:22,370
Take that!

495
00:26:23,370 --> 00:26:25,329
Guys, he hit me! Smash him!

496
00:26:26,662 --> 00:26:28,162
He might be your enemy,
but who attacks someone there?!

497
00:26:28,204 --> 00:26:29,454
- Sorry, brother! Sorry, brother!
- Let me down!

498
00:26:33,329 --> 00:26:35,412
Hey! Why are you playing piggyback on me?!

499
00:26:37,662 --> 00:26:39,120
They're playing piggyback on me.

500
00:26:40,829 --> 00:26:42,079
Hey, spin him, spin him!
He's gonna black out!

501
00:26:42,120 --> 00:26:43,412
Hey, put me down!
I’m diabetic!

502
00:26:43,454 --> 00:26:44,495
He's completely knocked out,
throw him away!

503
00:26:44,537 --> 00:26:45,662
I'm feeling a little dizzy too.

504
00:26:50,079 --> 00:26:52,495
Dude, he thinks we're
just some 'Soup Boys'

505
00:26:52,620 --> 00:26:54,370
let's show him we're
the actual 'Manjummel Boys'!

506
00:26:54,454 --> 00:26:56,995
- Dude, loosen the rope a little!
- Done!

507
00:27:08,495 --> 00:27:10,204
Hey! What are you doing?

508
00:27:10,245 --> 00:27:11,912
He was picking nits!

509
00:27:16,912 --> 00:27:19,620
She only asked for a 50-rupee discount,
but this guy totally wiped the shop clean!

510
00:27:19,704 --> 00:27:20,892
Seriously, sir, you tell me...

511
00:27:20,995 --> 00:27:23,495
who did we just fight for, and why?!

512
00:27:23,625 --> 00:27:24,373
I have no idea.

513
00:27:24,704 --> 00:27:26,079
Are you hitting him
because you spent so much

514
00:27:26,120 --> 00:27:27,745
and still couldn't make
things work with her?

515
00:27:27,787 --> 00:27:29,954
Or are you hitting him because that
shopkeeper talked trash about her?

516
00:27:29,995 --> 00:27:31,537
Even I'm totally confused.

517
00:27:31,579 --> 00:27:34,120
Sir, I only beat him up because
he talked trash about my girl.

518
00:27:34,204 --> 00:27:36,704
But sir, do you know what
she told me after all that chaos?

519
00:27:36,745 --> 00:27:38,537
- What did she say?
- Hey, don't you have any sense?

520
00:27:38,579 --> 00:27:41,037
Hanging out with trash
and fighting just like them!

521
00:27:41,204 --> 00:27:43,037
Man, that's brutal!
She's calling someone trash.

522
00:27:43,079 --> 00:27:44,495
Hey, she's talking about you!

523
00:27:44,537 --> 00:27:45,953
Hey! Who you calling trash?

524
00:27:45,954 --> 00:27:48,329
You, you idiot!
Trash! Trash! Trash!

525
00:27:48,495 --> 00:27:51,828
Look, his face might look like trash,
but he's actually a really good guy.

526
00:27:51,829 --> 00:27:54,369
- Man, she was actually nicer!
- Avantika! Hey... honey?

527
00:27:54,370 --> 00:27:57,995
♪ I tried a dark joke
to see your reaction... ♪

528
00:27:58,370 --> 00:27:59,912
♪ You didn't even crack a smile... ♪

529
00:27:59,954 --> 00:28:03,662
♪ I poured my heart out
in a whole paragraph... ♪

530
00:28:03,787 --> 00:28:05,370
♪ And you just texted back "LOL" ♪

531
00:28:05,412 --> 00:28:08,037
♪ I swiped right on all
the hype you gave me... ♪

532
00:28:08,079 --> 00:28:10,786
♪ Now my eyes are tearing up,
and I'm crying... ♪

533
00:28:10,787 --> 00:28:14,745
♪ What on earth is the solution
to this situation? Tell me! ♪

534
00:28:15,204 --> 00:28:18,204
♪ You don't turn to look,
you don't listen... ♪

535
00:28:18,245 --> 00:28:20,912
♪ You won't talk a little,
you won't let me close... ♪

536
00:28:20,954 --> 00:28:23,454
♪ Treading through dirt
and mud every single day... ♪

537
00:28:23,495 --> 00:28:26,161
♪ Getting slapped left and right,
yet I never learn... ♪

538
00:28:26,162 --> 00:28:29,036
♪ You don't notice anything,
you don't listen... ♪

539
00:28:29,037 --> 00:28:31,662
♪ You won't talk a little,
you won't let me close... ♪

540
00:28:31,704 --> 00:28:34,328
♪ Getting slapped left and right,
yet I never learn... ♪

541
00:28:34,329 --> 00:28:38,704
♪ My stubborn heart
just won't give up! ♪

542
00:28:54,037 --> 00:28:56,079
Why's Gowtham so quiet?

543
00:28:56,120 --> 00:28:59,204
He dumped Swetha and now
he's finally realizing what he lost.

544
00:28:59,245 --> 00:29:04,454
♪ Her eyes...
When will I ever look into them again? ♪

545
00:29:04,579 --> 00:29:09,829
♪ Her hands...
When will I ever hold them again? ♪

546
00:29:09,870 --> 00:29:15,204
♪ Her eyes...
When will I ever look into them again? ♪

547
00:29:15,287 --> 00:29:21,620
♪ Her hands...
When will I ever hold them again? ♪

548
00:29:24,204 --> 00:29:26,244
Sir, where are you?
You said you'd clear the payment?

549
00:29:26,245 --> 00:29:29,120
I'm just heading to my office.
Come over there and collect the cash.

550
00:29:29,162 --> 00:29:32,120
Okay, sir. I'll see another client
and head straight to your office.

551
00:29:32,162 --> 00:29:33,037
Please keep the cash ready.

552
00:29:41,995 --> 00:29:43,204
- Dad!
- Huh?

553
00:29:43,245 --> 00:29:44,994
Why are you cleaning the bike, Dad?

554
00:29:44,995 --> 00:29:46,578
So what? It's our bike anyway.

555
00:29:46,579 --> 00:29:48,328
Okay, Dad, I'm off to work now.

556
00:29:48,329 --> 00:29:49,870
- I'm running late.
- And...

557
00:29:49,912 --> 00:29:52,995
you asked me to remind you
about Kavitha's semester fees.

558
00:29:53,204 --> 00:29:54,954
Oh no! I completely forgot!

559
00:29:55,537 --> 00:29:57,329
I don't have any cash right now.

560
00:29:57,412 --> 00:29:59,120
I only have enough money
to pay off my credit card.

561
00:29:59,162 --> 00:29:59,858
Raghu?

562
00:30:00,870 --> 00:30:02,662
You have a credit card?

563
00:30:04,245 --> 00:30:05,662
No... no, Dad!

564
00:30:05,704 --> 00:30:08,412
A friend told me he was
short on his credit card bill, so...

565
00:30:08,495 --> 00:30:09,120
Huh.

566
00:30:11,870 --> 00:30:14,704
You give this to Kavitha, Dad.
I'll manage somehow.

567
00:30:14,745 --> 00:30:15,329
- Bye, Dad!
- Alright.

568
00:30:18,079 --> 00:30:21,245
Son, tell your friend this...

569
00:30:21,412 --> 00:30:24,537
He borrowed from you today
to pay his credit card bill.

570
00:30:24,620 --> 00:30:27,662
Tomorrow, he’ll borrow from
someone else just to pay you back.

571
00:30:27,912 --> 00:30:30,245
Debt is like cancer.

572
00:30:30,287 --> 00:30:33,370
It only keeps growing,
it won't disappear that easily.

573
00:30:33,412 --> 00:30:34,912
- Tell him that.
- Huh... okay, Dad.

574
00:30:34,954 --> 00:30:36,537
- Don't forget.
- I will surely tell him, Dad.

575
00:30:36,579 --> 00:30:37,579
Alright, get going.

576
00:30:39,079 --> 00:30:40,079
Ride safely.

577
00:30:41,287 --> 00:30:43,649
Sir, a bank collection agent
is here to see you.

578
00:30:45,579 --> 00:30:47,662
- Please tell him I'm on leave!
- Okay, sir.

579
00:30:54,995 --> 00:30:56,662
[phone rings]

580
00:30:57,579 --> 00:30:59,536
- Hello.
- Why is your phone switched off?

581
00:30:59,537 --> 00:31:02,204
Hey, I'm already facing
a heavy "raid" at work!

582
00:31:02,245 --> 00:31:05,537
Office raid? Or are you out on
an ECR "ride" with someone?

583
00:31:05,579 --> 00:31:08,078
Hey! Who calls an office landline
to ask questions like this?!

584
00:31:08,079 --> 00:31:10,370
You have no idea the kind of pressure
I'm dealing with here right now!

585
00:31:10,412 --> 00:31:12,954
Why? Do you think we don't deal with
stress at my workplace?

586
00:31:13,454 --> 00:31:16,037
What, do you think we're just sitting here
swinging our legs and enjoying ourselves?

587
00:31:18,454 --> 00:31:20,911
You practically begged
for my number back then.

588
00:31:20,912 --> 00:31:22,204
- Now that you have it...
- Raghu!

589
00:31:22,245 --> 00:31:23,204
...you just cut my calls?

590
00:31:23,245 --> 00:31:24,745
Sir, I'm just on the line with a client.

591
00:31:24,787 --> 00:31:25,994
Then who exactly is this?

592
00:31:25,995 --> 00:31:28,620
Because your line was busy,
the client called me directly!

593
00:31:28,995 --> 00:31:31,037
Sir, just two minutes.
I will call you back.

594
00:31:31,245 --> 00:31:33,329
Do you have any intention
of working or not?

595
00:31:33,579 --> 00:31:35,412
Why did I even hire someone like you...

596
00:31:35,454 --> 00:31:36,995
Hey, I'll call from my mobile.
Hang up now!

597
00:31:38,412 --> 00:31:39,245
Hey, tell me.

598
00:31:39,495 --> 00:31:41,036
You promised to take me out
this evening, right?

599
00:31:41,037 --> 00:31:42,787
Look, give me a second.
Let me call you right back.

600
00:31:45,329 --> 00:31:46,869
Why is your phone switched off, sir?

601
00:31:46,870 --> 00:31:48,704
No, sir... there was
a meeting inside, that's why...

602
00:31:48,745 --> 00:31:50,787
Then why are you sitting right here
and lying that you're not in?

603
00:31:50,870 --> 00:31:52,454
[phone rings]

604
00:31:52,495 --> 00:31:53,245
What is it now?

605
00:31:53,287 --> 00:31:54,995
Hey, you still haven't told me
where you're taking me.

606
00:31:55,037 --> 00:31:57,287
I'll take you wherever you want to go!
Just hang up now!

607
00:31:57,772 --> 00:31:58,953
Sir! Just take out the money first!

608
00:31:58,954 --> 00:32:00,661
Honestly sir,
I had it all set aside for you.

609
00:32:00,662 --> 00:32:01,786
It's just that on the way...

610
00:32:01,787 --> 00:32:03,162
Oh, let me guess...
on your way here,

611
00:32:03,204 --> 00:32:06,262
you saw some orphans and
generously gave it all away?

612
00:32:06,662 --> 00:32:08,536
Sir, you are crossing the line.

613
00:32:08,537 --> 00:32:09,828
Me, crossing the line?

614
00:32:09,829 --> 00:32:11,245
Look at you spinning tales!

615
00:32:11,287 --> 00:32:12,829
Didn't you think of this when you
were swiping that card left and right?

616
00:32:12,870 --> 00:32:14,412
Why do people like you
even take out loans, sir?

617
00:32:18,204 --> 00:32:20,370
[phone rings]

618
00:32:20,579 --> 00:32:22,204
When are you coming to pick me up?

619
00:32:23,370 --> 00:32:24,369
The things I want to do
to her right now...

620
00:32:24,370 --> 00:32:26,495
Hey! When are you finally
going to start working?

621
00:32:26,829 --> 00:32:28,662
Sir, when are you finally going to pay me?

622
00:32:28,745 --> 00:32:29,829
When are you coming to pick me up?

623
00:32:29,870 --> 00:32:31,244
Hey! When are you finally
going to start working?

624
00:32:31,245 --> 00:32:32,453
When are you coming to pick me up?

625
00:32:32,454 --> 00:32:33,536
Sir, when are you finally going to pay me?

626
00:32:33,537 --> 00:32:34,453
When are you coming to pick me up?

627
00:32:34,454 --> 00:32:35,495
Hey! When are you finally
going to start working?

628
00:32:35,537 --> 00:32:36,412
When are you coming to pick me up?

629
00:32:39,986 --> 00:32:40,662
It's always like this, sir.

630
00:32:41,162 --> 00:32:43,037
Without even understanding
the situation I'm in,

631
00:32:43,079 --> 00:32:45,120
she'll just keep nagging
and driving me crazy.

632
00:32:45,245 --> 00:32:48,995
Look sir, for everything that went wrong
so far, it was either my fault or hers.

633
00:32:49,037 --> 00:32:51,245
But everything that went down after that?

634
00:32:51,287 --> 00:32:52,829
- That's entirely on Ranbir Kapoor.
- Huh?!

635
00:32:52,870 --> 00:32:54,995
What on earth did Ranbir Kapoor
do in your story?

636
00:32:55,037 --> 00:32:56,162
Not in my story, sir.

637
00:32:56,204 --> 00:32:57,201
In his story.

638
00:32:58,787 --> 00:33:01,245
She and I had gone to watch
the movie Animal.

639
00:33:02,412 --> 00:33:04,870
Look at this guy...
using brand new techniques!

640
00:33:10,329 --> 00:33:11,162
Hey, brother!

641
00:33:11,204 --> 00:33:12,870
Why are you kissing the phone?

642
00:33:12,995 --> 00:33:16,537
Look, it’s far better to do this than
to just sit idle next to a beautiful girl.

643
00:33:17,412 --> 00:33:18,870
Just shut up and watch the movie!

644
00:33:19,037 --> 00:33:19,828
<i>Who was that?</i>

645
00:33:19,829 --> 00:33:22,287
He’s just some random guy who actually
came to watch the movie, dear.

646
00:33:22,620 --> 00:33:26,537
When everyone else is having biryani,
won't I crave it too, sir?

647
00:33:26,579 --> 00:33:28,204
Hmm... I suppose so.

648
00:33:28,329 --> 00:33:30,245
I saw my biryani
right in front of me.

649
00:33:31,204 --> 00:33:34,329
Sir, just as I was about to
taste my biryani...

650
00:33:38,745 --> 00:33:40,204
- Hey...
- I knew it!

651
00:33:40,245 --> 00:33:44,786
I got suspicious the moment
you booked an entire row online.

652
00:33:44,787 --> 00:33:47,495
But when you started grinning
during a serious scene,

653
00:33:47,537 --> 00:33:50,620
I knew you were up to something.

654
00:33:50,662 --> 00:33:52,995
- Avantika, it's nothing like that!
- Shut up! Don't talk to me.

655
00:33:53,037 --> 00:33:55,744
Seriously, who tries
for a first kiss in public?

656
00:33:55,745 --> 00:33:57,745
Don't you need the right time and place?

657
00:33:58,287 --> 00:34:00,537
- Get lost! He must be his fan, for sure!
- Hey...

658
00:34:02,454 --> 00:34:04,579
[phone rings]

659
00:34:04,787 --> 00:34:05,537
Hello.

660
00:34:05,579 --> 00:34:07,412
I had biryani today, dude.

661
00:34:09,454 --> 00:34:11,369
Like I said sir,
the whole town was eating biryani.

662
00:34:11,370 --> 00:34:13,078
Turns out, Tattoo had also
eaten biryani that day!

663
00:34:13,079 --> 00:34:14,537
- What?
- Hmm.

664
00:34:14,579 --> 00:34:20,287
Seriously, did you really eat biryani,
or are you just messing with me?

665
00:34:20,329 --> 00:34:22,995
I swear on this beer, man!
I had biryani.

666
00:34:23,037 --> 00:34:23,995
Here, have a drink!

667
00:34:24,454 --> 00:34:26,870
Super, dude. At least you were
lucky enough to get some biryani.

668
00:34:28,204 --> 00:34:29,370
[notification sound]

669
00:34:32,245 --> 00:34:35,036
Finally!
My personal loan got approved, dude.

670
00:34:35,037 --> 00:34:36,912
Only the office verification is left.

671
00:34:37,120 --> 00:34:40,662
Once this amount hits my account,
all my problems will be solved!

672
00:34:40,704 --> 00:34:42,828
I’ll clear this credit card bill,
the bike loan,

673
00:34:42,829 --> 00:34:46,037
all those petty office debts,
and finally be free!

674
00:34:47,037 --> 00:34:50,495
Hey, you aren't saying a word about
the money I got you for interest!

675
00:34:50,537 --> 00:34:52,662
- I'm including that amount too, man!
- Oh, perfect then!

676
00:34:52,704 --> 00:34:54,245
- Cheers, dude!
- Cheers!

677
00:34:55,120 --> 00:34:58,579
[phone rings]

678
00:34:58,829 --> 00:35:01,579
No matter how happiness comes my way,
she just can't stand it, dude.

679
00:35:01,620 --> 00:35:03,995
Give me a minute. She can
sniff things out right over the phone!

680
00:35:04,454 --> 00:35:05,954
Do me a favour and just go.

681
00:35:06,454 --> 00:35:08,495
[phone ring continues]

682
00:35:09,412 --> 00:35:11,037
- Tell me.
- Raghu...

683
00:35:11,704 --> 00:35:12,995
My mom's not home.

684
00:35:13,620 --> 00:35:14,995
She's gone to Bangalore.

685
00:35:15,454 --> 00:35:17,745
I’m all alone...
Do you want to come over?

686
00:35:18,412 --> 00:35:21,244
<i>"Seriously, who tries
for a first kiss in public?"</i>

687
00:35:21,245 --> 00:35:23,829
<i>"Don't you need the right time and place?"</i>

688
00:35:24,370 --> 00:35:26,661
I'm on my way right now!

689
00:35:26,662 --> 00:35:28,245
- Hey, hey, hey!
- Huh?

690
00:35:28,495 --> 00:35:30,328
On your way...
maybe pick up some...

691
00:35:30,329 --> 00:35:32,537
- something for safety...
- Huh!

692
00:35:33,120 --> 00:35:34,204
I will get it.

693
00:35:37,162 --> 00:35:42,079
You didn't misunderstand me, did you...
asking you over when my mom's away?

694
00:35:42,120 --> 00:35:44,829
No, no. What’s wrong with that?

695
00:35:45,245 --> 00:35:49,245
- This is my first time.
- For me too... it's my first time.

696
00:35:51,537 --> 00:35:54,829
- What is it? Are you hungry?
- Huh...

697
00:35:58,412 --> 00:36:00,829
Don't be hasty.
That's exactly why I'm going.

698
00:36:01,287 --> 00:36:03,454
- Oh, is it really for that?
- Exactly for that.

699
00:36:08,829 --> 00:36:09,870
Raghuvara...

700
00:36:09,912 --> 00:36:11,912
I went there to eat biryani.

701
00:36:11,954 --> 00:36:14,662
Instead, the aroma of rasam hit me.
Confused, I got up to check it out...

702
00:36:14,704 --> 00:36:15,745
- Hey!
- Huh?

703
00:36:15,787 --> 00:36:16,995
What are you doing?

704
00:36:17,120 --> 00:36:18,244
I’m making rasam.

705
00:36:18,245 --> 00:36:19,870
Why on earth are you
making rasam right now?!

706
00:36:19,912 --> 00:36:20,994
But you said you were hungry.

707
00:36:20,995 --> 00:36:23,829
Hey, I meant a different
kind of hunger. Not this!

708
00:36:23,870 --> 00:36:27,120
I came all this way for biryani.
And you...

709
00:36:27,162 --> 00:36:30,829
You don't do that to the girl you love.

710
00:36:31,120 --> 00:36:32,370
Listen to me.

711
00:36:32,537 --> 00:36:34,328
- I won't listen.
- Don't come near me.

712
00:36:34,329 --> 00:36:35,245
I will come.

713
00:36:37,912 --> 00:36:40,245
- Don't come any closer...
- Too late. I'm already here.

714
00:36:41,579 --> 00:36:42,453
Hey, hey, hey!

715
00:36:42,454 --> 00:36:43,912
What on earth are you doing in the dark?

716
00:36:44,204 --> 00:36:45,579
If you stay here any longer,

717
00:36:45,620 --> 00:36:47,787
I can't guarantee my modesty.
You need to leave right now.

718
00:36:47,829 --> 00:36:50,204
- Please, Avi.
- No, no. Get away!

719
00:36:56,495 --> 00:36:57,745
Why on earth did you buy this?

720
00:36:57,787 --> 00:36:59,829
Didn't you tell me to
buy some safety stuff?

721
00:36:59,870 --> 00:37:01,578
I told you to buy snacks for safety!

722
00:37:01,579 --> 00:37:03,995
But you brought this so you
could eat me like a snack!

723
00:37:04,329 --> 00:37:06,162
- Gross!
- Who are you calling gross?!

724
00:37:06,204 --> 00:37:08,037
You're the one who told me to come over
when your mom wasn't home!

725
00:37:08,120 --> 00:37:10,745
You're the one who randomly
put on a saree and looked stunning!

726
00:37:11,120 --> 00:37:13,536
You're the one who told me
it was your first time!

727
00:37:13,537 --> 00:37:16,412
You're the one who whispered in a husky
voice, "That's exactly why I'm going"!

728
00:37:16,454 --> 00:37:18,078
And then you call me gross?

729
00:37:18,079 --> 00:37:20,454
Yes, you are!
You are gross, gross, gross!

730
00:37:20,579 --> 00:37:22,829
Why? Does wearing a saree mean
I'm only doing it to look hot?

731
00:37:22,870 --> 00:37:25,287
The fault is in your eyes,
so stop blaming me!

732
00:37:26,204 --> 00:37:29,245
Fine, then why did you invite me
over when nobody was home?

733
00:37:30,662 --> 00:37:32,454
We fought at the theatre,

734
00:37:32,495 --> 00:37:34,995
so I wanted to invite you over,
talk it out, and make up.

735
00:37:35,120 --> 00:37:37,245
But you totally misjudged me, didn't you?

736
00:37:37,537 --> 00:37:40,162
Do you know how memorable
a first kiss is supposed to be?

737
00:37:40,412 --> 00:37:41,995
It's such a special feeling.

738
00:37:42,037 --> 00:37:43,995
It’s supposed to happen
naturally... unplanned.

739
00:37:44,037 --> 00:37:46,995
But you... you went ahead and planned
the whole thing out, didn't you?

740
00:37:47,037 --> 00:37:49,495
Do you have any idea
how much that hurts me?

741
00:37:52,370 --> 00:37:55,704
Hey, I'm really sorry.
I just wasn't thinking straight.

742
00:37:57,287 --> 00:37:59,412
Just go! You don't understand me at all.

743
00:37:59,912 --> 00:38:04,079
- I'm not that kind of girl, Raghu.
- Oh god... I'm the one who messed up.

744
00:38:12,329 --> 00:38:16,494
I’m standing here crying my eyes out,
and you're still thinking about that?

745
00:38:16,495 --> 00:38:17,579
- Get out!
- Hey...

746
00:38:19,287 --> 00:38:21,454
Hey... what are you doing here?

747
00:38:21,495 --> 00:38:24,787
When you ditched our beer plans
to go eat biryani,

748
00:38:24,829 --> 00:38:27,245
I knew right then you wouldn't
even score a plate of plain rice!

749
00:38:27,537 --> 00:38:28,912
Seriously? You didn't eat at all?

750
00:38:29,120 --> 00:38:31,369
The whole apartment has gone
to sleep after the function.

751
00:38:31,370 --> 00:38:33,037
Forget about it, dude.
Let's have some beer!

752
00:38:33,079 --> 00:38:34,454
- Come on guys! Pack up, fast!
- Hey!

753
00:38:34,995 --> 00:38:36,829
How the hell can we
drink out here in the open?

754
00:38:36,954 --> 00:38:39,079
Dude, the catering boys are our boys.

755
00:38:39,120 --> 00:38:40,787
Just drink up! Hmm!

756
00:39:07,037 --> 00:39:09,995
♪ Come out, my little sweetheart! ♪

757
00:39:10,037 --> 00:39:13,328
♪ Oh parrot who has hurt my youth! ♪

758
00:39:13,329 --> 00:39:16,078
♪ Come out, my little sweetheart! ♪

759
00:39:16,079 --> 00:39:19,370
♪ Oh parrot who has hurt my youth! ♪

760
00:39:19,412 --> 00:39:22,161
♪ Will you give yourself to me? ♪

761
00:39:22,162 --> 00:39:25,119
♪ Or are you going to come
and clash with me? ♪

762
00:39:25,120 --> 00:39:29,287
♪ You invited me into your home
and then chased me away! Come out! ♪

763
00:39:32,079 --> 00:39:34,661
♪ Come out, my little sweetheart! ♪

764
00:39:34,662 --> 00:39:37,704
♪ Oh parrot who has hurt my youth! ♪

765
00:39:38,329 --> 00:39:40,911
♪ Come out, my little sweetheart! ♪

766
00:39:40,912 --> 00:39:43,995
♪ Oh parrot who has hurt my youth! ♪

767
00:40:09,245 --> 00:40:13,412
♪ I swear on my drink,
I won't let you go! ♪

768
00:40:13,454 --> 00:40:17,079
♪ From now on, without hugging you tight
I won't be under control! ♪

769
00:40:17,329 --> 00:40:18,662
♪ Hey, baby! ♪

770
00:40:21,662 --> 00:40:25,869
♪ Without giving you a child in ten months,
I won't lie idle! ♪

771
00:40:25,870 --> 00:40:29,204
♪ I won't give up
Oh dear, I won't be afraid! ♪

772
00:40:29,412 --> 00:40:30,829
♪ It's a promise! ♪

773
00:40:33,745 --> 00:40:36,662
♪ Seeing me,
you thought I was a coward? ♪

774
00:40:36,704 --> 00:40:39,787
♪ Thinking I was poor,
you closed your door? ♪

775
00:40:40,037 --> 00:40:46,161
♪ Once half a bottle went in
I became Duryodhana! ♪

776
00:40:46,162 --> 00:40:52,329
♪ Once a full bottle goes in
I will become Dushasana! ♪

777
00:40:52,662 --> 00:40:55,329
♪ Come out, my little sweetheart! ♪

778
00:40:55,537 --> 00:40:58,620
♪ Come out, my little sweetheart!
Come out! Come out! ♪

779
00:40:58,745 --> 00:41:01,495
♪ Come out, my little sweetheart! ♪

780
00:41:01,537 --> 00:41:04,620
♪ Oh parrot who has hurt my youth! ♪

781
00:41:04,912 --> 00:41:07,620
♪ Come out, my little sweetheart! ♪

782
00:41:07,662 --> 00:41:10,662
♪ Oh parrot who has hurt my youth! ♪

783
00:41:10,787 --> 00:41:13,536
♪ Will you give yourself to me? ♪

784
00:41:13,537 --> 00:41:16,620
♪ Or are you going to come
and clash with me? ♪

785
00:41:16,662 --> 00:41:21,037
♪ You invited me into your home
and then chased me away! Come out! ♪

786
00:41:37,995 --> 00:41:39,495
Why did you ask me to
come over so urgently?

787
00:41:39,912 --> 00:41:42,745
I don't care what you have to do,
we need to get married right now!

788
00:41:43,162 --> 00:41:43,911
Hey?!

789
00:41:43,912 --> 00:41:45,954
Wait, why are you in such
a hurry for our wedding all of a sudden?

790
00:41:59,370 --> 00:42:01,412
Hey, why are you
shoving this into my hand?

791
00:42:01,454 --> 00:42:02,412
Everyone is watching us!

792
00:42:02,454 --> 00:42:04,579
I don't care about them watching!

793
00:42:04,829 --> 00:42:06,120
My mom already saw it!

794
00:42:06,995 --> 00:42:08,912
She found it in the house
and handed it to me.

795
00:42:08,954 --> 00:42:10,079
You're the one who left it behind!

796
00:42:10,329 --> 00:42:12,329
Now my mom knows you came over!

797
00:42:12,370 --> 00:42:13,537
But nothing happened!

798
00:42:13,579 --> 00:42:15,661
You and I both know that.

799
00:42:15,662 --> 00:42:16,911
But does she?

800
00:42:16,912 --> 00:42:20,287
She jumped straight to conclusions
and completely humiliated me!

801
00:42:20,370 --> 00:42:22,287
She needs to realize her
perspective is entirely wrong.

802
00:42:22,579 --> 00:42:24,370
And for that to happen...
our marriage has to happen!

803
00:42:24,412 --> 00:42:26,287
Wait, what?!
Are you out of your mind?

804
00:42:26,704 --> 00:42:28,328
Look, I have a sister who
needs to get married first.

805
00:42:28,329 --> 00:42:30,579
I can't just drop everything
and get married on a whim!

806
00:42:32,829 --> 00:42:34,370
How on earth do I make her understand?

807
00:42:34,495 --> 00:42:35,204
Come with me for a minute.

808
00:42:37,120 --> 00:42:37,787
Sit down.

809
00:42:42,745 --> 00:42:44,495
Please try to understand what I'm saying.

810
00:42:44,829 --> 00:42:46,579
Even if I run away and get married,

811
00:42:46,620 --> 00:42:48,995
my parents will still get to enjoy
watching my sister's wedding.

812
00:42:49,037 --> 00:42:51,204
But you're an only child to your mom.

813
00:42:51,245 --> 00:42:53,120
Wouldn't she dream of seeing
your wedding happen beautifully?

814
00:42:53,162 --> 00:42:56,162
Fine... but all of that mattered
before she saw this trash.

815
00:42:56,204 --> 00:42:59,203
My mom has already judged my character.

816
00:42:59,204 --> 00:43:03,162
So I have to prove to her
that this is love, not lust!

817
00:43:03,329 --> 00:43:05,245
Now, are you going to marry me...

818
00:43:06,204 --> 00:43:07,411
or should I just drink this poison?

819
00:43:07,412 --> 00:43:08,204
Hey!

820
00:43:08,287 --> 00:43:09,745
- Let go! No... let me...
- Hey, stop it! Hey!

821
00:43:10,745 --> 00:43:11,745
You tell me, sir!

822
00:43:11,787 --> 00:43:13,704
If the girl you love stands right
in the middle of a busy office,

823
00:43:13,829 --> 00:43:14,744
in front of everyone,

824
00:43:14,745 --> 00:43:18,287
holding poison and screaming,
"Marry me right now or I'll kill myself!"

825
00:43:18,329 --> 00:43:19,537
What is a guy even supposed to do, sir?

826
00:43:19,579 --> 00:43:20,704
What did you do?

827
00:43:30,579 --> 00:43:31,245
Sir.

828
00:43:32,120 --> 00:43:34,079
Look, if you want to marry a girl...

829
00:43:34,120 --> 00:43:35,912
you either take her to a temple,

830
00:43:35,954 --> 00:43:37,994
or you take her to the
marriage registrar's office.

831
00:43:37,995 --> 00:43:39,870
Why did this guy take her
all the way to Ooty?

832
00:43:40,704 --> 00:43:43,369
Exactly! Who asked you to
take her all the way to Ooty?

833
00:43:43,370 --> 00:43:44,454
Ask him, sir!

834
00:43:45,579 --> 00:43:47,494
That’s exactly what I asked her too, sir!

835
00:43:47,495 --> 00:43:52,079
Everyone in my family got married
at our family deity's temple.

836
00:43:52,120 --> 00:43:55,412
My mom always dreamed that
my wedding would happen there, too.

837
00:43:55,454 --> 00:43:57,370
For that, you're supposed
to go to the family temple!

838
00:43:57,579 --> 00:43:59,620
Why on earth did you bring me
to Chennai Silks?!

839
00:44:01,287 --> 00:44:03,162
Well, yeah! Are we supposed
to just get married like this?

840
00:44:03,204 --> 00:44:05,703
Don't we need to buy the bridal saree,
the sacred thread, and the accessories?

841
00:44:05,704 --> 00:44:06,829
Come on, let's go shopping!

842
00:44:12,829 --> 00:44:14,453
Sir, I swear to you,

843
00:44:14,454 --> 00:44:16,954
even if this wedding was happening with
the full consent of both our families,

844
00:44:16,995 --> 00:44:19,287
I don't know if they would
have shopped this much.

845
00:44:19,329 --> 00:44:20,704
She’s literally running away with me,

846
00:44:20,745 --> 00:44:22,995
why the hell is she picking out a
'Samudhrika' silk saree for 1 lakhs?

847
00:44:23,037 --> 00:44:24,620
- Huh?!
- Unbelievable!

848
00:44:27,037 --> 00:44:29,120
Raghu, I like this one.

849
00:44:30,745 --> 00:44:32,204
How much is this saree?

850
00:44:33,253 --> 00:44:33,759
Hello.

851
00:44:33,912 --> 00:44:36,787
Dude, send me 1 lakh urgently.

852
00:44:37,329 --> 00:44:37,995
Okay.

853
00:44:39,537 --> 00:44:40,454
- Bro.
- Hmm?

854
00:44:40,495 --> 00:44:42,661
That 2-lakh finance amount
the boss just approved...

855
00:44:42,662 --> 00:44:44,286
transfer 1 lakh of it
to the number I give you.

856
00:44:44,287 --> 00:44:45,287
Okay.

857
00:44:47,162 --> 00:44:48,162
Okay.

858
00:44:48,662 --> 00:44:49,829
Tell me, dude.

859
00:44:50,120 --> 00:44:52,579
Dude... please send 60,000 rupees.

860
00:44:53,579 --> 00:44:54,495
Alright.

861
00:44:56,162 --> 00:44:57,245
Dude, she just walked into the parlour!

862
00:44:57,412 --> 00:45:00,245
Bro, out of that remaining 40,000,
just send 20,000 over.

863
00:45:00,287 --> 00:45:00,954
Done.

864
00:45:01,079 --> 00:45:03,370
- Dude, can I tell you something?
- Go ahead.

865
00:45:03,412 --> 00:45:06,037
Look, a pilot should always fly the plane,

866
00:45:06,079 --> 00:45:07,870
the plane shouldn't control the pilot.

867
00:45:07,912 --> 00:45:09,661
Otherwise, you'll miss the landing.
Be careful.

868
00:45:09,662 --> 00:45:13,245
There’s drama at her home,
her mom's not agreeing,

869
00:45:13,287 --> 00:45:16,370
and asked me to marry her
without breaking up...

870
00:45:16,579 --> 00:45:18,245
So she’s the pilot of my flight, dude.

871
00:45:18,329 --> 00:45:20,037
My flight will never crash-land.

872
00:45:20,287 --> 00:45:21,995
- Can I tell you something?
- What?

873
00:45:22,037 --> 00:45:24,744
Cut the crap advice and just
GPay me the money right now!

874
00:45:24,745 --> 00:45:25,412
Get lost!

875
00:45:26,495 --> 00:45:29,204
Sir, by the time we bought the saree,
the sacred thread, and all the accessories

876
00:45:29,245 --> 00:45:31,578
and finally made it to the temple...

877
00:45:31,579 --> 00:45:32,995
they had already shut the
gates and closed it down!

878
00:45:34,287 --> 00:45:35,912
With literally zero options left...

879
00:45:35,954 --> 00:45:37,829
we just took a room at
a cottage for the night, sir.

880
00:45:38,745 --> 00:45:42,203
Do you know why I brought you
all the way to Ooty?

881
00:45:42,204 --> 00:45:45,120
Yeah... to get married
at your family temple.

882
00:45:45,954 --> 00:45:48,494
There is no family temple in Ooty.

883
00:45:48,495 --> 00:45:49,578
You've got to be kidding me!

884
00:45:49,579 --> 00:45:51,412
Then why the hell did we come
all the way to Ooty?!

885
00:45:51,704 --> 00:45:55,036
No, when me and
my friends all hit puberty,

886
00:45:55,037 --> 00:45:56,912
we signed an "Angel Agreement."

887
00:45:56,954 --> 00:45:58,162
Wait, I don't get it.

888
00:45:58,204 --> 00:46:00,829
In life, first kiss, first
romance should happen

889
00:46:00,870 --> 00:46:04,579
in a hill station and
on a full moon day.

890
00:46:04,620 --> 00:46:07,245
But you had to go and ruin it...

891
00:46:07,287 --> 00:46:09,912
by rushing into our first kiss
back at the house itself.

892
00:46:09,954 --> 00:46:12,161
Which is why we're in Ooty!

893
00:46:12,162 --> 00:46:14,912
So our first romance can happen
exactly the way I dreamed.

894
00:46:15,204 --> 00:46:17,662
Hmm... your planning is great and all.

895
00:46:18,204 --> 00:46:21,537
But if we’d just gotten married
instead of shopping right away,

896
00:46:21,579 --> 00:46:23,537
we’d be having our first night by now.

897
00:46:23,579 --> 00:46:26,370
We could always just get married
after the first night!

898
00:46:26,579 --> 00:46:29,454
It's so easy to figure out what guys
are thinking, no matter what.

899
00:46:29,995 --> 00:46:33,287
But women? You can never tell
what’s going on in their heads or when!

900
00:46:33,454 --> 00:46:35,120
We'll figure it all out later.

901
00:46:35,787 --> 00:46:38,328
For now... can we just cuddle?

902
00:46:38,329 --> 00:46:40,995
Huh! Absolutely.

903
00:46:44,495 --> 00:46:47,079
[phone vibrating]

904
00:46:47,620 --> 00:46:50,287
[phone vibrating continues]

905
00:46:50,870 --> 00:46:52,995
Brother, where are you?!

906
00:46:53,287 --> 00:46:54,579
The police came to the house.

907
00:46:54,787 --> 00:46:56,954
They said all sorts of things and
took Mom and Dad to the station.

908
00:46:57,120 --> 00:46:58,662
I'm very scared!

909
00:47:03,454 --> 00:47:06,412
Ma'am, on what grounds are you detaining
my parents at the station like this?!

910
00:47:06,454 --> 00:47:09,244
A girl has gone missing,
and her parents have filed a complaint.

911
00:47:09,245 --> 00:47:10,287
What else do you expect me to do?

912
00:47:10,329 --> 00:47:12,411
If the complaint is against me,
take action against me!

913
00:47:12,412 --> 00:47:15,037
Why are you dragging my parents to the
station and humiliating them?!

914
00:47:15,287 --> 00:47:17,954
You should have thought about
all this before kidnapping the girl!

915
00:47:17,995 --> 00:47:19,412
Nobody kidnapped me, ma'am!

916
00:47:19,454 --> 00:47:21,079
We left on our own to get married.

917
00:47:21,120 --> 00:47:21,912
[slaps]

918
00:47:24,412 --> 00:47:25,912
If you really wanted to marry her,

919
00:47:25,954 --> 00:47:28,662
you should have come to me first
and asked me to get you two married!

920
00:47:28,787 --> 00:47:31,287
At least, you should have come with
your family to formally ask for her hand!

921
00:47:31,704 --> 00:47:33,704
What exactly did you head
to Ooty and book a room for, huh?!

922
00:47:35,454 --> 00:47:38,579
Madam, please... I just need to speak
to my daughter alone for ten minutes.

923
00:47:38,745 --> 00:47:40,287
Ma'am, I don't want to talk to her.

924
00:47:40,537 --> 00:47:44,494
Hey! She gave birth to you, raised you,
educated you, and sent you to work...

925
00:47:44,495 --> 00:47:46,704
and you just run off
with some guy you like.

926
00:47:46,870 --> 00:47:48,703
She's only asking for ten
minutes of your time.

927
00:47:48,704 --> 00:47:50,078
Is it really that hard for
you to talk to her?!

928
00:47:50,079 --> 00:47:52,037
Go. Just go talk to her, go!

929
00:47:52,329 --> 00:47:53,037
Come on.

930
00:47:53,537 --> 00:47:54,537
One minute.

931
00:47:57,995 --> 00:48:01,620
Instead of you two talking in
private to tear them apart,

932
00:48:01,870 --> 00:48:04,912
why don't the two of us talk
and unite them?

933
00:48:04,995 --> 00:48:07,745
Please! Who would ever marry their
daughter off to a guy like your son?

934
00:48:08,037 --> 00:48:09,620
What’s wrong with my son?!

935
00:48:09,662 --> 00:48:12,078
He’s good-looking,
he studied engineering,

936
00:48:12,079 --> 00:48:15,579
and he works at a good company
making 40,000 rupees a month!

937
00:48:15,620 --> 00:48:17,995
He'll take good care of her.

938
00:48:18,370 --> 00:48:19,162
Yeah, right!

939
00:48:19,370 --> 00:48:23,328
Your son can't even pay off his debts,
he's just running around hiding!

940
00:48:23,329 --> 00:48:25,037
Who are you calling a debtor?!

941
00:48:25,079 --> 00:48:26,912
My son doesn't owe
a single dime to anyone!

942
00:48:26,954 --> 00:48:29,287
Oh yeah? Let's hear your
son say that to my face.

943
00:48:34,079 --> 00:48:38,204
Your son borrows money from
everyone in town and just blows it all!

944
00:48:38,245 --> 00:48:40,579
Did your whole family
sit down and plan this?

945
00:48:40,620 --> 00:48:43,411
To find a rich girl, make him fall
in love, and live off her money?!

946
00:48:43,412 --> 00:48:45,329
Look here, don't talk
without knowing the truth!

947
00:48:45,370 --> 00:48:46,662
Oh, what truth?
What is there to know?!

948
00:48:48,454 --> 00:48:51,495
You wanted the truth?
Here it is!

949
00:48:53,079 --> 00:48:55,037
I've made sure to inquire about
everything before coming here.

950
00:49:05,120 --> 00:49:08,245
You think your son is living
on a 40,000-rupee salary?

951
00:49:08,579 --> 00:49:09,870
He rides a three-lakh bike,

952
00:49:10,287 --> 00:49:11,704
eats lavish lunches at five-star hotels,

953
00:49:11,912 --> 00:49:13,328
and only shops at the mall!

954
00:49:13,329 --> 00:49:14,329
Why do all that?

955
00:49:14,829 --> 00:49:18,329
Just to fake being rich and trick
my daughter into loving him!

956
00:49:18,370 --> 00:49:20,245
Why are you talking like this?

957
00:49:20,287 --> 00:49:22,037
Shut up for a minute, will you?

958
00:49:22,370 --> 00:49:27,079
Would you give your daughter to someone
who runs around wasting money like this?

959
00:49:28,370 --> 00:49:31,079
Maybe you would give,
but I never will.

960
00:49:31,370 --> 00:49:32,037
Come!

961
00:49:37,120 --> 00:49:37,994
Listen!

962
00:49:37,995 --> 00:49:40,787
Whatever that girl decides
when she comes out,

963
00:49:41,079 --> 00:49:42,120
that’s final.

964
00:49:42,870 --> 00:49:45,329
I don't want anyone screaming
and shouting in my station.

965
00:49:56,662 --> 00:49:57,579
Talk.

966
00:49:57,662 --> 00:50:00,745
I made a mistake, ma'am.
I'm going back home with my mother.

967
00:50:01,645 --> 00:50:03,520
You can take her home, madam.

968
00:50:08,579 --> 00:50:09,579
Come, let's go.

969
00:50:31,287 --> 00:50:34,079
Get ready!
The temple will close soon.

970
00:50:38,287 --> 00:50:38,870
Dad...

971
00:50:51,204 --> 00:50:51,995
Mom...

972
00:50:52,620 --> 00:50:53,745
I'm off to work.

973
00:50:55,787 --> 00:50:56,995
- Disgusting!
- Mom?

974
00:51:04,995 --> 00:51:06,495
- Mom!
- Hey!

975
00:51:07,037 --> 00:51:09,412
Stop! Pull over!
Hey, auto, stop!

976
00:51:12,495 --> 00:51:13,495
- Here, brother.
- Careful!

977
00:51:13,537 --> 00:51:15,329
- Get moving, I'll follow.
- Hurry please!

978
00:51:27,704 --> 00:51:29,454
Hey! Are you blind?!

979
00:51:29,495 --> 00:51:30,579
Why the hell are you blocking the road?

980
00:51:30,787 --> 00:51:32,578
Hey! Get your hands off my keys!

981
00:51:32,579 --> 00:51:33,704
You piece of...

982
00:51:36,370 --> 00:51:37,662
Dad... Dad?!

983
00:51:42,495 --> 00:51:43,245
Dad!

984
00:51:58,454 --> 00:52:00,287
Hey... hey, son!

985
00:52:04,245 --> 00:52:07,037
Stop it! Just listen to me!

986
00:52:18,370 --> 00:52:19,245
Hey!

987
00:52:42,787 --> 00:52:45,162
Hey! Let him go! Hey...

988
00:52:54,204 --> 00:52:55,412
Hey, get lost!

989
00:52:56,329 --> 00:52:56,954
Hey!

990
00:52:57,704 --> 00:52:58,329
Hey!

991
00:52:58,412 --> 00:53:00,412
- Why are you taking our bike?!
- Take your hands off me!

992
00:53:00,704 --> 00:53:02,579
You haven't paid the
bike EMI in six months!

993
00:53:02,704 --> 00:53:03,567
What do you expect us to do?

994
00:53:05,620 --> 00:53:08,536
Look, your son hasn't paid
the EMI in six months.

995
00:53:08,537 --> 00:53:10,995
Give me three months' payment now,
and I'll leave the vehicle with you.

996
00:53:11,495 --> 00:53:13,079
I don't have that much money.

997
00:53:13,120 --> 00:53:15,495
You can't even afford that?
Then why do you people even need a bike?

998
00:53:15,537 --> 00:53:16,828
You two can just walk.

999
00:53:16,829 --> 00:53:18,704
The bike's secured!
Come on, let's move.

1000
00:53:29,329 --> 00:53:30,662
Just get lost...

1001
00:53:42,704 --> 00:53:44,829
Hey, where is mom?

1002
00:53:44,870 --> 00:53:46,829
Mom and dad are in the second ward.

1003
00:53:47,204 --> 00:53:48,620
They said it was just a dizzy spell.

1004
00:53:49,037 --> 00:53:52,454
The doctor said it's nothing
to worry about. It’s nothing serious.

1005
00:53:52,995 --> 00:53:54,870
Aren't you getting late for office?

1006
00:53:55,079 --> 00:53:56,912
Didn't you say you had
a project to submit today?

1007
00:53:57,287 --> 00:53:58,370
Pick up the phone!

1008
00:53:58,787 --> 00:53:59,912
Did he answer?

1009
00:54:00,204 --> 00:54:01,370
He's not picking up!

1010
00:54:02,620 --> 00:54:04,370
You go ahead and submit it.
I’ll handle things here.

1011
00:54:09,454 --> 00:54:10,370
Keep this.

1012
00:54:11,162 --> 00:54:11,912
Hmm.

1013
00:54:14,037 --> 00:54:15,579
- Take care of mom.
- Okay, brother.

1014
00:54:16,412 --> 00:54:18,078
- Hello.
- Hey, where are you?

1015
00:54:18,079 --> 00:54:19,412
I'm on my way.

1016
00:54:19,454 --> 00:54:22,037
The clients are already here waiting.
Just grab the files and get over here!

1017
00:54:22,704 --> 00:54:23,954
- Raghu...
- Let go of me!

1018
00:54:24,370 --> 00:54:25,704
I understand your anger.

1019
00:54:26,079 --> 00:54:29,454
If I hadn't gone with my mother yesterday,
do you know what could have happened?

1020
00:54:29,495 --> 00:54:31,620
I don't care what happens!
I don't give a damn!

1021
00:54:31,787 --> 00:54:33,787
I'm late for work, let me through!

1022
00:54:34,370 --> 00:54:37,620
She said, "If you don't come with me
right now, I'll hang myself."

1023
00:54:37,745 --> 00:54:39,829
I had no choice but to go with her.

1024
00:54:39,870 --> 00:54:43,454
Huh! What a noble, dignified family!
You'll hang yourselves? My foot!

1025
00:54:43,495 --> 00:54:45,245
If she cared so much about honour,

1026
00:54:45,287 --> 00:54:47,370
she should've hanged herself
the day you ran away!

1027
00:54:47,412 --> 00:54:49,704
Or better yet,
when she found condoms in the house...

1028
00:54:50,454 --> 00:54:51,662
she should've done it then.

1029
00:54:51,745 --> 00:54:54,245
Instead, she will file
a kidnapping complaint

1030
00:54:54,287 --> 00:54:56,079
and drag our names through
the mud before she dies?

1031
00:54:56,329 --> 00:54:59,495
Raghu, please, just hear me out
before you lose your temper.

1032
00:54:59,704 --> 00:55:01,619
My mom's anger has subsided a little now.

1033
00:55:01,620 --> 00:55:03,412
If you come and talk
to her now, she’ll agree.

1034
00:55:03,454 --> 00:55:05,370
The moment you rejected me
at the police station,

1035
00:55:05,662 --> 00:55:07,620
I threw you and your love away.

1036
00:55:07,662 --> 00:55:09,329
I don't have time to argue with you.

1037
00:55:09,370 --> 00:55:11,870
I have a ton of work at the office,
so please get out of my way!

1038
00:55:11,912 --> 00:55:14,912
So your office and your work
are more important to you than me?

1039
00:55:14,995 --> 00:55:15,787
Yes!

1040
00:55:15,829 --> 00:55:17,620
My work is far more
important to me than you are.

1041
00:55:18,620 --> 00:55:20,454
- But you are important to me!
- Hey! Hands off! Just let me go!

1042
00:55:20,537 --> 00:55:21,744
Just come to my house and talk!

1043
00:55:21,745 --> 00:55:23,454
- She'll accept us if you talk to her!
- Why should I talk with your mom?

1044
00:55:23,662 --> 00:55:24,370
Hey!

1045
00:55:47,620 --> 00:55:50,079
Come talk to my mom right now,

1046
00:55:50,829 --> 00:55:52,495
or I swear I'll kill myself!

1047
00:55:52,912 --> 00:55:55,328
In today's society, there is simply
no protection left for women.

1048
00:55:55,329 --> 00:55:56,537
- Why bother killing yourself?
- Violence against women,

1049
00:55:56,579 --> 00:55:57,912
- I’ll kill you myself.
- should not be accepted.

1050
00:55:58,454 --> 00:56:00,745
We are witnessing a devastating
rise in violence against women.

1051
00:56:00,787 --> 00:56:01,620
Leave me, Raghu.

1052
00:56:01,954 --> 00:56:03,204
Huh?! Hey!

1053
00:56:08,037 --> 00:56:10,829
In broad daylight,
in the middle of the street...

1054
00:56:10,870 --> 00:56:15,078
has patriarchy really given you unlimited
power that you can just kill a girl?!?

1055
00:56:15,079 --> 00:56:16,787
Ma 'am, you don't know anything.

1056
00:56:16,829 --> 00:56:18,161
You won't understand even if I tell you.

1057
00:56:18,162 --> 00:56:19,662
Please don't interfere in this.

1058
00:56:19,995 --> 00:56:21,203
Listen, young man.

1059
00:56:21,204 --> 00:56:23,328
I am the head of this Women’s Association

1060
00:56:23,329 --> 00:56:25,579
precisely to step in
whenever a girl is in trouble!

1061
00:56:25,620 --> 00:56:26,662
What is the problem?

1062
00:56:26,870 --> 00:56:27,829
Who is he?

1063
00:56:27,870 --> 00:56:28,995
My lover, ma'am.

1064
00:56:29,120 --> 00:56:29,662
Hey!

1065
00:56:30,037 --> 00:56:31,828
If you even say the word 'lover',
I will kill you!

1066
00:56:31,829 --> 00:56:32,494
Hey!

1067
00:56:32,495 --> 00:56:34,495
Ma’am, I have an important
meeting at the office.

1068
00:56:34,537 --> 00:56:37,162
I don’t have time to argue with
you or her right now. I’m leaving.

1069
00:56:37,405 --> 00:56:38,075
Hey!

1070
00:56:42,454 --> 00:56:43,995
I'm late for work, ma'am.

1071
00:56:44,037 --> 00:56:46,120
Go to the office, or go all the way
to America for all I care,

1072
00:56:46,162 --> 00:56:48,454
but give this girl an answer
before you leave!

1073
00:56:49,079 --> 00:56:52,204
- Ma'am, he doesn't need to answer me.
- Then what?

1074
00:56:52,245 --> 00:56:54,536
Tell him to come and talk to my mother.
That is enough.

1075
00:56:54,537 --> 00:56:55,662
Did you hear what she said?

1076
00:56:55,829 --> 00:56:58,454
Go meet that girl's mother
in person, speak with her,

1077
00:56:58,495 --> 00:57:00,329
and only then can you
go to your office. Understood?

1078
00:57:00,704 --> 00:57:01,745
Ma'am, please!

1079
00:57:01,954 --> 00:57:03,287
Please try to understand my situation.

1080
00:57:03,329 --> 00:57:04,954
I have an important meeting at the office.

1081
00:57:05,120 --> 00:57:07,411
I'll go and speak with her mother
this evening right after it's over.

1082
00:57:07,412 --> 00:57:08,162
Is that enough?

1083
00:57:08,995 --> 00:57:10,412
I swear I'll go and talk, ma'am.

1084
00:57:11,620 --> 00:57:16,245
If you haven't gone and spoken
to that girl's mother by this evening...

1085
00:57:16,287 --> 00:57:19,037
Even I don't know what
I will do to you. I warn you!

1086
00:57:19,079 --> 00:57:20,079
Do you understand?

1087
00:57:20,787 --> 00:57:22,620
- Tell them to let me through.
- Hmm, hmm... go!

1088
00:57:23,204 --> 00:57:25,495
If he doesn't show up, call me.

1089
00:57:25,537 --> 00:57:26,245
Okay, ma'am.

1090
00:57:26,329 --> 00:57:27,662
- You cannot go inside.
- Why?

1091
00:57:27,870 --> 00:57:29,162
Because you've been fired.

1092
00:57:29,245 --> 00:57:31,036
They've ordered us to bar
your entry if you turn up.

1093
00:57:31,037 --> 00:57:31,870
Hey!

1094
00:57:32,037 --> 00:57:34,495
I have slaved away for this
company for five whole years!

1095
00:57:34,579 --> 00:57:36,703
The least you could have done
was call me inside to fire me!

1096
00:57:36,704 --> 00:57:38,620
Are you really going to humiliate me
at the gates and throw me out?!

1097
00:57:38,704 --> 00:57:40,495
I've been ordered to collect your
laptop bag before you leave.

1098
00:57:44,579 --> 00:57:45,120
Take this.

1099
00:57:45,537 --> 00:57:47,662
Sir, you have someone waiting for you.

1100
00:57:50,079 --> 00:57:52,495
- Are you Raghuvaran?
- Hmm... yes.

1101
00:57:52,537 --> 00:57:55,370
Sir, I'm here from the bank
for your personal loan verification.

1102
00:58:08,870 --> 00:58:10,079
What's happening here?

1103
00:58:10,287 --> 00:58:12,412
Dad told us to pack up and
head back to our hometown, brother.

1104
00:58:12,454 --> 00:58:13,453
You have to talk to him.

1105
00:58:13,454 --> 00:58:15,537
- Did you load everything?
- Almost done, sir.

1106
00:58:15,829 --> 00:58:17,912
Dad, why are we all moving
back to our hometown right now?

1107
00:58:17,954 --> 00:58:20,120
Not 'we.' It's just the three of us,
we are going.

1108
00:58:20,745 --> 00:58:23,870
Yesterday, you humiliated us
inside the police station.

1109
00:58:23,912 --> 00:58:28,412
And today... you publicly disgraced
us right in the middle of the street!

1110
00:58:30,495 --> 00:58:33,287
In the past, whenever someone
looked at me and smiled,

1111
00:58:33,329 --> 00:58:34,704
it felt like genuine respect.

1112
00:58:35,579 --> 00:58:38,745
But now, if someone laughs at me...

1113
00:58:41,870 --> 00:58:44,244
When you see someone
in your town smiling at you,

1114
00:58:44,245 --> 00:58:47,994
and all you feel is fear
or overwhelming shame...

1115
00:58:47,995 --> 00:58:49,579
then you must know you don't
belong in that place anymore.

1116
00:58:49,912 --> 00:58:51,454
Which is why we are leaving.

1117
00:58:52,579 --> 00:58:55,245
Mom, at least you tell Dad...

1118
00:58:55,287 --> 00:58:56,412
Tell him what?

1119
00:58:56,495 --> 00:58:58,619
We have a girl old enough
to get married at home,

1120
00:58:58,620 --> 00:59:00,536
and you took on debt
to spend money on someone else?

1121
00:59:00,537 --> 00:59:02,787
That was the day I lost all faith in you.

1122
00:59:04,454 --> 00:59:06,579
If the people who cornered you
on the street today

1123
00:59:07,245 --> 00:59:09,620
when both of you are not at home,

1124
00:59:09,787 --> 00:59:11,537
storm into our home tomorrow
to question me and your sister,

1125
00:59:11,579 --> 00:59:13,245
I will die of shame
right then and there!

1126
00:59:14,245 --> 00:59:14,870
Get away from me!

1127
00:59:16,037 --> 00:59:19,162
Here, take this. Keep it.

1128
00:59:20,370 --> 00:59:20,992
Dad...

1129
00:59:21,995 --> 00:59:23,162
What is this?

1130
00:59:23,329 --> 00:59:25,120
It’s the property deed
to our house in the village.

1131
00:59:25,162 --> 00:59:27,745
Sell all of this, clear your debts,

1132
00:59:28,037 --> 00:59:30,412
- and go live the life you want.
- Dad, please...

1133
00:59:30,454 --> 00:59:31,870
- The car is here. Let's go.
- Dad, please...

1134
00:59:32,704 --> 00:59:34,995
Dad... I swear I will fix everything.

1135
00:59:35,787 --> 00:59:37,912
You might fix what is yet to come.

1136
00:59:38,454 --> 00:59:39,911
But what about everything
you've already destroyed?

1137
00:59:39,912 --> 00:59:42,079
Mom, at least you tell Dad...

1138
00:59:51,954 --> 00:59:55,662
[phone rings]

1139
00:59:58,708 --> 00:59:59,333
Hello.

1140
01:00:00,370 --> 01:00:01,954
You promised you'd come and meet my mom...

1141
01:00:02,340 --> 01:00:03,114
When are you coming?

1142
01:00:05,704 --> 01:00:06,537
To hell with you...

1143
01:00:09,662 --> 01:00:10,869
Why are you standing there
like you've seen a ghost?

1144
01:00:10,870 --> 01:00:11,787
Give it to me.

1145
01:00:24,454 --> 01:00:25,204
Hey!

1146
01:00:30,579 --> 01:00:32,912
The moment a girl sheds a single tear,

1147
01:00:32,954 --> 01:00:35,203
you automatically decide the guy is guilty.

1148
01:00:35,204 --> 01:00:36,162
He didn't do a single thing wrong,

1149
01:00:36,204 --> 01:00:37,787
yet you've dragged him
and put him on trial here!

1150
01:00:37,829 --> 01:00:41,078
Sir, that girl didn't tell a straight
forward story like this boy claims.

1151
01:00:41,079 --> 01:00:42,954
Who? This guy?

1152
01:00:43,037 --> 01:00:45,454
He gave you a straight forward story,
and you heard it?

1153
01:00:46,287 --> 01:00:47,537
Where is that girl?

1154
01:00:48,245 --> 01:00:49,579
Look, here she comes.

1155
01:00:49,620 --> 01:00:50,704
How do you know?!

1156
01:00:50,745 --> 01:00:51,745
It's coming!

1157
01:00:53,329 --> 01:00:54,704
The smell's coming!

1158
01:00:54,829 --> 01:00:58,329
The smell of the 8,000 rupees
perfume I bought her is coming, sir!

1159
01:01:05,329 --> 01:01:06,620
What have you done, ma'am?

1160
01:01:06,662 --> 01:01:08,370
I did what you asked for.

1161
01:01:08,579 --> 01:01:09,578
What did I say?

1162
01:01:09,579 --> 01:01:11,662
I told you to stop him
from leaving the country!

1163
01:01:11,704 --> 01:01:13,370
Why the hell have you brought him here?

1164
01:01:13,412 --> 01:01:15,870
Sir, I’m the victim here and
I haven't even filed a complaint yet.

1165
01:01:15,912 --> 01:01:18,370
How can you take action
based on what they filed?

1166
01:01:19,079 --> 01:01:20,744
I will complain against you, sir.

1167
01:01:20,745 --> 01:01:21,787
Good grief!

1168
01:01:21,829 --> 01:01:24,620
How did you survive a four-year
relationship with her?

1169
01:01:24,954 --> 01:01:27,912
She’s been inside for exactly four seconds
and she already made me an accused!

1170
01:01:27,995 --> 01:01:30,911
You put him through hell
in the name of love,

1171
01:01:30,912 --> 01:01:33,828
then you ran to them and complained
as if he cheated you,

1172
01:01:33,829 --> 01:01:37,662
and they're acting like they’re saving
all of womankind by dragging him here!

1173
01:01:37,954 --> 01:01:40,329
Withdraw your complaint
and just get out! Screw this!

1174
01:01:40,662 --> 01:01:43,329
Even if she drops the charges, sir,
I am not going anywhere.

1175
01:01:43,370 --> 01:01:44,537
What do you mean you're not going?!

1176
01:01:44,829 --> 01:01:47,328
- Sir, please tell her to give me L3.
- What the hell is L3?

1177
01:01:47,329 --> 01:01:48,662
Love Leaving Letter, sir.

1178
01:01:48,787 --> 01:01:52,286
Sir, tell her to give it in writing that
she has nothing to do with me anymore.

1179
01:01:52,287 --> 01:01:53,787
It's literally a 'love divorce,' sir!

1180
01:01:53,829 --> 01:01:56,370
Tell her to put it all down
in a letter and sign it.

1181
01:01:56,412 --> 01:01:58,703
And you and Madam
can sign it as witnesses.

1182
01:01:58,704 --> 01:02:00,662
Look, I can't give you any such letter.

1183
01:02:00,704 --> 01:02:02,203
The law doesn't recognize that.

1184
01:02:02,204 --> 01:02:03,829
Then you give me a letter, sir!

1185
01:02:03,870 --> 01:02:04,869
Saying what?!

1186
01:02:04,870 --> 01:02:07,619
Write a letter like this, sir.
'Following the complaint

1187
01:02:07,620 --> 01:02:09,994
filed by Avantika and her family
against Raghuvaran...

1188
01:02:09,995 --> 01:02:13,704
A thorough investigation has revealed
that Raghuvaran is completely innocent.

1189
01:02:13,745 --> 01:02:15,662
Therefore, in the future,

1190
01:02:15,704 --> 01:02:17,870
if Avantika or her associates,

1191
01:02:17,912 --> 01:02:20,703
file a case in any police station
across Tamil Nadu,

1192
01:02:20,704 --> 01:02:23,994
the police department guarantees
that it will not be accepted.

1193
01:02:23,995 --> 01:02:25,579
Just write that and give it to me, sir.

1194
01:02:25,620 --> 01:02:27,744
- I’ll leave right this second!
- Hey, what's wrong with you?

1195
01:02:27,745 --> 01:02:30,287
One minute you're asking her for a letter,
the next you're asking me?

1196
01:02:30,329 --> 01:02:32,745
Look here, it won't take me a second to
lose my temper and show you my other side.

1197
01:02:32,787 --> 01:02:33,662
I'm warning you!

1198
01:02:34,454 --> 01:02:36,662
Sir! What else do you expect me to do?

1199
01:02:36,704 --> 01:02:38,995
Even with a job, it's impossible
for me to handle the problems I have.

1200
01:02:39,037 --> 01:02:40,245
With no work to be found here,

1201
01:02:40,287 --> 01:02:41,828
I literally begged and cried
to my friend in Dubai,

1202
01:02:41,829 --> 01:02:43,453
and managed to secure a job
that included four months of training.

1203
01:02:43,454 --> 01:02:44,829
But they went and threw dirt on that, too!

1204
01:02:44,870 --> 01:02:47,162
Sir, I know all about that company.

1205
01:02:47,204 --> 01:02:50,536
Why does he need to go now for
a job that only starts in four months?

1206
01:02:50,537 --> 01:02:51,495
For his position,

1207
01:02:51,537 --> 01:02:54,078
that exact company provides customized
training right here in Chennai!

1208
01:02:54,079 --> 01:02:55,745
Just to escape from me...

1209
01:02:55,787 --> 01:02:58,079
he is deliberately using training
as an excuse to run off to Dubai!

1210
01:02:58,745 --> 01:03:01,620
Did you see that, sir? She filed this
case knowing absolutely everything!

1211
01:03:01,877 --> 01:03:03,454
She will never let me go to Dubai, sir.

1212
01:03:03,745 --> 01:03:05,204
You must get her to sign that L3 for me!

1213
01:03:05,495 --> 01:03:06,662
I'm not signing any L3!

1214
01:03:06,745 --> 01:03:07,745
And why won't you?!

1215
01:03:07,787 --> 01:03:09,203
Sir, did I force him to
fall in love with me?

1216
01:03:09,204 --> 01:03:10,454
Hold on, hold on, hold on!

1217
01:03:10,829 --> 01:03:13,912
How did he make you love him?
At least you tell me.

1218
01:03:14,204 --> 01:03:15,579
Is that what's important right now, sir?

1219
01:03:15,620 --> 01:03:17,537
Ugh... fine, you won't tell me either.

1220
01:03:17,704 --> 01:03:19,912
Okay, at least you spit out whatever
you came to say and get it over with!

1221
01:03:20,745 --> 01:03:23,078
Sir, after doing everything I liked

1222
01:03:23,079 --> 01:03:26,245
and acting exactly how
I wanted for four whole years...

1223
01:03:26,287 --> 01:03:27,745
how can he suddenly just say
he doesn't want me anymore, sir?

1224
01:03:27,787 --> 01:03:31,454
If he just comes and talks to my mom,
we can convince her.

1225
01:03:32,037 --> 01:03:34,412
Sir, tell him to come and talk
to my mother directly!

1226
01:03:34,454 --> 01:03:37,661
Did you see that, sir? Even now, she only
thinks about herself and her mother...

1227
01:03:37,662 --> 01:03:39,162
but does she ever think about me, sir?

1228
01:03:39,204 --> 01:03:41,620
She genuinely believes the entire
world revolves around her, sir!

1229
01:03:41,662 --> 01:03:43,244
I did everything for her, sir.

1230
01:03:43,245 --> 01:03:46,370
Sir, doesn't everyone do this for
each other when they're in love?

1231
01:03:46,995 --> 01:03:49,245
Which 'everyone'?
And who exactly is doing what for whom?

1232
01:03:49,454 --> 01:03:51,453
You mean what every single guy
out there blindly does for a girl!

1233
01:03:51,454 --> 01:03:52,869
Because I loved her,

1234
01:03:52,870 --> 01:03:55,286
my time is gone,
my career is gone,

1235
01:03:55,287 --> 01:03:57,120
the trust my family had in me is gone,

1236
01:03:57,162 --> 01:03:59,036
and my dignity is
completely shattered!

1237
01:03:59,037 --> 01:04:01,745
If I marry her, my whole life is over!

1238
01:04:01,787 --> 01:04:03,537
Sir, I absolutely do not want her!

1239
01:04:05,037 --> 01:04:07,203
I truly thought he did all of this
because he wanted to, sir.

1240
01:04:07,204 --> 01:04:09,912
I never realized he was
suffering this much to do it.

1241
01:04:10,079 --> 01:04:11,953
But sir... in the end, I'm the only one
standing here losing everything, aren't I?

1242
01:04:11,954 --> 01:04:13,620
So, what do you want her
to do about it now?

1243
01:04:17,287 --> 01:04:19,495
Sir, it’s easy to be Avantika
in a relationship.

1244
01:04:19,662 --> 01:04:21,204
But it’s incredibly hard to be Raghuvaran.

1245
01:04:21,245 --> 01:04:23,787
If she can, just let her try being
in my shoes for a four months.

1246
01:04:23,829 --> 01:04:24,661
Let's see if she can handle it.

1247
01:04:24,662 --> 01:04:26,204
- I don't understand!
- Sir...

1248
01:04:26,537 --> 01:04:28,704
Everything I did for her during
these four years of love...

1249
01:04:28,745 --> 01:04:30,954
tell her to do the exact same things
for me for just four months, sir!

1250
01:04:31,120 --> 01:04:33,787
Whether she has a bike or not, she must
pick and drop me off every single day.

1251
01:04:33,829 --> 01:04:36,579
Whether she likes it or not,
she must only do what I want!

1252
01:04:36,620 --> 01:04:40,745
Whether she has time or not, she must
be available for me 24/7 like a genie!

1253
01:04:40,787 --> 01:04:42,786
With a mere 40,000 salary,

1254
01:04:42,787 --> 01:04:44,494
she must run around carrying a
one-lakh rupee financial burden for her!

1255
01:04:44,495 --> 01:04:46,495
Tell her to do all
of this back for me, sir.

1256
01:04:46,537 --> 01:04:48,037
Then I will gladly go
and talk to her mother!

1257
01:04:48,079 --> 01:04:49,579
But if she can't do it...

1258
01:04:49,620 --> 01:04:51,036
tell her to sign the L3
and get out of my life, sir!

1259
01:04:51,037 --> 01:04:52,370
- That's the end of it.
- Okay, sir.

1260
01:04:52,412 --> 01:04:53,869
Sir, I'm ready to become Raghuvaran.

1261
01:04:53,870 --> 01:04:56,162
You'll change?!
Hey, are you out of your mind?

1262
01:04:56,662 --> 01:04:59,119
Sir, just give me two minutes...
I'll talk to her alone and come back, sir.

1263
01:04:59,120 --> 01:05:00,120
Hmm, hmm.

1264
01:05:00,579 --> 01:05:01,412
Ma'am?!

1265
01:05:01,454 --> 01:05:02,454
Look at you!

1266
01:05:02,495 --> 01:05:03,911
Don't talk in haste!

1267
01:05:03,912 --> 01:05:06,454
He's just trying to drag you into
a massive trap and trap you!

1268
01:05:06,787 --> 01:05:10,287
We can never actually do the things
that guys do when they're in love.

1269
01:05:10,704 --> 01:05:14,454
Just shut up, sign that L3,
and make your escape!

1270
01:05:14,620 --> 01:05:16,037
What are you saying, ma'am?

1271
01:05:16,537 --> 01:05:18,662
He isn't just my first love...

1272
01:05:18,745 --> 01:05:20,245
He is the sum of all my love!

1273
01:05:20,454 --> 01:05:22,204
When I asked him to marry me,

1274
01:05:22,287 --> 01:05:24,495
even I didn’t think about my own mother.

1275
01:05:24,620 --> 01:05:25,787
But he did.

1276
01:05:25,870 --> 01:05:27,579
Even at the police station the last time,

1277
01:05:27,745 --> 01:05:29,787
when my mother came and
spoke so terribly to him...

1278
01:05:29,912 --> 01:05:32,787
he never pointed fingers at me or said
I was the one spending his money, ma'am.

1279
01:05:32,829 --> 01:05:34,537
Anyone can find a guy who loves them.

1280
01:05:34,620 --> 01:05:36,870
But she will never find a man who willingly
takes the blame just to protect her.

1281
01:05:37,162 --> 01:05:38,495
I want him, ma'am.

1282
01:05:38,537 --> 01:05:40,454
Go to hell!
Come, let's get back in there.

1283
01:05:46,204 --> 01:05:49,037
Sir... whatever he said,
I will do it all, sir!

1284
01:05:50,370 --> 01:05:52,329
She said she'll do it, right?
Now get lost!

1285
01:06:01,495 --> 01:06:02,995
- Be gone, evil Satan!
- Huh?!

1286
01:06:04,329 --> 01:06:05,120
Give me your hand.

1287
01:06:05,829 --> 01:06:07,787
Welcome to the Men's World!

1288
01:06:09,037 --> 01:06:11,370
I can't even begin to imagine what's going
to happen over the next four months...

1289
01:06:11,412 --> 01:06:13,037
♪ I’m not a broke boy,
I’m a rogue boy! ♪

1290
01:06:13,079 --> 01:06:14,579
♪ Not your boy toy,
I’m Popeye! ♪

1291
01:06:14,620 --> 01:06:16,079
♪ Those who touched me
have never been spared! ♪

1292
01:06:16,120 --> 01:06:17,704
♪ In this story,
I’m the tortoise! ♪

1293
01:06:17,745 --> 01:06:19,287
♪ I slipped a bit,
lost my balance! ♪

1294
01:06:19,329 --> 01:06:20,870
♪ I’m not like I was before,
I’ve transformed! ♪

1295
01:06:20,912 --> 01:06:22,454
Follow me!
♪ Now, I’m going to do stuff differently! ♪

1296
01:06:22,495 --> 01:06:25,036
♪ Watch me climb up
and strike like Maari! ♪

1297
01:06:25,037 --> 01:06:27,995
♪ Yeah, I’ll climb up
and strike like Maari! ♪

1298
01:06:28,037 --> 01:06:30,162
[a movie scene on TV]<i>"Let the butterfly you love fly away."</i>

1299
01:06:30,704 --> 01:06:32,620
<i>"If it returns, it was always yours."</i>

1300
01:06:32,954 --> 01:06:35,286
<i>"And if it doesn't, let it go.
That's your words!"</i>

1301
01:06:35,287 --> 01:06:36,454
<i>"Did I really say that?"</i>

1302
01:06:37,162 --> 01:06:38,704
[movie scene continues on TV]
[phone rings]

1303
01:06:38,745 --> 01:06:40,287
Hello, tell me Kishore.

1304
01:06:40,329 --> 01:06:43,620
Avantika, there is a client meeting
at 9.30 tomorrow. Please join.

1305
01:06:43,870 --> 01:06:45,454
Okay, I will take care of it.

1306
01:06:46,329 --> 01:06:48,995
The moment I pick up my phone,
they start pestering the life out of me!

1307
01:06:49,037 --> 01:06:50,412
<i>"...I gave it deep thought
and made a decision, too."</i>

1308
01:06:51,287 --> 01:06:56,162
<i>"I’ve taken a bulldozer to the temple
I built in my own heart."</i>

1309
01:06:57,704 --> 01:06:58,287
[whispers]
Hello.

1310
01:06:58,412 --> 01:06:59,829
- Where are you?
- At home.

1311
01:06:59,912 --> 01:07:01,370
Be wherever you want,

1312
01:07:01,620 --> 01:07:03,079
but I've got a training class
first thing tomorrow morning.

1313
01:07:03,120 --> 01:07:05,579
I will be at Tattoo's room.
Come and pick me up.

1314
01:07:05,620 --> 01:07:07,370
Oh no! I can't do it.

1315
01:07:07,620 --> 01:07:09,870
There is a client meeting
at 9.30 tomorrow.

1316
01:07:09,912 --> 01:07:11,954
It is your job to pick me up
and drop me.

1317
01:07:12,370 --> 01:07:15,162
You said you will do
what boys do in love, right?

1318
01:07:15,954 --> 01:07:17,204
Come and do it.

1319
01:07:17,245 --> 01:07:19,162
I can't do it.
You better get a cab.

1320
01:07:19,912 --> 01:07:22,120
I’ll see how you manage
to go to that client meeting.

1321
01:07:22,704 --> 01:07:23,579
Hey, Google!

1322
01:07:24,287 --> 01:07:25,745
Call, Harichandran sir.

1323
01:07:26,079 --> 01:07:27,245
[phone rings]

1324
01:07:27,537 --> 01:07:28,412
Tell me, sir.

1325
01:07:28,454 --> 01:07:29,995
You don’t need to go
to the office tomorrow.

1326
01:07:30,079 --> 01:07:31,537
Apparently, he isn’t going
to his training class either.

1327
01:07:31,579 --> 01:07:33,244
And he told me not to go anywhere, too.

1328
01:07:33,245 --> 01:07:36,244
Both of you just come down to the station
and hand over that L3 form he asked for.

1329
01:07:36,245 --> 01:07:38,412
You do your job. He will do his job.

1330
01:07:38,454 --> 01:07:39,661
And I will do my job.

1331
01:07:39,662 --> 01:07:40,620
Sir, sir...

1332
01:07:40,787 --> 01:07:42,037
Don't do all that, sir.

1333
01:07:42,579 --> 01:07:45,120
I've got to pick him up, right?
I will do it, sir.

1334
01:07:45,162 --> 01:07:47,454
We can just head over to Mayajaal,
catch a movie, and then head back home.

1335
01:07:47,495 --> 01:07:48,619
We can have lunch on the way.

1336
01:07:48,620 --> 01:07:51,120
We can buy your favourite
ice cream as well.

1337
01:07:52,829 --> 01:07:54,579
- You’re in love?
- We are, sir.

1338
01:07:54,620 --> 01:07:55,662
Bloody hell! Just get out of here!

1339
01:07:56,204 --> 01:07:58,079
First you roam around
glued to each other,

1340
01:07:58,120 --> 01:08:00,454
and then you split up and bring
your messy drama to me!

1341
01:08:01,454 --> 01:08:04,037
If you drive this slowly,
I won't reach my class until tomorrow!

1342
01:08:10,454 --> 01:08:12,745
This is as fast as I can drive.
If you're in such a hurry, you drive!

1343
01:08:13,037 --> 01:08:13,620
Fine, get on.

1344
01:08:17,412 --> 01:08:19,745
Hey, whenever you ride on my bike,
is this how you sit?

1345
01:08:19,787 --> 01:08:20,537
Fine.

1346
01:08:21,412 --> 01:08:22,412
Hey...

1347
01:08:23,079 --> 01:08:23,829
What?

1348
01:08:24,204 --> 01:08:25,370
Further back.

1349
01:08:25,620 --> 01:08:26,620
Even further!

1350
01:08:27,412 --> 01:08:28,870
Even further!

1351
01:08:30,454 --> 01:08:32,911
Any further back and I'd have
to ride on the vehicle behind us!

1352
01:08:32,912 --> 01:08:34,870
Okay, come safely.
I'm already late for class!

1353
01:08:35,995 --> 01:08:36,870
Oh...

1354
01:08:37,120 --> 01:08:37,954
Bye.

1355
01:08:45,204 --> 01:08:46,454
[punches the punching bag]
Hi, Raghu!

1356
01:08:48,537 --> 01:08:50,120
[punches with more force]

1357
01:08:51,370 --> 01:08:52,162
[punches again]

1358
01:08:55,037 --> 01:08:55,870
Oh no!

1359
01:08:56,037 --> 01:08:57,662
Was he punching my photo all this time?!

1360
01:09:00,829 --> 01:09:02,704
Being together is one thing,
sticking photos together is another.

1361
01:09:02,787 --> 01:09:04,869
This isn't just fake, it wouldn't
even happen in my dreams.

1362
01:09:04,870 --> 01:09:06,620
Why are you talking so negatively?

1363
01:09:06,704 --> 01:09:08,161
Shall we go straight to your village

1364
01:09:08,162 --> 01:09:10,329
plead on our knees
and convince your parents

1365
01:09:10,454 --> 01:09:11,912
and bring them back? Huh?

1366
01:09:16,787 --> 01:09:18,245
Don't you have any conscience at all?

1367
01:09:18,287 --> 01:09:21,244
That day, when your mother humiliated
my parents at the police station,

1368
01:09:21,245 --> 01:09:23,037
you didn't even feel like apologizing.

1369
01:09:23,079 --> 01:09:24,954
My sister, she's younger than you,

1370
01:09:24,995 --> 01:09:26,495
do you have any idea how terrified she was?

1371
01:09:26,620 --> 01:09:28,370
You didn't even try to console her.

1372
01:09:28,412 --> 01:09:29,787
Today, because you need
something from them,

1373
01:09:29,829 --> 01:09:31,494
are you actually ready
to fall at their feet?

1374
01:09:31,495 --> 01:09:32,204
Listen!

1375
01:09:32,329 --> 01:09:34,287
Even if they ask me to marry you,

1376
01:09:34,579 --> 01:09:36,328
I’m not interested.

1377
01:09:36,329 --> 01:09:38,079
Leave me alone!
Here, take your phone.

1378
01:09:38,329 --> 01:09:39,787
I need to deal this with
the person behind her ideas.

1379
01:09:40,037 --> 01:09:41,829
Oh no!
He's leaving.

1380
01:09:41,995 --> 01:09:43,287
Hey, Raghu! Stop, stop!

1381
01:09:43,787 --> 01:09:45,954
Sorry for venting and messing up the vibe.

1382
01:09:46,204 --> 01:09:47,829
Let's talk about this later.

1383
01:09:47,870 --> 01:09:49,870
How can I make you feel better right now?

1384
01:09:52,037 --> 01:09:53,287
Will you get me some booze?

1385
01:09:55,120 --> 01:09:55,995
Me?!

1386
01:09:58,245 --> 01:10:01,162
Hey, why is the wine shop
marked as closed?

1387
01:10:01,204 --> 01:10:02,244
But so many people are standing here?

1388
01:10:02,245 --> 01:10:03,495
Just to buy alcohol in black.

1389
01:10:04,162 --> 01:10:04,704
Oh.

1390
01:10:05,537 --> 01:10:07,120
- Then what about you?
- In black, of course!

1391
01:10:07,745 --> 01:10:09,204
Go get it quickly.

1392
01:10:10,579 --> 01:10:11,579
What's wrong?

1393
01:10:13,329 --> 01:10:14,037
Hmm...

1394
01:10:14,829 --> 01:10:15,704
Alright, I'll go myself.

1395
01:10:15,870 --> 01:10:16,995
I told you I'd handle it myself.

1396
01:10:17,245 --> 01:10:18,119
I'll do it myself.

1397
01:10:18,120 --> 01:10:20,329
This holiday should not exist
in the next generation!

1398
01:10:23,079 --> 01:10:24,869
- Sorry, bro.
- Keep the sorry aside.

1399
01:10:24,870 --> 01:10:26,745
What are you doing here?

1400
01:10:26,870 --> 01:10:28,536
I came here to buy some booze in black.

1401
01:10:28,537 --> 01:10:29,329
In black?

1402
01:10:29,537 --> 01:10:30,537
You scoundrels!

1403
01:10:30,579 --> 01:10:32,495
Isn't drinking until midnight
at the pub enough,

1404
01:10:32,537 --> 01:10:34,412
that you've come to buy
in the black market at noon?

1405
01:10:34,454 --> 01:10:36,370
- Don't talk like a fool, bro.
- Like a fool?

1406
01:10:36,704 --> 01:10:39,037
Brother, how do you buy liquor in black?

1407
01:10:39,079 --> 01:10:41,662
Did you think this was as simple
as buying syrup at a pharmacy?

1408
01:10:41,704 --> 01:10:43,829
That's what all these wine shop
warriors are waiting for.

1409
01:10:43,870 --> 01:10:45,829
Once the shutter opens,
they'll dive in immediately.

1410
01:10:45,995 --> 01:10:47,328
See how they’re running
to ruin their livers?

1411
01:10:47,329 --> 01:10:48,829
Who the hell is stepping
on my foot while running?

1412
01:10:48,912 --> 01:10:51,869
Oh no! With so many people going,
how are we going to buy it, brother?

1413
01:10:51,870 --> 01:10:53,869
Earning the reputation of
a good husband from a wife

1414
01:10:53,870 --> 01:10:55,745
and diving in to buy beer
in black isn't that easy, dear.

1415
01:10:55,787 --> 01:10:56,786
Practice is key.

1416
01:10:56,787 --> 01:10:58,036
Oh no! It's getting late.

1417
01:10:58,037 --> 01:10:58,787
Why?

1418
01:10:58,912 --> 01:11:01,287
Do your hands and legs shake
at 12 o'clock just like mine?

1419
01:11:01,704 --> 01:11:04,203
Oh, the booze isn't for me,
it's for my boyfriend.

1420
01:11:04,204 --> 01:11:05,120
For your boyfriend?

1421
01:11:05,162 --> 01:11:07,245
I've seen girlfriends make
their boyfriends thirsty,

1422
01:11:07,287 --> 01:11:08,412
but this is the first time
I'm seeing a girlfriend

1423
01:11:08,454 --> 01:11:09,704
making her boyfriend happy
by getting him booze!

1424
01:11:09,745 --> 01:11:10,495
Bro!

1425
01:11:10,537 --> 01:11:11,828
You are very lucky!

1426
01:11:11,829 --> 01:11:13,579
He's been making me pay for it
since he has already given it to me.

1427
01:11:13,704 --> 01:11:14,994
Tell him to do whatever else he wants.

1428
01:11:14,995 --> 01:11:18,370
But tell him not to go and dance saying
'My love life failed...' after he's drunk.

1429
01:11:18,412 --> 01:11:19,704
- I'll let him know.
- I'm going in.

1430
01:11:20,495 --> 01:11:21,745
Hey, make way!

1431
01:11:22,454 --> 01:11:25,745
Oh man! I can't handle the pressure from
the wife, please, for the love of god.

1432
01:11:26,079 --> 01:11:27,662
Where is she?
Move aside!

1433
01:11:27,745 --> 01:11:29,786
Oh my, are you trying to sacrifice me
for the sake of your love?

1434
01:11:29,787 --> 01:11:31,329
You sent me inside without
giving me any money!

1435
01:11:31,370 --> 01:11:32,870
They're stomping all over my neck!
Give me the money!

1436
01:11:32,954 --> 01:11:35,120
- Oh no! Sorry, brother.
- Sorry? They're going to shut the shutters!

1437
01:11:35,162 --> 01:11:37,244
Move aside, you guys! You won't progress,
and you won't let me progress either!

1438
01:11:37,245 --> 01:11:39,954
Oh no, my sister's husband isn't well!

1439
01:11:39,995 --> 01:11:42,119
The doctor said he'd die
if he doesn't drink up soon.

1440
01:11:42,120 --> 01:11:46,203
Oh man, brother, just hold on
for five minutes! I'm coming right back.

1441
01:11:46,204 --> 01:11:47,454
Hey, make way, idiot!

1442
01:11:48,662 --> 01:11:50,120
This one's for me, this one's for you.

1443
01:11:50,162 --> 01:11:50,954
Oh my...

1444
01:11:51,412 --> 01:11:53,412
Raghu, success!

1445
01:11:53,537 --> 01:11:56,787
Hey, that's not my brand.
Mine is 280 rupees.

1446
01:11:57,037 --> 01:11:58,787
It's not his brand it seems. Give it here!

1447
01:12:02,579 --> 01:12:04,162
Hey bro, why did you drink that?

1448
01:12:04,204 --> 01:12:06,203
Only those who drink occasionally
look at the brand.

1449
01:12:06,204 --> 01:12:08,079
But for me, the very thing
I drink is the brand!

1450
01:12:08,204 --> 01:12:10,829
Brother, stop being annoying
and just go get the brand he asked for.

1451
01:12:10,995 --> 01:12:11,745
Sorry, girl.

1452
01:12:11,787 --> 01:12:14,995
My sister's husband doesn't like
that brand. Let me in!

1453
01:12:15,037 --> 01:12:16,204
Oh no! They got me.

1454
01:12:16,245 --> 01:12:19,204
Oh, girl! They blocked me right at
the entrance and pushed me out.

1455
01:12:19,245 --> 01:12:20,328
I couldn't get in.

1456
01:12:20,329 --> 01:12:23,912
You can't even get a drink in black,
you call yourself a man?

1457
01:12:23,954 --> 01:12:26,329
Oh! So that's how you talk?

1458
01:12:26,370 --> 01:12:28,245
That's exactly why
he's walking all over you.

1459
01:12:28,287 --> 01:12:30,204
Don't blame me,
you go take a round yourself, go!

1460
01:12:30,245 --> 01:12:31,579
Hey, hey, hey!

1461
01:12:33,995 --> 01:12:36,245
Oh no! Oh my... I can't breathe!

1462
01:12:37,245 --> 01:12:40,619
- Save me, brother! Save me, please...
- The great Titanic heroine...

1463
01:12:40,620 --> 01:12:42,454
she's raising her hands and screaming
in the ocean waves.

1464
01:12:42,495 --> 01:12:44,119
- I can't do this, brother!
- Are you speaking ill of men?

1465
01:12:44,120 --> 01:12:46,412
Just wait and watch, they are going to make
an omelet out of you and cast you out.

1466
01:12:46,454 --> 01:12:47,744
Brother, save me.

1467
01:12:47,745 --> 01:12:50,619
Please save me. brother!
Brother... brother, please...

1468
01:12:50,620 --> 01:12:52,620
Now you understand
the pain men face, don't you?

1469
01:12:52,662 --> 01:12:53,578
Save me!

1470
01:12:53,579 --> 01:12:55,620
- Save me, brother!
- Welcome back.

1471
01:12:57,954 --> 01:13:00,787
- Will you talk like that again?
- Never, brother! I will never talk.

1472
01:13:00,870 --> 01:13:02,412
Please brother, go and get it.

1473
01:13:02,995 --> 01:13:05,662
I can't do it for you.
I will get it for that boy.

1474
01:13:06,412 --> 01:13:08,995
Let me in! Did you come
to buy or stand in the way?

1475
01:13:09,495 --> 01:13:10,495
We won!

1476
01:13:11,329 --> 01:13:13,787
- I am the winner!
- Raghu... success!

1477
01:13:14,037 --> 01:13:14,412
Huh?!

1478
01:13:14,454 --> 01:13:16,245
- Why did you snatch it again?
- Where did I snatch it?

1479
01:13:16,287 --> 01:13:17,120
It was the Inspector.

1480
01:13:17,162 --> 01:13:19,203
Good morning, sir!
Hey, run! It's the police!

1481
01:13:19,204 --> 01:13:20,494
- Hey run! It's the police!
- Give it to me, sir!

1482
01:13:20,495 --> 01:13:22,162
- Here, take it! Move!
- Who is stepping on my foot again?

1483
01:13:22,204 --> 01:13:23,037
Hold this, come on, hold it!
Move!

1484
01:13:23,079 --> 01:13:24,079
- Run! Run!
- I'm already late!

1485
01:13:24,120 --> 01:13:26,870
- Bye, dude! Thank you!
- Hey, drop me and go.

1486
01:13:26,954 --> 01:13:28,870
No, I have a meeting now.

1487
01:13:29,204 --> 01:13:30,995
What? I'm asking you to drop me and go.

1488
01:13:31,037 --> 01:13:32,745
- Bye! Be safe!
- Hey! Hey!

1489
01:13:40,704 --> 01:13:42,204
Hey, who is it?
Why are you going inside?

1490
01:13:42,245 --> 01:13:43,954
The housekeeping time is over,
why are you coming now?

1491
01:13:47,245 --> 01:13:49,578
Hey! Who are you calling housekeeping?

1492
01:13:49,579 --> 01:13:51,204
- I'm Avantika.
- Which Avantika?

1493
01:13:51,245 --> 01:13:53,079
Hey, you're always ogling, aren't you?

1494
01:13:53,120 --> 01:13:55,037
Always smirking and fawning
with a "Good morning,"

1495
01:13:55,079 --> 01:13:55,954
that Avantika!

1496
01:13:55,995 --> 01:13:57,744
Madam, whenever you come there,
a scent hits me here,

1497
01:13:57,745 --> 01:13:58,870
why have you come like this?

1498
01:13:59,537 --> 01:14:00,954
Why? What happened?

1499
01:14:00,995 --> 01:14:02,370
Is this her original look?

1500
01:14:03,995 --> 01:14:07,120
I thought you would look
after me in all sorts of ways,

1501
01:14:07,245 --> 01:14:09,662
but I never imagined you would
make me look after you like this.

1502
01:14:09,704 --> 01:14:10,662
Bloody Raghu!

1503
01:14:13,745 --> 01:14:15,454
Massage a little more here...

1504
01:14:16,370 --> 01:14:17,869
- right on my shoulder.
- She looks worn out.

1505
01:14:17,870 --> 01:14:19,370
Here, massage my hand as well.

1506
01:14:20,079 --> 01:14:20,995
What happened?

1507
01:14:21,037 --> 01:14:22,954
Oh my... why do you even ask?

1508
01:14:22,995 --> 01:14:25,744
I’ve been travelling with him
since this morning...

1509
01:14:25,745 --> 01:14:30,079
I hit a speed breaker, and boy,
it gave a sharp jolt.

1510
01:14:31,037 --> 01:14:32,370
My back is aching so badly.

1511
01:14:32,412 --> 01:14:33,619
If it’s already this much
after just one week,

1512
01:14:33,620 --> 01:14:35,454
wait until the four weeks are over.

1513
01:14:35,495 --> 01:14:38,870
Oh no, Merlin, please don't start!
Don't just go around supporting him.

1514
01:14:39,579 --> 01:14:41,037
Okay... where is Mamtha?

1515
01:14:41,704 --> 01:14:43,286
She just went to meet Kishore.

1516
01:14:43,287 --> 01:14:46,370
I think she has gone to discuss
about the on-site project.

1517
01:14:47,412 --> 01:14:49,954
- Is she going for the on-site project?!
- Hmm.

1518
01:14:50,870 --> 01:14:52,245
Actually, I wanted to go.

1519
01:14:52,287 --> 01:14:53,954
- Kishore, this project's report...
- Hey, Mamtha!

1520
01:14:54,412 --> 01:14:55,412
- One second.
- Okay.

1521
01:14:55,454 --> 01:14:56,578
Bro, I need a favour from you.

1522
01:14:56,579 --> 01:14:59,203
- I definitely cannot give you a leave.
- No, bro. Not that.

1523
01:14:59,204 --> 01:15:01,119
You are discussing about
the on-site project, right?

1524
01:15:01,120 --> 01:15:01,912
Yes.

1525
01:15:02,704 --> 01:15:03,912
This year, let me go.

1526
01:15:03,954 --> 01:15:06,620
Hey Avi, you’ve never really had
much interest in on-site work, have you?

1527
01:15:06,662 --> 01:15:07,495
What's new now?

1528
01:15:07,537 --> 01:15:09,954
Even if that were the case, your mom
wouldn't let you go alone, would she?

1529
01:15:09,995 --> 01:15:12,120
I will manage that. You please...

1530
01:15:13,245 --> 01:15:14,287
She is irritating me.

1531
01:15:14,745 --> 01:15:15,954
Bro, please count me in.

1532
01:15:15,995 --> 01:15:17,495
I have a lot of commitments.

1533
01:15:17,537 --> 01:15:19,704
If I get that project,
it will be very helpful.

1534
01:15:19,745 --> 01:15:21,244
So please, let me go this year.

1535
01:15:21,245 --> 01:15:22,744
Kishore, you have nothing to worry about.

1536
01:15:22,745 --> 01:15:23,954
I'm not worried about that.

1537
01:15:25,037 --> 01:15:27,329
You don't do the work properly here.

1538
01:15:27,370 --> 01:15:29,287
You don't respond to my calls at all.

1539
01:15:29,704 --> 01:15:31,870
You’re coming and going as you please...

1540
01:15:31,954 --> 01:15:33,869
Bro, but I told you
I wanted permission, didn't I?

1541
01:15:33,870 --> 01:15:36,245
Permission isn't about telling,
it's about asking!

1542
01:15:36,412 --> 01:15:38,204
When have you ever
asked me for permission?

1543
01:15:38,245 --> 01:15:40,036
Oh no, bro. I will 'ask'
permission from now.

1544
01:15:40,037 --> 01:15:42,662
So you'll ask for permission, but you
still won't commit to working properly?

1545
01:15:42,704 --> 01:15:44,412
Bro, I didn't mean it like that.

1546
01:15:44,537 --> 01:15:46,037
I'll take care of the work, I promise.

1547
01:15:46,079 --> 01:15:47,829
- Please, just add my name.
- Hmm.

1548
01:15:47,870 --> 01:15:48,870
Thanks, bro!

1549
01:15:51,037 --> 01:15:52,162
I will add you.

1550
01:15:52,454 --> 01:15:53,454
Hey, Mamtha!

1551
01:15:55,995 --> 01:15:57,537
Thanks for letting it go.

1552
01:15:58,037 --> 01:16:00,829
- No, I don't get it. Did I let it go?
- Yes!

1553
01:16:00,870 --> 01:16:01,579
Yeah, yeah.

1554
01:16:01,954 --> 01:16:04,037
Ms. Avantika,
the Inspector's here to meet you.

1555
01:16:04,329 --> 01:16:04,828
Hey?!

1556
01:16:04,829 --> 01:16:06,619
- Inspector?!
- He's waiting downstairs.

1557
01:16:06,620 --> 01:16:08,495
Oh, no! Why did he come?

1558
01:16:08,662 --> 01:16:10,912
Why are you making me stand out
here in this scorching heat?

1559
01:16:10,954 --> 01:16:13,744
There are much bigger criminals
in town for you to catch, sir.

1560
01:16:13,745 --> 01:16:16,578
Why are you focusing only on me?

1561
01:16:16,579 --> 01:16:19,454
I was chasing the accused.

1562
01:16:19,495 --> 01:16:21,537
He ended up chasing me
and made me wait here.

1563
01:16:21,829 --> 01:16:24,619
He said you left halfway through,
and insisted that I drop him off.

1564
01:16:24,620 --> 01:16:27,537
Was I given this jeep
just to drive him around?

1565
01:16:28,495 --> 01:16:30,454
Sir, he didn’t even care that I’m a woman,

1566
01:16:30,579 --> 01:16:32,745
he told me to buy him booze in black.

1567
01:16:32,787 --> 01:16:34,662
I even bought it for him
before I came here.

1568
01:16:35,079 --> 01:16:37,537
Hey, this is too much.

1569
01:16:37,579 --> 01:16:38,162
Sir...

1570
01:16:38,579 --> 01:16:39,537
Just a minute, sir.

1571
01:16:43,495 --> 01:16:45,078
<i>"Raghu, I'm hungry."</i>

1572
01:16:45,079 --> 01:16:46,954
<i>- "Hey, it's 2 o'clock in the night."
- "Why?"</i>

1573
01:16:47,037 --> 01:16:48,245
<i>"We shouldn't be hungry
at 2 o'clock in the night?"</i>

1574
01:16:48,412 --> 01:16:50,870
<i>"Just go grab some of that
midnight biryani."</i>

1575
01:16:52,204 --> 01:16:53,162
There's one more, sir.

1576
01:16:53,245 --> 01:16:54,412
Oh no... not that one.

1577
01:16:56,204 --> 01:16:59,204
<i>"Raghu, my friends and I have
planned to see the IPL."</i>

1578
01:16:59,245 --> 01:17:00,745
<i>"Arrange 5 tickets."</i>

1579
01:17:00,787 --> 01:17:02,454
<i>"Hey, are you kidding me?"</i>

1580
01:17:02,495 --> 01:17:04,954
<i>"There will be 5,000 people in the queue.
I'll have to stand there all night long."</i>

1581
01:17:04,995 --> 01:17:07,704
<i>"Stand! You claim to be in love,
you can't even do this?"</i>

1582
01:17:07,745 --> 01:17:09,495
- Give that to me!
- <i>"What better work do you have?"</i>

1583
01:17:09,662 --> 01:17:11,620
Sir, do you know why she
snatched my phone in such a hurry?

1584
01:17:11,662 --> 01:17:13,870
She then went on to curse me
with the filthiest language.

1585
01:17:15,579 --> 01:17:18,579
What can I do? He’s got
all the evidence against you.

1586
01:17:18,704 --> 01:17:20,328
Just give that L3 and go.

1587
01:17:20,329 --> 01:17:22,537
I have to be the one
running errands for your love.

1588
01:17:22,662 --> 01:17:24,745
Sir, let me take permission and come back.

1589
01:17:25,162 --> 01:17:26,704
I'll drop him off myself.

1590
01:17:27,495 --> 01:17:28,329
Take it.

1591
01:17:28,495 --> 01:17:30,120
The TL is going to give me a real earful.

1592
01:17:30,954 --> 01:17:32,954
Sir, it looks like she'll take some time.

1593
01:17:33,037 --> 01:17:34,537
Can you keep me company
for about 10 minutes?

1594
01:17:34,579 --> 01:17:36,620
Not only did you stop me
from doing my duty,

1595
01:17:36,662 --> 01:17:38,287
but you actually want me
to keep you company?

1596
01:17:39,079 --> 01:17:40,704
- Hey, come here!
- Sir?

1597
01:17:43,037 --> 01:17:44,078
Hmm, tell me, sir.

1598
01:17:44,079 --> 01:17:46,995
Here! He says he wants 10 minutes
of company. Go keep him company!

1599
01:17:47,162 --> 01:17:48,495
You'll go crazy in a little while.

1600
01:17:48,704 --> 01:17:51,245
- Thank you, sir!
- I think I should get L3 from him first.

1601
01:17:51,454 --> 01:17:52,245
My fate!

1602
01:17:52,662 --> 01:17:54,453
Bro, shall I tell you my story?

1603
01:17:54,454 --> 01:17:55,454
Bye, sir!

1604
01:17:55,495 --> 01:17:56,495
Get lost!

1605
01:17:58,620 --> 01:18:00,912
Hey, there's a tea shop!
Stop, stop, stop!

1606
01:18:00,954 --> 01:18:03,370
Finally, it crossed your mind
to buy me a tea.

1607
01:18:04,579 --> 01:18:06,662
My head is throbbing,
go buy me a cup of tea.

1608
01:18:07,870 --> 01:18:09,412
You won't even do that?

1609
01:18:09,454 --> 01:18:10,829
I'm the one who's supposed
to buy it for you, right?

1610
01:18:10,870 --> 01:18:11,995
Why should I buy it for you?

1611
01:18:13,162 --> 01:18:14,495
He’s already having tea here.

1612
01:18:14,537 --> 01:18:16,412
- Hi, Chetta!
- Is he going to add this to my tab too?

1613
01:18:16,662 --> 01:18:17,662
Hi, Tattoo brother!

1614
01:18:19,579 --> 01:18:20,620
- Chetta!
- Yes?

1615
01:18:20,662 --> 01:18:21,954
- One tea...
- Huh...

1616
01:18:22,120 --> 01:18:23,745
- Can I get an apology as well?
- Yes, you can.

1617
01:18:23,787 --> 01:18:26,204
Chetta, never sign security for anything.

1618
01:18:26,537 --> 01:18:28,537
The people who owe money
are out having the time of their lives.

1619
01:18:28,579 --> 01:18:30,703
And here I am, having
to hide under a blanket.

1620
01:18:30,704 --> 01:18:33,829
Both of you stay in the same room.
Why don't you talk to each other?

1621
01:18:33,870 --> 01:18:36,162
Look who’s talking!
The mighty peacemaker himself.

1622
01:18:36,204 --> 01:18:37,370
Oh, so we're letting
white pigeons fly, are we?

1623
01:18:37,412 --> 01:18:38,745
Just make the tea!

1624
01:18:38,829 --> 01:18:41,079
Go play peacemaker with
your wife who went away first.

1625
01:18:41,204 --> 01:18:42,787
Why is Tattoo brother leaving angrily?

1626
01:18:42,829 --> 01:18:45,037
You went to Ooty and blew money on
a wedding that never even happened,

1627
01:18:45,204 --> 01:18:47,036
that was the money he got us
using himself as collateral.

1628
01:18:47,037 --> 01:18:48,870
Give back that wedding necklace
and the silk saree,

1629
01:18:48,954 --> 01:18:50,328
and he might just make peace.

1630
01:18:50,329 --> 01:18:51,829
What? Will you return it?

1631
01:18:51,954 --> 01:18:52,786
Oh no!

1632
01:18:52,787 --> 01:18:54,870
That was the first purchase
for our wedding.

1633
01:18:54,912 --> 01:18:57,037
Those are memories.
I won’t give them back.

1634
01:18:57,204 --> 01:18:59,495
- Your tea's ready!
- As if you will give back if you could.

1635
01:19:00,287 --> 01:19:01,329
- Thanks, Chetta.
- Huh.

1636
01:19:05,579 --> 01:19:07,037
Fine... you can go now.

1637
01:19:07,370 --> 01:19:08,995
Pick me up tomorrow morning.

1638
01:19:09,120 --> 01:19:10,412
Eh... Raghu.

1639
01:19:10,620 --> 01:19:11,704
Can I give you something?

1640
01:19:14,079 --> 01:19:16,620
You're giving me the L3 today?
Thank you so much!

1641
01:19:16,787 --> 01:19:18,829
This is not L3, it's L2.

1642
01:19:18,954 --> 01:19:19,912
Love Letter?

1643
01:19:20,287 --> 01:19:22,037
Wasn't it enough that I loved you once?

1644
01:19:22,162 --> 01:19:24,745
- Must I love you again and again?
- L2 means Leave Letter.

1645
01:19:25,245 --> 01:19:27,204
Oh... L2 means Leave Letter?

1646
01:19:27,245 --> 01:19:28,245
Mmm hmm.

1647
01:19:29,412 --> 01:19:30,912
Dear Raghuvaran...

1648
01:19:33,329 --> 01:19:36,994
It's my 'Office Day' tomorrow,
so I can't come over to pick you up.

1649
01:19:36,995 --> 01:19:38,911
Honestly, after spending the
whole week hanging out with you,

1650
01:19:38,912 --> 01:19:41,037
even my office security
doesn't recognize me anymore.

1651
01:19:41,329 --> 01:19:44,870
I need tomorrow off just to freshen up
and put on some makeup for work.

1652
01:19:44,995 --> 01:19:48,537
So, I’m requesting a one-day leave.

1653
01:19:49,079 --> 01:19:50,495
Your's faithfully, Avantika.

1654
01:19:52,037 --> 01:19:53,537
Full of spelling mistakes!

1655
01:19:53,704 --> 01:19:55,370
And you call yourself
a Communication Engineer.

1656
01:19:56,870 --> 01:19:58,412
Just one day, right? Take it.

1657
01:20:00,037 --> 01:20:01,329
- Thanks, Raghu!
- Hmm.

1658
01:20:06,162 --> 01:20:08,204
[song plays on loudspeaker]

1659
01:20:11,495 --> 01:20:14,869
♪ Hey, listen up, rhythmic thunder,
Popping off, bursting under... ♪

1660
01:20:14,870 --> 01:20:16,704
♪ Caught in the trap,
pulling through, Pistah! ♪

1661
01:20:16,745 --> 01:20:19,620
♪ Keep the rhythm, watch it grow,
move it fast, Pistah! ♪

1662
01:20:19,662 --> 01:20:21,912
♪ Keep the rhythm, watch it grow,
move it fast! ♪

1663
01:20:22,620 --> 01:20:26,036
♪ Hey, listen up, rhythmic thunder,
Popping off, bursting under... ♪

1664
01:20:26,037 --> 01:20:27,870
♪ Caught in the trap,
pulling through, Pistah! ♪

1665
01:20:27,912 --> 01:20:30,704
♪ Keep the rhythm, watch it grow,
move it fast, Pistah! ♪

1666
01:20:30,745 --> 01:20:33,120
♪ Keep the rhythm, watch it grow,
move it fast! ♪

1667
01:20:33,829 --> 01:20:36,454
♪ Boom! Hey! ♪

1668
01:20:36,495 --> 01:20:39,453
♪ Hey, drumming, thumping,
shaking the ground, Boom! ♪

1669
01:20:39,454 --> 01:20:42,495
♪ Hey, beat it, strike it,
let it ring out! ♪

1670
01:20:42,537 --> 01:20:46,245
♪ Lock it in, keep it moving, go, go! ♪

1671
01:20:46,370 --> 01:20:47,579
- Greetings, madam.
- Hi!

1672
01:20:48,204 --> 01:20:50,037
I haven't seen you people here before.

1673
01:20:50,537 --> 01:20:52,369
- Which branch are you?
- I'm from the Adyar branch.

1674
01:20:52,370 --> 01:20:53,245
Oh!

1675
01:20:54,662 --> 01:20:56,245
- Which branch are you?
- I'm from the Anna Nagar branch!

1676
01:20:56,287 --> 01:20:57,204
Greetings.

1677
01:20:57,495 --> 01:20:59,954
Wait, my company doesn't
even have a branch there.

1678
01:20:59,995 --> 01:21:01,537
And we aren't from your office!

1679
01:21:04,204 --> 01:21:05,579
Then who asked you to come?

1680
01:21:05,620 --> 01:21:07,412
Look! He’s the one!

1681
01:21:26,662 --> 01:21:28,412
Why’d you stop? Dance!

1682
01:21:28,954 --> 01:21:30,162
Who are these people?

1683
01:21:30,204 --> 01:21:32,578
These people?
They came to see me.

1684
01:21:32,579 --> 01:21:34,370
I brought them to see you.

1685
01:21:34,495 --> 01:21:35,662
Why should they see me?

1686
01:21:35,704 --> 01:21:38,619
Six months of missed EMIs.
They came and asked me.

1687
01:21:38,620 --> 01:21:41,204
You're the one who promised
to handle it for the next four months.

1688
01:21:41,245 --> 01:21:42,287
Answer them now.

1689
01:21:42,870 --> 01:21:45,197
Why did you have to bring them here
in front of everyone?

1690
01:21:51,704 --> 01:21:53,829
They cornered me
on the street just like this.

1691
01:21:53,954 --> 01:21:56,162
One guy even snatched my bike
right in the middle of the road.

1692
01:21:56,954 --> 01:21:57,704
And this guy here...

1693
01:21:58,079 --> 01:22:00,954
he asked me to pay up right in the middle
of the office, in front of everyone!

1694
01:22:01,162 --> 01:22:03,245
Another one rejected my loan
and just vanished.

1695
01:22:04,120 --> 01:22:06,204
Humiliation doesn’t come with a warning.

1696
01:22:06,245 --> 01:22:06,620
Look...

1697
01:22:07,370 --> 01:22:09,162
it just shows up on your doorstep,
out of nowhere, just like this.

1698
01:22:10,787 --> 01:22:11,454
Hmm...

1699
01:22:12,245 --> 01:22:13,245
Can't pay?

1700
01:22:13,662 --> 01:22:16,412
If you can't, just sign the L3.
I'll take care of all these people myself.

1701
01:22:16,579 --> 01:22:17,745
You can walk away free.

1702
01:22:18,245 --> 01:22:20,787
Okay... I’ll settle this.

1703
01:22:20,829 --> 01:22:22,120
Just tell me how much he owes to whom.

1704
01:22:31,745 --> 01:22:33,704
- How much do we owe you?
- 94,000 rupees, madam.

1705
01:22:33,729 --> 01:22:34,329
Huh?!

1706
01:22:34,787 --> 01:22:36,662
What did you do for 94,000 rupees?

1707
01:22:36,704 --> 01:22:37,912
What did I do?

1708
01:22:38,204 --> 01:22:39,287
You’re the one who did this to me!

1709
01:22:39,329 --> 01:22:42,079
hat useless necklace you bought?
This is the result of that.

1710
01:22:42,120 --> 01:22:44,704
It was only 50,000 and change, wasn't it?

1711
01:22:44,787 --> 01:22:46,079
Why do we have to pay 94,000 rupees?

1712
01:22:46,120 --> 01:22:49,995
It would’ve been 56,000 rupees if
you’d paid within the 45-day billing cycle.

1713
01:22:50,037 --> 01:22:51,454
But you didn't pay anything at all!

1714
01:22:51,912 --> 01:22:52,662
Why didn't you pay?

1715
01:22:52,704 --> 01:22:55,037
I had the money ready to pay that off.

1716
01:22:55,204 --> 01:22:56,287
But then you called me and said,

1717
01:22:56,454 --> 01:23:00,995
'Raghu, my birthday is next week,
surprise me with an iPhone!'

1718
01:23:01,454 --> 01:23:03,079
And you know what the highlight is?

1719
01:23:03,120 --> 01:23:05,120
The fact that you asked
for your own 'surprise'...

1720
01:23:05,162 --> 01:23:06,245
that’s the highlight!

1721
01:23:06,287 --> 01:23:06,995
Okay...

1722
01:23:07,620 --> 01:23:10,787
but how would you get
an iPhone for just 56,000 rupees?

1723
01:23:10,829 --> 01:23:12,620
Logical! Good question.

1724
01:23:12,787 --> 01:23:15,079
I didn't have enough for it,
so I borrowed from him.

1725
01:23:16,245 --> 01:23:18,119
He took a loan of 1 lakh from me.

1726
01:23:18,120 --> 01:23:20,329
Ask him yourself,
did he repay it in 45 days?

1727
01:23:21,079 --> 01:23:22,162
Why are you looking at me?

1728
01:23:22,370 --> 01:23:24,411
You didn't just spend every 45 days...

1729
01:23:24,412 --> 01:23:26,495
you were spending every 45 minutes!

1730
01:23:27,162 --> 01:23:29,704
You don't see me as a lover.

1731
01:23:29,912 --> 01:23:31,745
You see me as Aladdin’s genie, don't you?

1732
01:23:31,995 --> 01:23:33,454
You're swiping me down to nothing.

1733
01:23:33,912 --> 01:23:37,287
Every single time you call,
I'm forced to get a new card.

1734
01:23:37,870 --> 01:23:39,745
Because I couldn't pay the two lakhs,

1735
01:23:39,787 --> 01:23:42,870
I took one more from a third party,
and it turned into three.

1736
01:23:42,912 --> 01:23:44,912
And since I couldn't
handle those three lakhs,

1737
01:23:44,954 --> 01:23:47,912
I borrowed another from a
fourth person... and it became four.

1738
01:23:48,079 --> 01:23:49,370
Four became five.

1739
01:23:49,412 --> 01:23:50,495
Five became six.

1740
01:23:50,537 --> 01:23:51,703
Six became seven.

1741
01:23:51,704 --> 01:23:53,287
Finally, it ended up at 7.5 lakhs in debt.

1742
01:23:53,662 --> 01:23:56,287
In the middle of all this chaos,
I was paying house rent,

1743
01:23:56,495 --> 01:23:57,995
my sister’s college fees,

1744
01:23:58,245 --> 01:24:02,245
and the EMI for the bike I used
to take you around every day,

1745
01:24:02,370 --> 01:24:03,954
plus, I had to pay for the petrol too!

1746
01:24:04,745 --> 01:24:05,787
I've had it!

1747
01:24:06,579 --> 01:24:09,412
But just to prove your character,

1748
01:24:09,454 --> 01:24:11,494
you made us run away
to Ooty to get married...

1749
01:24:11,495 --> 01:24:12,912
and you ruined everything!

1750
01:24:13,120 --> 01:24:17,037
The job and family a man needs
to live a good life are gone.

1751
01:24:18,120 --> 01:24:22,162
All I have left are the loans
and the love that destroyed me.

1752
01:24:22,787 --> 01:24:23,787
And as proof,

1753
01:24:24,037 --> 01:24:25,829
I have a 15 lakhs debt,

1754
01:24:26,120 --> 01:24:27,120
and you, standing right there!

1755
01:24:32,870 --> 01:24:35,662
Now tell me.
Will you sign on the L3,

1756
01:24:35,912 --> 01:24:38,620
or will you give the guarantee that you’ll
take responsibility for all these loans?

1757
01:24:40,245 --> 01:24:43,454
For the next four months,
no one is to call and disturb me.

1758
01:24:43,537 --> 01:24:45,787
If you need anything, ask her.

1759
01:24:45,870 --> 01:24:46,579
Okay?

1760
01:24:47,912 --> 01:24:50,662
I will pay off all your dues.
You can leave now.

1761
01:24:52,037 --> 01:24:52,954
Thank you very much, sir.

1762
01:24:55,037 --> 01:24:55,912
Hello, brother!

1763
01:24:56,329 --> 01:24:58,537
I was the one who said
I'd settle the loans.

1764
01:24:59,204 --> 01:25:00,578
Why are you thanking him?

1765
01:25:00,579 --> 01:25:04,120
Madam, usually, we’re the ones who have
to go collect the money from borrowers.

1766
01:25:04,287 --> 01:25:06,120
But look at him,
he borrowed the money himself,

1767
01:25:06,162 --> 01:25:08,120
and now he’s even doing
our job of collecting it!

1768
01:25:08,245 --> 01:25:09,453
Isn't he just great?

1769
01:25:09,454 --> 01:25:11,162
- Sir, thanks.
- Thank you, sir.

1770
01:25:12,704 --> 01:25:14,079
All the credits goes to...

1771
01:25:18,287 --> 01:25:20,204
- Hey, stop! Don't sign it!
- Don't sign it!

1772
01:25:37,454 --> 01:25:39,620
♪ When we love,
are we the Accused? ♪

1773
01:25:41,995 --> 01:25:43,329
♪ Are we the Accused? ♪

1774
01:25:44,870 --> 01:25:46,829
♪ When we love,
are we the Accused? ♪

1775
01:25:54,120 --> 01:25:56,911
♪ Love O love... Love O love... ♪

1776
01:25:56,912 --> 01:25:57,829
♪ Are we the Accused? ♪

1777
01:25:57,870 --> 01:26:01,454
♪ Love O love... Love O love... ♪

1778
01:26:01,495 --> 01:26:05,120
♪ 1v1, it’s a battle, no lie... ♪

1779
01:26:05,245 --> 01:26:08,911
♪ Betting on the fight,
as I’m ready to die... ♪

1780
01:26:08,912 --> 01:26:11,662
He can only go to Dubai if he
finishes his training properly.

1781
01:26:11,745 --> 01:26:13,036
What if you ruin his training?

1782
01:26:13,037 --> 01:26:16,745
Oh my God! He already left me
because he lost his job.

1783
01:26:16,787 --> 01:26:19,954
If I mess up his Dubai plans now,
he’ll kill me before he leaves.

1784
01:26:24,912 --> 01:26:27,912
Don't worry. From now on, everything
you've ever wanted will come true.

1785
01:26:28,037 --> 01:26:30,787
I visited the temple and
performed a prayer for you.

1786
01:26:32,620 --> 01:26:34,412
- Here.
- What is it?

1787
01:26:34,620 --> 01:26:36,120
L3! Sign it.

1788
01:26:36,912 --> 01:26:40,162
♪ Cut the cord, L3 takes the toll,
Wants a breakup, cuts me to the soul... ♪

1789
01:26:40,204 --> 01:26:43,954
♪ Face all scowled, he's full of hate,
Stabbing me sharp, sealing my fate... ♪

1790
01:26:44,370 --> 01:26:48,037
So, this group has been going around for
ages, boasting about how 'great' men are.

1791
01:26:48,204 --> 01:26:50,162
Tell me, what exactly
have they accomplished?

1792
01:26:50,204 --> 01:26:51,079
Make a list!

1793
01:26:51,120 --> 01:26:53,287
Come on, tell me,
what have these guys actually done?

1794
01:26:53,412 --> 01:26:54,412
First, entertainment.

1795
01:26:54,495 --> 01:26:55,537
Economy.

1796
01:26:55,579 --> 01:26:56,454
Emergency.

1797
01:26:56,495 --> 01:27:00,912
[list goes on]

1798
01:27:01,162 --> 01:27:02,912
- ...etcetera.
- ...etcetera.

1799
01:27:03,162 --> 01:27:05,245
Look at how long this list is getting.

1800
01:27:05,287 --> 01:27:08,412
So, for the people who were
there for us all this time...

1801
01:27:08,454 --> 01:27:10,662
we... hmm, we didn't
do a damn thing for them.

1802
01:27:10,704 --> 01:27:14,536
♪ When we love, are we the Accused?
You turned into Batista, left me bruised... ♪

1803
01:27:14,537 --> 01:27:18,078
♪ Cheap little games, a tangled mess,
Caught in the trap, under so much stress... ♪

1804
01:27:18,079 --> 01:27:21,786
♪ Am I just a dog?
You, the Minister man? ♪

1805
01:27:21,787 --> 01:27:25,537
♪ I accepted your test,
failed every plan... ♪

1806
01:27:25,579 --> 01:27:29,204
♪ When we love...
When we love, are we the Accused? ♪

1807
01:27:29,287 --> 01:27:32,954
♪ Trapped, my man,
trapped, my Cinderella fine... ♪

1808
01:27:32,995 --> 01:27:36,619
♪ When we love...
When we love, are we the Accused? ♪

1809
01:27:36,620 --> 01:27:40,287
♪ Trapped, my man,
trapped, my Cinderella fine... ♪

1810
01:27:42,912 --> 01:27:45,370
- Be safe.
- This is your mom’s scooter, right?

1811
01:27:45,412 --> 01:27:47,703
Does she go door-to-door
delivering water cans?

1812
01:27:47,704 --> 01:27:48,787
Why do you ask?

1813
01:27:48,829 --> 01:27:51,245
You’re the one who told me
this was a water-delivery bike, right?

1814
01:27:51,287 --> 01:27:52,954
So, is the whole family out there
delivering water cans now?

1815
01:27:53,245 --> 01:27:55,120
Bad fellow!
He remembers everything!

1816
01:28:13,329 --> 01:28:16,119
A man plans his life.

1817
01:28:16,120 --> 01:28:21,370
But you? You have pinned my life to
your bedroom door for the next 4 months?

1818
01:28:21,412 --> 01:28:24,204
You're lucky this is all I'm doing.
You deserve much more!

1819
01:28:39,537 --> 01:28:43,161
♪ He told my mom,
Now this Cinderella is in a bind... ♪

1820
01:28:43,162 --> 01:28:46,787
♪ Too much tension, too much stress,
Stabbing in my head, a total mess... ♪

1821
01:28:46,829 --> 01:28:50,412
♪ Wanted a life for us, a pair,
Now I’m just a slipper, stripped and bare... ♪

1822
01:28:50,454 --> 01:28:54,245
♪ Caught in the loan, like noodles I’m spun,
Twisted and crushed, the damage is done... ♪

1823
01:28:54,537 --> 01:28:55,662
Fine, I'll order.

1824
01:28:57,329 --> 01:28:59,912
I’m eating nothing but
curd rice and pickle.

1825
01:29:00,704 --> 01:29:03,579
And he... he demands mutton
biryani and tawa fish fry.

1826
01:29:05,037 --> 01:29:08,869
♪ When we love, are we the Accused?
You turned into Batista, left me bruised... ♪

1827
01:29:08,870 --> 01:29:12,495
♪ Cheap little games, a tangled mess,
Caught in the trap, under so much stress... ♪

1828
01:29:12,537 --> 01:29:15,953
♪ Am I just a dog?
You, the Minister man? ♪

1829
01:29:15,954 --> 01:29:20,204
♪ I accepted your test,
failed every plan... ♪

1830
01:29:21,329 --> 01:29:22,454
Where are you taking me?

1831
01:29:22,495 --> 01:29:25,204
I brought only 6 collection
agents that day.

1832
01:29:25,245 --> 01:29:26,494
I think I forgot two of them.

1833
01:29:26,495 --> 01:29:28,120
They are waiting downstairs.

1834
01:29:28,162 --> 01:29:30,579
Come and sign the papers
and get back to work.

1835
01:29:31,537 --> 01:29:32,537
Come soon!

1836
01:29:32,579 --> 01:29:34,829
I won't come! Just let me go!

1837
01:29:40,745 --> 01:29:44,495
♪ When we love...
When we love, are we the Accused? ♪

1838
01:29:44,537 --> 01:29:45,411
♪ I'm trapped... ♪

1839
01:29:45,412 --> 01:29:46,370
Tell me!

1840
01:29:46,412 --> 01:29:48,120
♪ I'm trapped...
Am I the Accused? ♪

1841
01:29:48,162 --> 01:29:51,870
♪ When we love...
When we love, are we the Accused? ♪

1842
01:29:51,912 --> 01:29:55,662
♪ Trapped, my man,
trapped, my Cinderella fine... ♪

1843
01:29:56,454 --> 01:29:57,745
♪ Are we the Accused? ♪

1844
01:29:58,329 --> 01:29:59,537
♪ Are we the Accused? ♪

1845
01:29:59,995 --> 01:30:01,120
♪ Are we really the Accused? ♪

1846
01:30:01,162 --> 01:30:03,079
<i>You have money to buy makeup,
but you can't pay your EMI?</i>

1847
01:30:03,120 --> 01:30:04,329
<i>Will you pay the EMI now or not?</i>

1848
01:30:04,370 --> 01:30:05,994
<i>- You were able to sign the surety.
- I'll come back again!</i>

1849
01:30:05,995 --> 01:30:07,370
<i>- You can't pay back as promised?
- If I don't get the money...</i>

1850
01:30:09,662 --> 01:30:10,662
How much is this, sir?

1851
01:30:10,704 --> 01:30:12,412
Ma'am, this is 65,000 rupees.

1852
01:30:12,454 --> 01:30:13,204
It's okay.

1853
01:30:13,537 --> 01:30:15,662
The price is higher now than
when I first bought it.

1854
01:30:15,870 --> 01:30:17,079
Ma'am, this is an imported item.

1855
01:30:17,204 --> 01:30:18,369
You won't get it that easily.

1856
01:30:18,370 --> 01:30:19,744
A customer ordered one yesterday.

1857
01:30:19,745 --> 01:30:21,204
Luckily, you got it today.

1858
01:30:23,079 --> 01:30:26,370
Sir, I bought this very piece
from you not long ago.

1859
01:30:26,412 --> 01:30:28,036
Same design, same piece.

1860
01:30:28,037 --> 01:30:29,579
I haven't even used it much.

1861
01:30:29,829 --> 01:30:33,412
If you take it back, could you
give me 40,000 rupees for it?

1862
01:30:33,454 --> 01:30:35,912
I’m in an emergency right now.
I’ll buy it back later.

1863
01:30:35,954 --> 01:30:38,620
Sorry, ma'am. Once a sale is final,
we do not accept returns.

1864
01:30:38,662 --> 01:30:42,994
Sir, didn't you just say this was
a high-demand, imported item?

1865
01:30:42,995 --> 01:30:44,995
That’s just sales talk.

1866
01:30:45,037 --> 01:30:46,204
It’s up to you to be careful what you buy.

1867
01:30:46,745 --> 01:30:48,453
We never forced you to take it, did we?

1868
01:30:48,454 --> 01:30:49,703
Are you kidding me?

1869
01:30:49,704 --> 01:30:52,704
I paid 56,000 for this because
I trusted your word!

1870
01:30:52,870 --> 01:30:54,120
How can you say you
won't take it back now?

1871
01:30:54,162 --> 01:30:55,662
We don’t accept returns.

1872
01:30:55,954 --> 01:30:58,912
But since you’re insisting, I’ll take it
back for 2,000 as an exchange.

1873
01:30:58,954 --> 01:31:00,494
And buy anything else you like.

1874
01:31:00,495 --> 01:31:01,661
Do I look like a fool to you?

1875
01:31:01,662 --> 01:31:03,912
You’re going to take my
56,000 rupees item for 2,000,

1876
01:31:03,954 --> 01:31:06,454
and then turn around and
sell it for 65,000 again?

1877
01:31:06,495 --> 01:31:07,620
And you expect me to
just walk away with that?

1878
01:31:07,662 --> 01:31:08,954
Hey! Quiet.

1879
01:31:09,412 --> 01:31:10,662
Everyone is looking at us.

1880
01:31:10,704 --> 01:31:11,620
Let them look at us.

1881
01:31:11,662 --> 01:31:13,412
There should be a value for money, right?

1882
01:31:13,454 --> 01:31:14,328
Waste fellows!

1883
01:31:14,329 --> 01:31:17,454
I would've cleared 3 EMIs.
I can't even clear one now.

1884
01:31:17,495 --> 01:31:18,995
What can we do
if she can't clear her EMIs?

1885
01:31:19,037 --> 01:31:20,412
What are you looking at?

1886
01:31:20,495 --> 01:31:22,369
- How much are you planning to spend?
- 30,000 rupees.

1887
01:31:22,370 --> 01:31:25,662
If you have 30,000 to spend, go to
Lalitha jewellery and buy some gold.

1888
01:31:25,704 --> 01:31:26,912
It will be useful in the future.

1889
01:31:27,162 --> 01:31:29,912
Look, if you want something
like this, just head to Pondy Bazaar.

1890
01:31:29,954 --> 01:31:31,453
You’ll find them
selling it for 300 rupees.

1891
01:31:31,454 --> 01:31:34,079
Buy it, use it, and throw it in the
trash when you're done.

1892
01:31:34,620 --> 01:31:37,912
Oh no! Without realizing this,
I've already committed to four people.

1893
01:31:42,079 --> 01:31:43,620
- What are you doing here?
- Oh no, him?

1894
01:31:44,245 --> 01:31:46,953
- I came to see the new collections.
- Did you see it?

1895
01:31:46,954 --> 01:31:47,662
I saw it.

1896
01:31:47,704 --> 01:31:49,245
I saw what you saw.

1897
01:31:49,579 --> 01:31:50,662
That's nothing...

1898
01:31:50,995 --> 01:31:52,662
They’ve got all these
old collections sitting there.

1899
01:31:52,745 --> 01:31:55,245
I went over and threatened them,
told them they’d better buy the new ones.

1900
01:31:55,370 --> 01:31:56,579
Oh!

1901
01:31:56,829 --> 01:31:58,161
- Shall we go?
- Keep threatening.

1902
01:31:58,162 --> 01:31:59,245
Keep rolling your lies as well.

1903
01:32:04,037 --> 01:32:08,120
Bro, I need 20,000 urgently.

1904
01:32:08,162 --> 01:32:11,370
Please, I’ll return it as soon
as my bonus arrives next month.

1905
01:32:11,829 --> 01:32:14,037
Why the 'please'?
You just need 20,000, right?

1906
01:32:16,257 --> 01:32:16,715
Here.

1907
01:32:17,537 --> 01:32:18,245
Thanks, bro.

1908
01:32:19,120 --> 01:32:21,078
Avantika, tomorrow
is your birthday, right?

1909
01:32:21,079 --> 01:32:21,829
Yeah, bro.

1910
01:32:21,870 --> 01:32:24,162
In ECR, my friend's guest house is free.

1911
01:32:24,245 --> 01:32:25,369
Shall we party there?

1912
01:32:25,370 --> 01:32:26,662
Just the two of us.

1913
01:32:35,120 --> 01:32:37,454
All these years, I’ve been
calling you 'brother', haven't I?

1914
01:32:38,287 --> 01:32:38,912
Yuck!

1915
01:32:40,829 --> 01:32:42,787
But I never called you as sister.

1916
01:32:44,037 --> 01:32:44,912
Hey, Avantika!

1917
01:32:45,162 --> 01:32:47,620
If 20,000 doesn't cut it,
let's sit down and cut a deal.

1918
01:32:51,954 --> 01:32:54,870
Even Raghu, who borrowed lakhs for me,

1919
01:32:55,495 --> 01:32:57,745
never once crossed the line
with me like this.

1920
01:32:59,329 --> 01:33:01,412
For just 20,000 rupees,

1921
01:33:03,162 --> 01:33:04,829
without a second thought,

1922
01:33:04,954 --> 01:33:07,870
he’s asking a woman who called
him 'brother' to come sleep with him.

1923
01:33:17,704 --> 01:33:18,495
[car unlocked]

1924
01:33:21,079 --> 01:33:22,329
[car unlocking]

1925
01:33:24,329 --> 01:33:26,287
- Who is that?
- Hey, get down from my car!

1926
01:33:31,495 --> 01:33:33,329
Hey, can't you hear me? Get off!

1927
01:33:36,329 --> 01:33:37,370
What does 'bro' mean?

1928
01:33:40,245 --> 01:33:41,370
She's cried for help already?

1929
01:33:45,204 --> 01:33:46,162
I'm talking to you!

1930
01:33:46,620 --> 01:33:47,619
What does 'bro' mean?

1931
01:33:47,620 --> 01:33:48,829
Hey, get down!

1932
01:34:26,245 --> 01:34:27,204
Tell me! What does 'bro' mean?

1933
01:35:21,870 --> 01:35:23,870
Bro! Bro!
Sorry, bro! Sorry, bro!

1934
01:35:24,204 --> 01:35:24,995
I'm really sorry, bro!

1935
01:35:25,245 --> 01:35:27,579
So, is 'brother' only
a title you use for men?

1936
01:35:27,870 --> 01:35:29,620
Just because you sit
in a position of power,

1937
01:35:29,745 --> 01:35:31,495
does that mean you stop
seeing women as sisters?

1938
01:35:31,579 --> 01:35:32,870
Bro! Bro!
I will see, bro.

1939
01:35:32,954 --> 01:35:35,829
I swear I will see, bro.
Look at me now!

1940
01:35:35,912 --> 01:35:37,037
I'm extremely sorry sisters!

1941
01:35:37,079 --> 01:35:38,620
He called us sisters?

1942
01:35:38,662 --> 01:35:40,787
From now on,
I will call all of them as sister, bro!

1943
01:35:43,079 --> 01:35:44,870
- Who told him?
- I did.

1944
01:35:52,912 --> 01:35:54,912
[dances in joy]

1945
01:36:03,204 --> 01:36:05,995
- Hey, baby! Happy birthday!
- Thank you, Mom!

1946
01:36:20,079 --> 01:36:21,079
Be happy always!

1947
01:36:41,745 --> 01:36:43,454
Everyone else is wishing me,

1948
01:36:43,954 --> 01:36:45,829
but this guy... he wants
a treat but not wishing me.

1949
01:36:45,912 --> 01:36:46,829
I just want to...

1950
01:36:53,079 --> 01:36:53,787
Here.

1951
01:36:53,995 --> 01:36:55,579
Pay for the party.

1952
01:36:56,037 --> 01:36:58,454
You just told me you were broke, so how
exactly are you affording a party this big?

1953
01:36:58,620 --> 01:36:59,412
It's an app.

1954
01:36:59,620 --> 01:37:00,079
Huh?

1955
01:37:00,537 --> 01:37:01,370
Loan app.

1956
01:37:03,204 --> 01:37:04,495
I'll finalize it for you today then.

1957
01:37:04,912 --> 01:37:07,037
- Hi!
- Hi, guys!

1958
01:37:09,245 --> 01:37:11,036
How long are we supposed to wait?

1959
01:37:11,037 --> 01:37:12,329
We haven't eaten a thing,
just waiting for you.

1960
01:37:12,412 --> 01:37:13,370
Sorry!

1961
01:37:13,495 --> 01:37:14,245
Let's have food.

1962
01:37:14,704 --> 01:37:17,120
- Has everyone ordered?
- Hmm, yeah!

1963
01:37:18,787 --> 01:37:20,454
Excuse me.
How much do you weigh?

1964
01:37:20,495 --> 01:37:21,120
What?!

1965
01:37:21,162 --> 01:37:22,620
What are you doing?

1966
01:37:22,662 --> 01:37:25,204
I'm just asking. Tell me.

1967
01:37:27,329 --> 01:37:28,079
Fifty five.

1968
01:37:28,120 --> 01:37:31,954
At 55kg, your body BMI can’t handle
more than 500g of food.

1969
01:37:32,162 --> 01:37:33,912
You’ve gone ahead and ordered
three kilos of food for yourself.

1970
01:37:33,954 --> 01:37:35,662
Will you do this if it were your money?

1971
01:37:38,620 --> 01:37:39,370
Excuse me.

1972
01:37:39,787 --> 01:37:42,162
Tell me, how much does it cost you to buy
groceries for your own home for a week?

1973
01:37:42,454 --> 01:37:44,620
It's 1500 to 2000 rupees per week.

1974
01:37:44,662 --> 01:37:46,245
1500 to 2000 rupees.

1975
01:37:46,495 --> 01:37:49,370
A whole family eats for a week
on 1,500 to 2,000 rupees.

1976
01:37:49,454 --> 01:37:51,495
And here you are, ordering more
than that for a single meal?

1977
01:37:52,454 --> 01:37:54,329
Just because it's not your money, right?

1978
01:37:54,745 --> 01:37:56,245
What is this, Avantika?

1979
01:37:56,579 --> 01:37:58,287
Did you invite me here
just to humiliate me?

1980
01:37:59,870 --> 01:38:01,704
Raghu, apologize to her now!

1981
01:38:03,579 --> 01:38:04,829
Sorry.
Sorry, guys.

1982
01:38:05,079 --> 01:38:06,162
Sorry. Please eat.

1983
01:38:06,870 --> 01:38:10,079
Whatever you've ordered,
eat without leaving any leftovers.

1984
01:38:10,245 --> 01:38:11,912
I will pay your bill myself.

1985
01:38:12,204 --> 01:38:16,162
If you leave any leftovers,
pay your own bills.

1986
01:38:17,162 --> 01:38:18,245
Hey! What's up?

1987
01:38:18,579 --> 01:38:21,037
Do you think I can't afford
to pay for the food I've eaten?

1988
01:38:21,245 --> 01:38:23,370
Pay! If you can afford it, then pay!

1989
01:38:23,412 --> 01:38:24,370
Who is stopping you?

1990
01:38:24,454 --> 01:38:26,954
I will pay for the food
you actually taste.

1991
01:38:27,120 --> 01:38:29,620
I will not pay for the food you waste.

1992
01:38:29,662 --> 01:38:31,329
Hey! Keep quiet.

1993
01:38:31,370 --> 01:38:32,204
What's this, Avantika?

1994
01:38:32,245 --> 01:38:34,870
He keeps talking,
and you’re just watching?

1995
01:38:34,912 --> 01:38:36,286
How would she even ask, buddy?

1996
01:38:36,287 --> 01:38:38,579
After all, her love is the
greatest love in the world!

1997
01:38:38,662 --> 01:38:40,954
Let her celebrate her birthday
with the greatest lover in the world.

1998
01:38:40,995 --> 01:38:41,912
Let’s go!

1999
01:38:41,995 --> 01:38:44,328
Hey! Why are you making an issue now?

2000
01:38:44,329 --> 01:38:45,995
Who? Are we making an issue?

2001
01:38:46,204 --> 01:38:47,037
Or is it him?

2002
01:38:47,079 --> 01:38:49,370
You can stay and eat with them.
We'll go.

2003
01:38:49,412 --> 01:38:50,287
Hey, come on, let's go.

2004
01:38:52,454 --> 01:38:53,162
Hey!

2005
01:38:53,745 --> 01:38:56,745
You claimed you could afford all this,
but now you're leaving without paying?

2006
01:38:57,204 --> 01:39:00,370
If anyone even thinks about forcing
a "party treat" on me again,

2007
01:39:00,454 --> 01:39:01,829
I’ll tear your face off, mark my words!

2008
01:39:01,912 --> 01:39:03,704
Come on, let's go!
Let's head to a different party.

2009
01:39:03,912 --> 01:39:05,079
What is your problem?

2010
01:39:05,162 --> 01:39:06,287
Why are you behaving like this?

2011
01:39:06,370 --> 01:39:07,579
It's my birthday today!

2012
01:39:07,704 --> 01:39:08,829
You didn't even wish me,

2013
01:39:09,037 --> 01:39:11,204
and you ended up humiliating
the friends who came to wish me?

2014
01:39:11,829 --> 01:39:13,120
Are you happy now?

2015
01:39:13,870 --> 01:39:15,079
Who are you calling friends?

2016
01:39:15,120 --> 01:39:17,619
How many people did you ask for money
to pay off your loan two days ago?

2017
01:39:17,620 --> 01:39:19,079
Did anyone help you?

2018
01:39:19,954 --> 01:39:21,620
The moment you invited them to a treat

2019
01:39:21,662 --> 01:39:23,412
if they had asked, "You're already
struggling without money,

2020
01:39:23,454 --> 01:39:25,329
why spend it on this now?",

2021
01:39:25,579 --> 01:39:26,745
they would be true friends.

2022
01:39:26,870 --> 01:39:29,579
Look. You can accept anything,

2023
01:39:29,954 --> 01:39:32,829
but wasting food is the
worst thing in the world.

2024
01:39:33,620 --> 01:39:35,745
Why? Is food not being wasted right now?

2025
01:39:35,912 --> 01:39:36,745
Wait a minute.

2026
01:39:42,495 --> 01:39:44,662
If anyone drinks for
the next one hour,

2027
01:39:44,995 --> 01:39:45,911
I will kill you!

2028
01:39:45,912 --> 01:39:46,911
- Bro!
- Yes, sir?

2029
01:39:46,912 --> 01:39:48,995
Whatever loss incurs in your
business in the next one hour,

2030
01:39:49,037 --> 01:39:49,912
put it on her tab.

2031
01:39:49,954 --> 01:39:51,162
- Okay?
- Okay, sir.

2032
01:39:57,704 --> 01:39:59,704
Happy birthday, sister!

2033
01:40:00,370 --> 01:40:01,329
Thank you!

2034
01:40:08,079 --> 01:40:09,745
All this... for me?

2035
01:40:10,370 --> 01:40:11,412
For the children.

2036
01:40:28,120 --> 01:40:30,204
It fell on the table, leave it aside.

2037
01:40:30,454 --> 01:40:31,829
I'll give you another piece.

2038
01:40:31,870 --> 01:40:32,954
No need, sister.

2039
01:40:33,329 --> 01:40:35,995
I've had stale food itself, sister.

2040
01:40:36,037 --> 01:40:39,912
It just fell on the table,
I will clean it and eat it.

2041
01:40:40,287 --> 01:40:43,162
My parents left me in an orphanage because

2042
01:40:43,204 --> 01:40:45,912
they didn't even have the
money to provide this food.

2043
01:40:46,037 --> 01:40:49,870
I know how much you must
have spent to buy me this food,

2044
01:40:50,370 --> 01:40:54,787
and I understand how hard you
had to work to earn that money, sister.

2045
01:41:03,829 --> 01:41:05,037
Hmm... this is so tasty.

2046
01:41:07,579 --> 01:41:08,287
Hi.

2047
01:41:17,995 --> 01:41:19,037
Why didn't you eat?

2048
01:41:20,454 --> 01:41:22,204
What did I do wrong, Merlin?

2049
01:41:23,079 --> 01:41:26,579
If friends are more important to you,
you should have sent Raghu away that day.

2050
01:41:26,787 --> 01:41:28,829
But you insulted your friends

2051
01:41:28,912 --> 01:41:31,120
and still stayed with Raghu,
the very person who insulted you.

2052
01:41:31,412 --> 01:41:34,245
Raghuvaran has become more
important to you than us, hasn't he?

2053
01:41:34,412 --> 01:41:35,787
He is important, Merlin.

2054
01:41:35,995 --> 01:41:40,579
Every birthday, I go to the temple
to seek God’s blessings.

2055
01:41:40,787 --> 01:41:42,079
But for this birthday...

2056
01:41:42,787 --> 01:41:45,245
he brought God
to come and wish me.

2057
01:41:45,745 --> 01:41:47,662
He is important to me, Merlin.

2058
01:41:47,954 --> 01:41:49,578
Then why are you worried about them?

2059
01:41:49,579 --> 01:41:52,453
Won't it be difficult if my
friends suddenly stop talking to me?

2060
01:41:52,454 --> 01:41:54,619
You feel bad that your
friends have left you,

2061
01:41:54,620 --> 01:41:58,537
but have you ever felt that it was because
of you that everyone who loved him left him?

2062
01:41:58,829 --> 01:42:00,037
That's why, Merlin...

2063
01:42:01,162 --> 01:42:05,120
Like he asked, I pick him up
and drop him off daily,

2064
01:42:05,579 --> 01:42:07,620
and I handle his debts too.

2065
01:42:07,662 --> 01:42:11,120
Avi, do you think the loans
are his biggest issues?

2066
01:42:11,162 --> 01:42:12,287
His problem is something else entirely.

2067
01:42:12,329 --> 01:42:13,787
Shall I ask you something simple?

2068
01:42:14,204 --> 01:42:15,579
What's his favourite food?

2069
01:42:15,620 --> 01:42:18,537
- I don't know.
- Fine. What's his favourite shirt brand?

2070
01:42:19,537 --> 01:42:20,120
I don't know.

2071
01:42:20,162 --> 01:42:22,829
At least, what is his favourite
place in Chennai?

2072
01:42:22,870 --> 01:42:23,912
I don't know, Merlin.

2073
01:42:24,120 --> 01:42:26,079
How many restaurants
have you visited with him?

2074
01:42:26,412 --> 01:42:27,954
How much shopping would
you have done with him?

2075
01:42:28,162 --> 01:42:29,537
Where all have you travelled together?

2076
01:42:30,287 --> 01:42:32,079
But you don't know what he likes.

2077
01:42:32,204 --> 01:42:33,120
Not only you,

2078
01:42:33,495 --> 01:42:36,662
but no girl has ever
entered a man's world.

2079
01:42:37,245 --> 01:42:39,370
You only think about
how much you want him,

2080
01:42:39,412 --> 01:42:41,245
but you never stop to think
about what he actually wants.

2081
01:42:42,579 --> 01:42:45,620
Education and career are a girl's rights,

2082
01:42:45,954 --> 01:42:47,537
but for boys, they are responsibilities.

2083
01:42:49,120 --> 01:42:51,120
Rights are something we demand and take.

2084
01:42:51,662 --> 01:42:54,203
Responsibilities are what are forced
upon them without them even asking.

2085
01:42:54,204 --> 01:42:57,287
Until you enter his world and
seek out what he actually needs,

2086
01:42:57,454 --> 01:42:59,329
you will never be able to understand him.

2087
01:43:03,370 --> 01:43:05,787
Do you know why
I'm telling you all of this?

2088
01:43:06,495 --> 01:43:12,412
I am someone who can see both
a man's world and a woman's world equally.

2089
01:43:12,995 --> 01:43:14,954
Think about what I said, Avi.

2090
01:43:25,537 --> 01:43:28,161
♪ I'm not sure if it’s right or wrong... ♪

2091
01:43:28,162 --> 01:43:30,453
♪ Is this the end? I don't understand... ♪

2092
01:43:30,454 --> 01:43:34,204
♪ I’m longing for you... ♪

2093
01:43:35,745 --> 01:43:38,369
♪ Can I be yours? Once more please? ♪

2094
01:43:38,370 --> 01:43:40,537
♪ I am ready to break
once more for you... ♪

2095
01:43:40,579 --> 01:43:44,162
♪ I’ll carry the weight
myself from now on... ♪

2096
01:43:44,204 --> 01:43:49,079
♪ You came looking for me,
why should you leave weeping now? ♪

2097
01:43:49,204 --> 01:43:54,162
♪ Let's get lost in the
sweetness of the pain... ♪

2098
01:43:54,329 --> 01:43:59,079
♪ The love you gave
is still in my ears... ♪

2099
01:43:59,245 --> 01:44:04,079
♪ The source of my love
flows through my eyes... ♪

2100
01:44:04,454 --> 01:44:09,787
♪ Who am I?
Really, who am I? ♪

2101
01:44:10,079 --> 01:44:14,287
♪ In your world,
Who am I? ♪

2102
01:44:14,537 --> 01:44:19,912
♪ Who am I?
Really, who am I? ♪

2103
01:44:20,204 --> 01:44:23,912
♪ In your world,
Who am I? ♪

2104
01:44:23,954 --> 01:44:25,954
<i>Can you GPay me 2000? It's urgent.</i>

2105
01:44:25,995 --> 01:44:27,079
Hmm, I'll send.

2106
01:44:28,912 --> 01:44:30,745
- Okay wait, I'll send.
- <i>Thank you.</i>

2107
01:44:32,162 --> 01:44:33,495
- Avantika, right?
- Hmm.

2108
01:44:46,829 --> 01:44:49,120
♪ I long to see you... ♪

2109
01:44:49,287 --> 01:44:51,829
♪ I fade away waiting every day... ♪

2110
01:44:51,870 --> 01:44:54,829
♪ Come, call me just once more... ♪

2111
01:44:56,912 --> 01:44:59,370
♪ You are my desire that never dies... ♪

2112
01:44:59,495 --> 01:45:01,954
♪ Even apart, you are my life... ♪

2113
01:45:01,995 --> 01:45:04,912
♪ Come, let’s be one,
just once more... ♪

2114
01:45:05,120 --> 01:45:09,994
♪ You came looking for me,
why should you leave weeping now? ♪

2115
01:45:09,995 --> 01:45:12,662
♪ Let's get lost in the
sweetness of the pain... ♪

2116
01:45:12,704 --> 01:45:15,369
Madam has applied for a credit card,
and I am here for the verification.

2117
01:45:15,370 --> 01:45:17,161
My daughter?
Applied for a credit card?!

2118
01:45:17,162 --> 01:45:19,037
Ma'am has applied for a personal loan.

2119
01:45:19,120 --> 01:45:22,286
Please cancel the verification,
she doesn't need any credit card anymore.

2120
01:45:22,287 --> 01:45:24,120
We don't need any loan, sir. Go!

2121
01:45:25,245 --> 01:45:29,329
♪ Who am I?
Really, who am I? ♪

2122
01:45:29,370 --> 01:45:30,329
Hello, brother.

2123
01:45:30,495 --> 01:45:31,120
Huh?

2124
01:45:32,204 --> 01:45:35,037
Dad and I are coming to Chennai
to pay the exam fees tomorrow.

2125
01:45:35,079 --> 01:45:36,744
I want to see you.

2126
01:45:36,745 --> 01:45:38,870
If possible, can you please come
to the bus stand tomorrow?

2127
01:45:38,912 --> 01:45:39,787
Okay.

2128
01:45:41,079 --> 01:45:44,453
♪ In your world,
Who am I? ♪

2129
01:45:44,454 --> 01:45:46,120
Bro, my salary will be
credited only at 12 o'clock.

2130
01:45:46,162 --> 01:45:47,662
What can I do if you come so early?

2131
01:45:47,704 --> 01:45:50,412
What should I do, Madam? It's the same
story every month. But you never pay.

2132
01:45:50,454 --> 01:45:52,829
I've made up my mind, Madam.
This time I won't leave until I get it.

2133
01:45:52,870 --> 01:45:54,953
Yes, madam.
We will get it and leave.

2134
01:45:54,954 --> 01:45:57,870
Calculate the EMI for 2 months.
I will come and pay it.

2135
01:45:57,995 --> 01:45:59,079
Thank you very much, madam.

2136
01:46:04,204 --> 01:46:05,120
Why?

2137
01:46:05,495 --> 01:46:08,079
Our Vice President came from Mumbai,

2138
01:46:08,120 --> 01:46:10,329
and the first thing
she asked for was you.

2139
01:46:10,370 --> 01:46:13,370
We think your on-site project
has been approved!

2140
01:46:13,412 --> 01:46:15,079
Congrats!

2141
01:46:16,537 --> 01:46:17,704
Thank you!

2142
01:46:18,287 --> 01:46:19,870
Hey, where is the treat?

2143
01:46:20,079 --> 01:46:22,079
For what? For him to come and insult us?

2144
01:46:22,120 --> 01:46:23,079
Sit down, man.

2145
01:46:23,245 --> 01:46:24,454
Yeah, I'll sit down.

2146
01:46:25,995 --> 01:46:27,370
Thank you, guys!

2147
01:46:27,579 --> 01:46:29,662
- I will go and meet her first. Hmm?
- Hmm.

2148
01:46:29,704 --> 01:46:31,579
What next? Her chair's ours!

2149
01:46:32,204 --> 01:46:33,870
What is this, Ma'am?
Why have you fired me?

2150
01:46:33,954 --> 01:46:35,620
Do you know what you have done?

2151
01:46:35,787 --> 01:46:37,828
We told you to send
a quotation with lower rates

2152
01:46:37,829 --> 01:46:40,079
to a new client without
the regular client's knowledge,

2153
01:46:40,162 --> 01:46:42,203
but you had sent it to them itself.

2154
01:46:42,204 --> 01:46:44,078
And now they are
accusing us of cheating

2155
01:46:44,079 --> 01:46:46,495
and threatening to stop
doing business with us.

2156
01:46:46,537 --> 01:46:48,662
No he is asking for
the balance to be settled.

2157
01:46:48,704 --> 01:46:50,995
Do you have any idea
how much the settlement amount is?

2158
01:46:51,120 --> 01:46:52,369
72 crores!

2159
01:46:52,370 --> 01:46:53,537
How do we settle them now?

2160
01:46:53,579 --> 01:46:55,870
Just be happy that we stopped
at just firing you.

2161
01:46:56,079 --> 01:46:58,370
In fairness, I should be taking
legal action against you.

2162
01:46:58,620 --> 01:47:01,079
It's better that you start
looking for openings elsewhere.

2163
01:47:05,370 --> 01:47:06,912
We have freezed your accounts.

2164
01:47:06,954 --> 01:47:09,412
It won't be cleared until
this problem is solved.

2165
01:47:09,954 --> 01:47:11,370
There’s no chance of that
happening anyway.

2166
01:47:11,620 --> 01:47:13,620
She promised to pay
two months' EMI together.

2167
01:47:13,787 --> 01:47:14,995
She just came and told us.

2168
01:47:15,120 --> 01:47:17,245
She said she will pay once
her salary is credited, sir.

2169
01:47:18,454 --> 01:47:19,829
How is it possible?

2170
01:47:24,537 --> 01:47:27,703
Oh no, the way he’s coming toward us,
he’s definitely going to make a scene.

2171
01:47:27,704 --> 01:47:30,412
So, Avantika, I heard that you said
you'd pay double EMI?

2172
01:47:30,454 --> 01:47:32,162
Have you been promoted or something?

2173
01:47:32,787 --> 01:47:34,829
Oh, so they did.

2174
01:47:38,412 --> 01:47:40,954
Sonamutha! Did you lose your job?

2175
01:47:42,912 --> 01:47:45,245
But look at the appointment order I got.

2176
01:47:45,287 --> 01:47:46,412
That too, in Dubai.

2177
01:47:46,579 --> 01:47:48,412
My placement has been confirmed!

2178
01:47:52,370 --> 01:47:53,454
- Take it.
- Thank you, sir.

2179
01:47:53,495 --> 01:47:54,370
- Take it.
- What's he doing?

2180
01:47:54,412 --> 01:47:55,329
- Thank you, sir.
- Take it.

2181
01:47:55,370 --> 01:47:56,286
I'm very happy.

2182
01:47:56,287 --> 01:47:58,870
What's up, sir? You're giving out
chocolates because you got a new job?

2183
01:47:58,912 --> 01:48:00,912
I'm not giving them out
because I got a job.

2184
01:48:01,370 --> 01:48:03,954
I'm doing it because she lost hers.

2185
01:48:04,454 --> 01:48:05,995
Why, sir?

2186
01:48:06,037 --> 01:48:07,995
She didn't pay the EMI even
when she had a job.

2187
01:48:08,120 --> 01:48:10,495
Now that she's lost it,
how is she supposed to pay?

2188
01:48:10,704 --> 01:48:11,744
She will give L3.

2189
01:48:11,745 --> 01:48:12,412
Raghu!

2190
01:48:12,454 --> 01:48:14,329
She is already feeling terrible
about losing her job,

2191
01:48:14,412 --> 01:48:16,287
it’s really wrong to talk
like that right now.

2192
01:48:16,329 --> 01:48:17,829
I lost my job because of her.

2193
01:48:17,870 --> 01:48:20,037
Did anyone advise her like this?

2194
01:48:20,454 --> 01:48:22,703
You said you can be Raghuvaran
for four months?

2195
01:48:22,704 --> 01:48:24,662
Well, you can never be Raghuvaran.

2196
01:48:25,162 --> 01:48:26,870
Come tomorrow and hand over the L3.

2197
01:48:37,995 --> 01:48:40,454
You’re asking for 15 lakhs
for a property worth 2 crores?

2198
01:48:40,662 --> 01:48:43,537
I’ve gotten myself into trouble with
credit card bills and various app loans.

2199
01:48:43,579 --> 01:48:44,829
I have to clear it all.

2200
01:48:44,870 --> 01:48:47,370
I will take the document back once
I get the settlement from my office.

2201
01:48:47,870 --> 01:48:49,829
Alright, I'll verify everything and
get back to you in a couple of days.

2202
01:48:49,870 --> 01:48:51,370
- Thank God, he forgot me.
- Hey, Tattoo!

2203
01:48:51,537 --> 01:48:53,954
I sent someone to bring you,
and now you brought someone?

2204
01:48:54,454 --> 01:48:56,245
- When are you planning to settle?
- Settu!

2205
01:48:56,287 --> 01:48:58,954
My 2 lakhs are also part of that 15 lakhs.

2206
01:48:58,995 --> 01:49:01,744
They have brought me here by
compromising that they will give it to me.

2207
01:49:01,745 --> 01:49:03,412
Verify it soon.

2208
01:49:03,495 --> 01:49:06,454
Perhaps he was my wife in a past life,
the very sight of him terrifies me.

2209
01:49:06,579 --> 01:49:08,453
Here, ask the auditor to verify this.

2210
01:49:08,454 --> 01:49:09,287
Okay, sir.

2211
01:49:12,245 --> 01:49:13,036
- Ma'am!
- Hmm?

2212
01:49:13,037 --> 01:49:14,787
Sir wants you to verify this document.

2213
01:49:14,912 --> 01:49:15,412
Okay.

2214
01:49:21,704 --> 01:49:24,829
What kind of mess did she get into that
she had to mortgage the house papers?

2215
01:49:28,120 --> 01:49:29,204
- Hello!
- Tell me, ma'am.

2216
01:49:29,245 --> 01:49:30,954
Kishore!
Is everything okay with Avantika?

2217
01:49:30,995 --> 01:49:32,954
Ma'am, don't you know anything?

2218
01:49:32,995 --> 01:49:35,454
Your daughter has been in love
with a guy named Raghu.

2219
01:49:52,954 --> 01:49:53,620
Here, take this.

2220
01:49:55,204 --> 01:49:57,079
Why did you ask me
to come alone to give this?

2221
01:49:57,454 --> 01:49:59,787
Dad is right there,
come and talk to him.

2222
01:50:03,329 --> 01:50:05,495
- No, I am not coming.
- Why?

2223
01:50:05,537 --> 01:50:06,829
I’m the one in debt.

2224
01:50:06,870 --> 01:50:09,995
Dad left me because he thought I wouldn't
be able to get you married, right?

2225
01:50:10,120 --> 01:50:11,412
Well, I have a job now.

2226
01:50:11,662 --> 01:50:15,079
Once I've paid off all my debts and
gotten you married off, then I'll talk.

2227
01:50:15,329 --> 01:50:16,120
Okay.

2228
01:50:16,870 --> 01:50:19,537
So, what have you decided
regarding Avantika?

2229
01:50:20,537 --> 01:50:21,745
[bus honking]
Hey, Kavitha!

2230
01:50:22,370 --> 01:50:24,370
It's time for the bus, you should leave.

2231
01:50:28,745 --> 01:50:30,620
- Couldn't you at least talk to him?
- Get on the bus.

2232
01:50:31,787 --> 01:50:32,412
[lady slaps]

2233
01:50:39,329 --> 01:50:41,245
Why should my daughter
have to pay off your debt?

2234
01:50:43,745 --> 01:50:45,161
Don't speak without knowing the facts.

2235
01:50:45,162 --> 01:50:46,745
I know exactly what's going on,
that's why I'm talking.

2236
01:50:46,787 --> 01:50:48,995
If you took the loan, pay it off
with your own assets.

2237
01:50:49,037 --> 01:50:51,829
Why are you asking her to use my property
and get my daughter to pay it off, huh?

2238
01:50:52,954 --> 01:50:53,704
Oh no, brother...

2239
01:50:53,870 --> 01:50:56,079
Why are you staring over there?
Look at my face and speak to me.

2240
01:50:56,120 --> 01:50:59,370
You’ve been paying your EMIs with my
daughter’s salary for the past 3 months.

2241
01:50:59,579 --> 01:51:01,454
You've been eating off her money.

2242
01:51:01,537 --> 01:51:04,537
You’ve made a grown-up girl run around
day and night without any regard.

2243
01:51:04,787 --> 01:51:08,079
In the name of love,
you've ruined my daughter's life.

2244
01:51:08,204 --> 01:51:09,662
Aren't you ashamed of yourself?

2245
01:51:11,787 --> 01:51:15,745
My daughter... would think twice
even before telling me a lie.

2246
01:51:15,870 --> 01:51:17,412
You’ve turned her into
a debtor like yourself

2247
01:51:17,454 --> 01:51:19,454
and made her steal my property deeds.

2248
01:51:21,537 --> 01:51:23,245
My daughter doesn't have
anyone other than me.

2249
01:51:23,287 --> 01:51:24,912
- Dad, go and stop her.
- No, you get on the bus.

2250
01:51:24,954 --> 01:51:27,787
Do you have any idea how much effort
I put into raising her as a single parent?

2251
01:51:28,995 --> 01:51:30,329
[bus moves]

2252
01:51:31,412 --> 01:51:32,579
To hell with your raising!

2253
01:51:34,079 --> 01:51:36,036
Who really ruined whose life?

2254
01:51:36,037 --> 01:51:38,412
It was your daughter who ruined mine.

2255
01:51:38,662 --> 01:51:40,995
And thanks to you, my family left me.

2256
01:51:41,037 --> 01:51:43,619
You said I borrowed 15 lakhs
and lived like a bum?

2257
01:51:43,620 --> 01:51:45,454
It’s because your daughter
spent money like a spendthrift

2258
01:51:45,495 --> 01:51:47,370
that I’m standing here
with a 15-lakh debt!

2259
01:51:47,745 --> 01:51:50,162
She wouldn't even drink a
20-rupee coffee at a street stall,

2260
01:51:50,412 --> 01:51:53,204
she only drinks 280-rupee
cappuccinos at Starbucks.

2261
01:51:53,620 --> 01:51:55,579
Your daughter doesn't know
the value of money.

2262
01:51:55,662 --> 01:51:57,495
And you? You don't know
the value of people.

2263
01:51:57,912 --> 01:52:00,661
Go away from here!
Don't make me do something I might regret.

2264
01:52:00,662 --> 01:52:02,120
How dare you speak to your
elders with such disrespect?

2265
01:52:02,162 --> 01:52:02,787
Oh!

2266
01:52:02,954 --> 01:52:04,619
Is respect just for elders?

2267
01:52:04,620 --> 01:52:06,328
Why? Are we not entitled to that?

2268
01:52:06,329 --> 01:52:08,037
My father just died and has
boarded the bus with a heavy heart.

2269
01:52:08,620 --> 01:52:10,620
How will I ever face him tomorrow?

2270
01:52:10,870 --> 01:52:12,369
Why are you just jumping to conclusions?

2271
01:52:12,370 --> 01:52:14,829
I knew the moment she
foolishly accepted this challenge

2272
01:52:14,870 --> 01:52:16,620
that she would eventually
get into trouble.

2273
01:52:16,662 --> 01:52:18,579
That’s why I have kept the property deeds

2274
01:52:18,620 --> 01:52:20,412
and jewellery my father gave me
to settle my debts safe.

2275
01:52:20,454 --> 01:52:22,704
I will use those to clear
your daughter’s debt,

2276
01:52:22,954 --> 01:52:24,995
but I will never ask you to sell
your property to pay off my loans.

2277
01:52:25,162 --> 01:52:28,079
My parents raised me by teaching me
how to keep a girl safe,

2278
01:52:28,120 --> 01:52:30,995
but they never taught me how to
use a girl to ensure one's own safety.

2279
01:52:32,162 --> 01:52:34,495
No creditor will come looking
for your daughter ever again.

2280
01:52:34,579 --> 01:52:36,454
Don't tell your daughter
to come looking for me as well.

2281
01:52:44,954 --> 01:52:46,079
Hi, Tattoo brother!

2282
01:52:46,370 --> 01:52:47,370
What are you doing here?

2283
01:52:47,412 --> 01:52:48,454
Go and ask your mom.

2284
01:52:48,662 --> 01:52:49,579
- What happened?
- Get away!

2285
01:53:08,620 --> 01:53:10,995
Why is Raghu's house document here?

2286
01:53:13,162 --> 01:53:14,912
Why is our house document not here?

2287
01:53:16,787 --> 01:53:18,245
Mom, you...

2288
01:53:19,204 --> 01:53:20,662
you are making a big mistake.

2289
01:53:22,245 --> 01:53:23,495
My dad should have been here.

2290
01:53:23,787 --> 01:53:25,954
He should have asked you
why you are doing this.

2291
01:53:26,370 --> 01:53:28,287
I am like this because of your dad.

2292
01:53:28,745 --> 01:53:32,579
Your dad isn't some big hero
like you were raised to believe.

2293
01:53:33,579 --> 01:53:34,995
He borrowed money from everyone and,

2294
01:53:35,412 --> 01:53:37,662
unable to pay it back, died by suicide,

2295
01:53:37,829 --> 01:53:39,745
he is a murderer who destroyed my life.

2296
01:53:39,954 --> 01:53:44,745
I carried both you and the debt that man
created, and wandered the streets.

2297
01:53:44,954 --> 01:53:46,704
No relative came to save us.

2298
01:53:47,495 --> 01:53:49,495
Only the education I received saved me.

2299
01:53:49,912 --> 01:53:52,370
So that you would never have to endure
the suffering I went through,

2300
01:53:53,245 --> 01:53:55,662
I made sure to take care
of every little thing for you.

2301
01:53:59,287 --> 01:54:01,995
That day at the police station,
when I saw you with that boy...

2302
01:54:03,162 --> 01:54:04,412
I died inside!

2303
01:54:04,745 --> 01:54:07,162
It felt exactly like looking
at your father and me.

2304
01:54:07,495 --> 01:54:09,829
I didn't want you to end up
in my situation.

2305
01:54:10,579 --> 01:54:12,162
That's why I told you
to stay away from him.

2306
01:54:12,870 --> 01:54:15,287
But it was only after speaking
to him today that I realized.

2307
01:54:16,245 --> 01:54:17,662
He is not like your dad,

2308
01:54:18,495 --> 01:54:20,579
it's you who have grown up
to be just like your dad!

2309
01:54:21,745 --> 01:54:23,787
You've been in love with
this guy for four years,

2310
01:54:25,037 --> 01:54:26,537
don't you even know how much he earns,

2311
01:54:26,579 --> 01:54:29,745
or how much you're making him spend?

2312
01:54:31,162 --> 01:54:32,954
I raised you well, but...

2313
01:54:34,370 --> 01:54:36,495
I didn't teach you what's right or wrong.

2314
01:54:37,412 --> 01:54:39,454
But, he has taught you well.

2315
01:54:39,829 --> 01:54:40,954
Now I'm saying it.

2316
01:54:41,912 --> 01:54:43,329
He's the right guy for you.

2317
01:54:45,329 --> 01:54:47,204
I have defamed his family.

2318
01:54:47,662 --> 01:54:51,745
Even if I have to beg them,
it's my responsibility to convince them.

2319
01:54:52,537 --> 01:54:55,037
It's your responsibility to convince him.

2320
01:54:55,662 --> 01:54:57,329
But he just wouldn't accept, mom.

2321
01:54:57,370 --> 01:55:00,870
You made a man who kept
saying 'no' spend money, didn't you?

2322
01:55:01,037 --> 01:55:03,995
Now, make the man who says
he won't love you, fall in love with you.

2323
01:55:05,912 --> 01:55:06,787
Okay.

2324
01:55:07,120 --> 01:55:08,120
Thanks, mom.

2325
01:55:20,787 --> 01:55:22,370
He left his phone here and...

2326
01:55:23,329 --> 01:55:25,079
hmm, he must have gone out to eat.

2327
01:55:37,037 --> 01:55:38,329
So, you wanted a side dish?

2328
01:55:38,745 --> 01:55:39,954
Well, here’s your side dish.

2329
01:55:44,745 --> 01:55:46,079
- Hey, hey, hey...
- She's running!

2330
01:55:46,204 --> 01:55:47,579
Hey, catch her!

2331
01:55:51,995 --> 01:55:52,704
Hey!

2332
01:55:55,412 --> 01:55:56,329
Raghu!

2333
01:55:57,537 --> 01:55:58,745
Come, come, let's go!

2334
01:56:04,829 --> 01:56:05,995
What are you doing?

2335
01:56:06,162 --> 01:56:08,662
Four men are chasing me.

2336
01:56:10,579 --> 01:56:11,579
There's no one there.

2337
01:56:12,370 --> 01:56:14,579
Please Raghu... stay. I'm scared.

2338
01:56:14,620 --> 01:56:17,329
Oh! Have you started your next drama?

2339
01:56:20,245 --> 01:56:22,537
How does everything just seem
to happen so naturally for you?

2340
01:56:22,704 --> 01:56:25,079
You will mortgage your house
documents to pay off my debt.

2341
01:56:25,287 --> 01:56:28,119
And you’ll even give it to the same
financier your mother works as an auditor.

2342
01:56:28,120 --> 01:56:29,662
All of this will happen without
you even knowing about it, right?

2343
01:56:29,704 --> 01:56:32,495
And today, you come and hug me right
when I’m walking through my area,

2344
01:56:32,537 --> 01:56:34,661
claiming that four thugs
are chasing you.

2345
01:56:34,662 --> 01:56:36,287
When I looked behind you,
no one was there.

2346
01:56:36,787 --> 01:56:38,244
What have you planned now?

2347
01:56:38,245 --> 01:56:39,829
- Raghu, what are you...
- Wait.

2348
01:56:39,870 --> 01:56:41,662
You should never be trusted.

2349
01:56:55,245 --> 01:56:57,787
Hey... what's all this?

2350
01:56:58,120 --> 01:57:00,370
- I really don't know, Raghu.
- Hey! Stop acting!

2351
01:57:00,579 --> 01:57:02,162
No, Raghu, I swear!

2352
01:57:02,704 --> 01:57:04,620
Four guys were chasing me.

2353
01:57:04,912 --> 01:57:06,245
I asked what's all this?

2354
01:57:07,954 --> 01:57:08,829
I really don't know.

2355
01:57:09,370 --> 01:57:10,537
Don't look at me like that.

2356
01:57:10,579 --> 01:57:11,911
How else should I look at you?

2357
01:57:11,912 --> 01:57:15,245
I asked you to stand in a man's shoes
for four months and face his struggles,

2358
01:57:16,204 --> 01:57:17,204
but you didn't have the guts for that.

2359
01:57:18,037 --> 01:57:19,662
Is this how you cheat
in such a shameful way?

2360
01:57:19,787 --> 01:57:21,329
I swear I didn't cheat you.

2361
01:57:21,370 --> 01:57:22,912
Who? You?

2362
01:57:23,245 --> 01:57:25,412
Usually, you sit with a good gap
between us on the scooter,

2363
01:57:25,620 --> 01:57:27,329
but that day, I noticed you were
sitting pressed right up against me.

2364
01:57:27,370 --> 01:57:29,370
Today, you're trying to record
yourself hugging me on the road.

2365
01:57:29,579 --> 01:57:31,370
Once we're married tomorrow,
if we get into an argument,

2366
01:57:31,412 --> 01:57:32,954
are you going to install
a camera in our bedroom too?

2367
01:57:33,495 --> 01:57:36,037
Until now, I thought you
were just irresponsible.

2368
01:57:36,329 --> 01:57:38,995
It only hit me today that
we’re just not a good match.

2369
01:57:39,120 --> 01:57:40,412
Are there no other men...

2370
01:57:44,037 --> 01:57:46,454
Does 'no means no' only apply to women?

2371
01:57:46,745 --> 01:57:48,495
Doesn't it apply to men too?

2372
01:57:49,245 --> 01:57:51,079
I don't need you in my life anymore.

2373
01:58:02,245 --> 01:58:04,787
[phone rings]

2374
01:58:16,412 --> 01:58:19,079
If you see a girl walking alone at night,
do you go after her?

2375
01:58:19,120 --> 01:58:21,495
Please don't hit us! Sir, please...

2376
01:58:21,537 --> 01:58:23,954
- Sir, did you ask for me?
- Oh, you're here?

2377
01:58:24,662 --> 01:58:26,954
Here is the L3 you asked for,
take it and leave!

2378
01:58:34,120 --> 01:58:36,161
- We'll never do it again, Sir!
- Please let us go, Sir!

2379
01:58:36,162 --> 01:58:38,370
- Sorry, Sir! Sorry, Sir!
- Sorry, Sir!

2380
01:58:38,412 --> 01:58:39,745
- Please let us go, Sir!
- Let us go, Sir!

2381
01:58:40,745 --> 01:58:42,370
- Sir, Sir, camera...
- Sir, our camera?

2382
01:58:44,079 --> 01:58:47,203
From now on, if you hide a camera
anywhere under the guise of a 'prank,'

2383
01:58:47,204 --> 01:58:48,704
I’m going to break it.

2384
01:58:49,079 --> 01:58:49,954
Take it and get lost!

2385
01:58:50,454 --> 01:58:51,162
- Get lost!
- Here, take it.

2386
01:58:51,204 --> 01:58:52,329
- Thanks, Sir.
- Thank you, Sir.

2387
01:58:52,370 --> 01:58:53,287
Come, let's go.

2388
01:58:54,495 --> 01:58:56,662
Hey! Why are you still here?

2389
01:58:57,995 --> 01:59:01,287
We can beat and punish people like them.

2390
01:59:01,412 --> 01:59:03,454
We can't do anything to you guys, right?

2391
01:59:05,162 --> 01:59:08,079
Hey, what happened that made
you want to end it all?

2392
01:59:09,579 --> 01:59:11,287
What else do you want me to do?

2393
01:59:11,579 --> 01:59:12,995
You know it, right?

2394
01:59:13,370 --> 01:59:16,370
Jashwanth married me only after knowing

2395
01:59:16,412 --> 01:59:18,745
that I loved Goutham
and had a breakup, right?

2396
01:59:18,787 --> 01:59:20,537
Everyone in our office knows this.

2397
01:59:20,579 --> 01:59:21,329
Then what?

2398
01:59:21,870 --> 01:59:25,662
Yesterday, everyone was sitting
in the hall having a casual chat.

2399
01:59:26,204 --> 01:59:29,787
Suddenly, there was a small
non-sync between him and me.

2400
01:59:29,954 --> 01:59:32,620
That turned into a heated argument.

2401
01:59:32,954 --> 01:59:36,537
He didn't even realize where
he was or what he was saying,

2402
01:59:36,579 --> 01:59:37,745
and in front of everyone,

2403
01:59:37,787 --> 01:59:41,204
he just blurted out that I’m the kind
of girl who goes off with other men.

2404
01:59:42,954 --> 01:59:46,244
You were whining about how
one girl ruined your life,

2405
01:59:46,245 --> 01:59:50,745
but do you have any idea how many women's
lives have been ruined because of men?

2406
01:59:51,370 --> 01:59:53,162
I'm watching it happen every single day.

2407
01:59:58,829 --> 02:00:01,536
If women stopped putting up
with everything,

2408
02:00:01,537 --> 02:00:03,662
there wouldn't be a single
family left in this country.

2409
02:00:05,495 --> 02:00:08,120
We left everything for you,
trusting you completely.

2410
02:00:08,704 --> 02:00:11,204
Why are you men like this?

2411
02:00:28,537 --> 02:00:29,204
[slaps Jashwanth]

2412
02:00:32,120 --> 02:00:36,787
You know why I agreed to
this stupid L3, four-month agreement?

2413
02:00:37,162 --> 02:00:39,744
So that in these four months,
you’d understand her love,

2414
02:00:39,745 --> 02:00:41,745
and she would understand your struggles.

2415
02:00:42,079 --> 02:00:44,662
She has understood. But you...

2416
02:00:45,745 --> 02:00:48,454
Love isn’t about keeping
score of what I did for you

2417
02:00:48,495 --> 02:00:51,744
or asking you to pay me back
for what I’ve done.

2418
02:00:51,745 --> 02:00:54,579
True love is saying, 'No matter what
happens, I will never leave you.'

2419
02:00:54,745 --> 02:00:55,369
Get lost!

2420
02:00:55,370 --> 02:00:57,245
♪ Just for you... ♪

2421
02:00:57,329 --> 02:01:00,204
♪ Who am I? ♪

2422
02:01:02,037 --> 02:01:02,829
Get out of my sight!

2423
02:01:02,870 --> 02:01:07,287
♪ In your world, who am I? ♪

2424
02:01:08,412 --> 02:01:10,037
Look at this moron!

2425
02:01:12,412 --> 02:01:13,161
Hey!

2426
02:01:13,162 --> 02:01:15,704
If I see anyone letting him
into the station again, you're done!

2427
02:01:22,579 --> 02:01:25,537
<i>"If you see a girl walking alone at night,
do you go after her?"</i>

2428
02:01:27,162 --> 02:01:29,745
<i>"Four men are chasing me."</i>

2429
02:01:29,787 --> 02:01:31,579
<i>"Have you started your next drama?"</i>

2430
02:01:35,995 --> 02:01:38,995
When you had everything,
she didn't ask for you.

2431
02:01:39,662 --> 02:01:42,995
She only wanted you when
you had nothing left.

2432
02:01:43,204 --> 02:01:46,037
Can’t you see from that
how much she loves you?

2433
02:01:47,829 --> 02:01:50,037
<i>"He’s the sum of all my love!"</i>

2434
02:01:50,579 --> 02:01:51,870
<i>"Will you get me booze?"</i>

2435
02:01:52,870 --> 02:01:54,995
<i>"Raghu, success!"</i>

2436
02:01:57,370 --> 02:01:59,787
You pushed that girl to give an L3.

2437
02:01:59,912 --> 02:02:02,036
<i>"That was my first purchase for marriage."</i>

2438
02:02:02,037 --> 02:02:03,454
<i>"It's all memories."</i>

2439
02:02:03,495 --> 02:02:06,537
<i>"From now on, if you hide a camera
anywhere under the guise of a 'prank,'</i>

2440
02:02:06,579 --> 02:02:08,037
<i>I’m going to break it."</i>

2441
02:02:08,620 --> 02:02:10,620
<i>"Once we're married tomorrow,
if we get into an argument,</i>

2442
02:02:10,662 --> 02:02:12,204
<i>are you going to install
a camera in our bedroom too?"</i>

2443
02:02:17,995 --> 02:02:22,620
♪ Really, who am I? ♪

2444
02:02:47,454 --> 02:02:50,537
Raghu, you need to leave
for Dubai in just a few days.

2445
02:02:51,162 --> 02:02:51,995
All the best!

2446
02:02:52,537 --> 02:02:54,454
- Happy journey.
- Thank you, Sir.

2447
02:02:55,745 --> 02:02:56,454
Thank you.

2448
02:03:08,829 --> 02:03:10,704
Why don't you answer my calls?

2449
02:03:10,912 --> 02:03:12,537
Why should I answer your calls?

2450
02:03:15,162 --> 02:03:16,870
I made a mistake by not understanding you.

2451
02:03:19,579 --> 02:03:20,995
You didn’t do anything wrong, Raghu.

2452
02:03:21,287 --> 02:03:22,787
I’m the one who made a mistake.

2453
02:03:23,662 --> 02:03:28,704
The day you said you didn’t want me
in front of everyone at the police station...

2454
02:03:29,162 --> 02:03:31,329
I should’ve left you that very day.

2455
02:03:32,579 --> 02:03:35,829
I was the fool who kept chasing
after you because I wanted only you.

2456
02:03:36,954 --> 02:03:38,495
I’m the one who made the mistake.

2457
02:03:39,620 --> 02:03:42,537
It’s true that I always wanted
to ride on a sports bike.

2458
02:03:44,745 --> 02:03:46,870
If fulfilling that wish was all I wanted,

2459
02:03:46,912 --> 02:03:49,537
I could’ve gone with someone
who owned one.

2460
02:03:50,579 --> 02:03:52,829
But do you know why I came with you?

2461
02:03:54,745 --> 02:03:58,245
People usually say girls
are their dad’s little princesses.

2462
02:03:59,037 --> 02:04:00,495
But I don’t have a father...

2463
02:04:00,954 --> 02:04:04,162
so I never knew what
that feeling was like.

2464
02:04:04,870 --> 02:04:08,995
But when I travelled with
my Raghu on the bike I loved,

2465
02:04:09,870 --> 02:04:11,745
that’s when I truly felt like a princess.

2466
02:04:14,079 --> 02:04:18,120
This is something I could only expect from
the one I love... from you alone, Raghu.

2467
02:04:19,745 --> 02:04:22,787
You kept saying I was
making you spend money...

2468
02:04:23,995 --> 02:04:30,162
but for a girl, receiving gifts
means more than giving them.

2469
02:04:30,745 --> 02:04:33,204
Because it gives her
the feeling that there’s someone

2470
02:04:33,245 --> 02:04:35,204
who truly cares enough
to do all this for her.

2471
02:04:37,162 --> 02:04:38,662
You broke it, didn't you?

2472
02:04:40,079 --> 02:04:45,370
Just when I started understanding you and
trying to become someone worthy of you...

2473
02:04:46,704 --> 02:04:48,329
you destroyed me!

2474
02:04:49,829 --> 02:04:52,495
You could’ve scolded me out of anger...

2475
02:04:52,537 --> 02:04:53,870
fought with me...

2476
02:04:54,954 --> 02:04:56,495
or even hit me if you wanted.

2477
02:04:56,704 --> 02:04:58,870
But instead, you humiliated me.

2478
02:04:58,912 --> 02:05:00,454
Why are you talking like this?

2479
02:05:01,662 --> 02:05:04,079
I thought you were angry with me...

2480
02:05:04,995 --> 02:05:07,495
but I never imagined that you hated me.

2481
02:05:09,245 --> 02:05:12,829
If a girl talks freely,
you call her cheap.

2482
02:05:12,954 --> 02:05:15,620
If she keeps her distance,
you say she has an attitude.

2483
02:05:17,579 --> 02:05:19,037
God, I’ve had enough!

2484
02:05:21,245 --> 02:05:23,745
I’ll never come back into your life again.

2485
02:05:24,579 --> 02:05:26,204
Please... don’t come looking for me either.

2486
02:05:27,162 --> 02:05:27,787
Hey!

2487
02:05:28,412 --> 02:05:31,287
I used to think girls could never
do the things boys do in love...

2488
02:05:32,245 --> 02:05:36,370
but now I realize men and women
are equal after all.

2489
02:05:37,662 --> 02:05:40,745
When a man says 'men and women are equal',

2490
02:05:40,787 --> 02:05:42,162
even that comes from male dominance.

2491
02:06:00,745 --> 02:06:03,162
[flight takes off]

2492
02:06:08,537 --> 02:06:09,995
Sir, I need to see the Inspector.

2493
02:06:10,120 --> 02:06:11,245
He is inside, please go.

2494
02:06:21,912 --> 02:06:22,662
Sir!

2495
02:06:24,204 --> 02:06:25,787
Hey! You again?

2496
02:06:26,537 --> 02:06:28,204
Sir! You again?

2497
02:06:28,245 --> 02:06:29,662
What is the problem now?

2498
02:06:29,745 --> 02:06:32,745
Oh no, Sir... it’s been nothing but
problems after marriage.

2499
02:06:33,079 --> 02:06:35,579
My wife and I just don’t get along, Sir.

2500
02:06:35,954 --> 02:06:38,828
If I suggest one name for
the baby, she chooses another.

2501
02:06:38,829 --> 02:06:41,245
If I pick a school, she enrols
the child somewhere else.

2502
02:06:41,287 --> 02:06:44,370
I want our kid to become an athlete,
but she wants them to be a dancer.

2503
02:06:46,495 --> 02:06:47,787
I can’t take this anymore, Sir.

2504
02:06:48,370 --> 02:06:51,370
You tell me... who’s responsible
for the child’s future?

2505
02:06:51,412 --> 02:06:52,829
The mother or the father?

2506
02:06:52,870 --> 02:06:55,995
Hey, wait... you got married?

2507
02:06:56,287 --> 02:06:57,995
Who did you marry?

2508
02:06:58,204 --> 02:07:00,869
Who else would I marry, Sir?
I married Avantika.

2509
02:07:00,870 --> 02:07:04,620
Hey, your father and her mother
never got along in the first place.

2510
02:07:04,662 --> 02:07:07,495
All that got sorted out,
and we got married with their blessings.

2511
02:07:07,579 --> 02:07:08,579
Oh!

2512
02:07:08,912 --> 02:07:10,912
She already spoke for half an hour

2513
02:07:10,954 --> 02:07:13,037
and left saying she didn’t
want you anymore, didn't she?

2514
02:07:13,204 --> 02:07:14,995
How did you convince her?

2515
02:07:15,204 --> 02:07:16,537
How did you make things right?

2516
02:07:16,579 --> 02:07:18,495
Sir, there’s many long stories about how
two people who fought and broke apart

2517
02:07:18,537 --> 02:07:20,870
found their way back together.

2518
02:07:21,162 --> 02:07:22,954
But I didn’t come here
to tell that story, Sir.

2519
02:07:23,162 --> 02:07:25,412
My story is about the problems
that started after marriage.

2520
02:07:25,454 --> 02:07:27,579
Please listen to my story
in the order I’m telling it, Sir.

2521
02:07:27,620 --> 02:07:28,412
Hey!

2522
02:07:28,454 --> 02:07:31,787
Will you never tell a story in
the right order till the very end?

2523
02:07:31,995 --> 02:07:33,204
I won’t!

2524
02:07:40,287 --> 02:07:43,912
♪ When we love...
When we love, are we the Accused? ♪

2525
02:07:43,954 --> 02:07:46,994
♪ Trapped, my man,
trapped, my Cinderella fine... ♪

2526
02:07:46,995 --> 02:07:49,495
♪ You know I can fry vadas in
my mouth with just words, right? ♪

2527
02:07:49,579 --> 02:07:51,412
♪ Let me show you how it's done! ♪

2528
02:08:20,079 --> 02:08:23,787
♪ When we love...
When we love, are we the Accused? ♪

2529
02:08:23,829 --> 02:08:24,786
♪ Trapped... ♪

2530
02:08:24,787 --> 02:08:25,745
Tell me!

2531
02:08:25,787 --> 02:08:27,578
♪ Trapped, my little Cinderella... ♪

2532
02:08:27,579 --> 02:08:31,286
♪ When we love...
When we love, are we the Accused? ♪

2533
02:08:31,287 --> 02:08:35,079
♪ Trapped, my man,
trapped, my Cinderella fine... ♪

2534
02:08:35,912 --> 02:08:36,580
♪ Are we the Accused? ♪

